(537, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A  code  listed  next  to  a  main  term  in  the  ICD-10-CM alphabetic  index  is  rendered  to  as  a  ????????????? (a)  default code (b) Clinical code (c) Code ?also? (d) see ?also?.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(538, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">?????????????are subdivided into homogeneous blocks of three digits categories. (a) Nomenclature regulations (b) Block<br />\ncategories of code (c) code numbers (d) Chapters.</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(539, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Congenital, Malformation, deformation and chromosomal abnormalities is found in ??????????? chapter of the ICD 10th revision  (a)  chapter  17  (b)  chapter  17  (c)  chapter  18 (d)chapter 15.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(540, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">????????????? is  used  as  guide  and  direct  the  coder  on  how  to<br />\nuse the tabular list and the alphabetical index (a) volume 1 (b) volume 4 (c) volume 3 (d) volume 2.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(541, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In  numbering  of  the  chapters  in  ICD-10th  revision,  the chapter  (12)  Diseases  of  the  skin  and  the  subcutaneous tissue was numbered?????????????(a) L00-L99 (b) K00-K93 (c) M00-M99 (d) O00-O99.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(542, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">?????????????is the disease, injury or complication that directly results to death which is the ultimate consequence of the underlying  cause  of  death  (a)  antecedent  cause  of  death<br />\n(b)  cause  of  death  (c)  underlying  cause  of  death  (d) immediate cause of death.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(543, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">????????????? is  either  a  legal  document  issued  by  a  medical practitioner which states when person died (a) immediate cause of death (b) Medical certificate (c) death certificate<br />\n(d) certificate of still-birth.</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(544, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The  condition  that  led  to  or  precipitated  the  immediate cause of death as recorded on a death certificate is known as  ????????????? (a)  underlying  cause  of  death  (b)  antecedent cause of death (c) Immediate cause of death (d) cause of death.</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(545, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Disease or injury which initiated the train of morbid events  leading  directly  to  death  or  the  circumstances  of the  accident  or  violence  which  produced  the  fatal  injury is?????????????(a) Antecedent cause of death (b) neonatal death<br />\n(c)  underlying  cause  of  death  (d)  immediate  cause  of death.</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(546, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Any death of a live-born infant occurring  within the first<br />\ntwenty eight days of life should be certified using ?????????????</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(547, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">(a) death certificate (b) certificate of still-birth (c) Medical certificate of cause of death (d) neonatal death certificate. ??????????????? provides  the  raw  data  from  which  mortality statistics   are   divided.   (a)   death   certificate   (b)   life expectancy (c) Medical certificate (d) underlying cause of death.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(548, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An   epidemiological   Practice   by   which   the   spread   of disease  is  monitored  in  order  to  establish   pattern  of progression is called ???????????(a) epidemiology (b) diseases case    report    (c)    diseases    notification    (d)    diseases surveillance.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(549, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">????????????? is  a  strategy  for  coordinating  and  integrating surveillance  activities  by  focusing  on  the  surveillance, laboratory and response functions of the national diseases surveillance  system.  (a)  IDSR  (b)  OPCS  (c)  RIDS  (d) KSO.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(550, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">?????????????  is   a   process   of   reporting   the   occurrence   of diseases   or   other   health   related   conditions   to   the appropriate   and   designated   authorities.   (a)   diseases surveillance  (b)  Diseases  notification  (c)  diseases  case report (d) Office of The Population Census Survey.</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(551, '2024/2025', 'Professional Diploma in Health Information Management', '300', 'First', 'ICD', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">?????????????is a statement from a physician or other health care provider that attests to the result of a medical examination of a patient. (a) death certificate (b) Medical certificate (c) cause of death certificate (d) underlying cause of death.</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
