(789, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the average of the following set of data 15, 25, 35, 45, 55, 65<br />\r\n(a) 25    <br />\r\n(b) 30<br />\r\n(c) 35 <br />\r\n(d) 40<br />\r</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(790, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If a=10 and d=10, then first four terms will be:<br />\r\n(a)10,30,50,60<br />\r\n(b)10,20,30,40<br />\r\n(c)10,15,20,25<br />\r\n(d)10,18,20,30<br />\r</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(791, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the average of first 150 natural numbers?<br />\r\n(A) 70<br />\r\n(B) 70.5<br />\r\n(C) 75<br />\r\n(D) 75.5<br />\r</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(792, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Simplify: 3x (4a - 5b) - 5x(3a - 2b)<br />\r\n(a) 3ax - 5b<br />\r\n(b) (3a - 5b)x<br />\r\n(c) (5b - 3a)x<br />\r\n(d) -(3a + 5b)x<br />\r</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(793, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The area of triangle is 52cm2. If the base of the triangle is 8cm, find its height.<br />\r\n(a) 6.5cm<br />\r\n(b) 7.5cm<br />\r\n(c) 13.0cm  <br />\r\n(d) 26cm<br />\r</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(794, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If ?240,000.00 is shared between 3 people in the ratio 5:4:3. What is the least share?<br />\r\n    (a) ?100,000.00<br />\r\n    (b) ? 96,000.00<br />\r\n    (c) ?80,000.00<br />\r\n    (d) ?60,000.00<br />\r</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(795, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the value of x in the equation 3x - 15 - 6 = 0 ?<br />\r\n(A) 7<br />\r\n(B) 8<br />\r\n(C) 9<br />\r\n(D) -9<br />\r</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(796, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">11th term of the A.P. -3, -1/2, ,2 ?. Is<br />\r\n(a)28<br />\r\n(b)22<br />\r\n(c)-38<br />\r\n(d)-48<br />\r</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(797, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In an Arithmetic Progression, if a=28, d=-4, n=7, then an is:<br />\r\n(a)4<br />\r\n(b)5<br />\r\n(c)3<br />\r\n(d)7<br />\r</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(798, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the average of the numbers: 0, 0, 4, 10, 5, and 5 ?<br />\r\n(A) 2<br />\r\n(B) 3<br />\r\n(C) 4<br />\r\n(D) 5<br />\r</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(799, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the rate of discount if a car which price was $4,000 was sold for $3,200 ?<br />\r\n(A) 14%<br />\r\n(B) 16%<br />\r\n(C) 18%<br />\r\n(D) 20%<br />\r</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(800, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the range of the following set of data 25, 22, 23, 27, 19, 15, 22, 23, 22, 22, 14,28.<br />\r\n(a) 25<br />\r\n(b) 23<br />\r\n(c) 14    <br />\r\n(d) 12<br />\r</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(801, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Health Assistants', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">3y = 4x - 1 and Ky = x + 3 are equations of two straight lines. If the two lines are perpendicular to each other, find K.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n    A. -4/3<br />\r\n    B. -3/4<br />\r\n    C. 3/4<br />\r\n    D. 4/3<br />\r</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(802, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of a chemical change?<br />\r\n A) Boiling water<br />\r\n B) Dissolving salt in water <br />\r\nC) Burning wood <br />\r\nD) Freezing water <br />\r</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(803, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the pH value of a neutral solution? <br />\r\nA) 1 <br />\r\nB) 7 <br />\r\nC) 10<br />\r\n D) 14</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(804, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is the most abundant gas in the Earth\'s atmosphere?<br />\r\n A) Oxygen <br />\r\nB) Nitrogen<br />\r\n C) Carbon dioxide <br />\r\nD) Argon</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(805, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a halogen? <br />\r\nA) Sodium <br />\r\nB) Chlorine <br />\r\nC) Calcium <br />\r\nD) Iron</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(806, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the chemical formula for methane? <br />\r\nA) CH4 <br />\r\nB) H2SO4 <br />\r\nC) NaCl<br />\r\n D) CO2</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(807, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which subatomic particle has a positive charge? <br />\r\n             A) Proton <br />\r\n             B) Neutron <br />\r\n             C) Electron <br />\r\n            D) Photon</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(808, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a noble gas? <br />\r\nA) Neon <br />\r\nB) Sodium <br />\r\nC) Potassium <br />\r\nD) Aluminum</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(809, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the chemical symbol for iron? <br />\r\nA) I <br />\r\nB) Fe <br />\r\nC) Au <br />\r\nD) Pb</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(810, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the atomic number of oxygen? <br />\r\nA) 6 <br />\r\nB) 8 <br />\r\nC) 10 <br />\r\nD) 12</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(811, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of a physical change? <br />\r\nA) Burning wood <br />\r\nB) Rusting iron <br />\r\nC) Melting ice <br />\r\nD) Cooking eggs</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(812, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the pH value of an acidic solution? <br />\r\nA) 1 <br />\r\nB) 7<br />\r\n C) 10 <br />\r\nD) 14</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(813, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a greenhouse gas? <br />\r\nA) Oxygen <br />\r\nB) Nitrogen <br />\r\nC) Carbon dioxide <br />\r\nD) Argon</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(814, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the chemical formula for carbon dioxide? <br />\r\nA) CO2<br />\r\n B) H2O <br />\r\nC) NaCl<br />\r\n D) C6H12O6</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(815, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an alkali metal? <br />\r\nA) Sodium<br />\r\n B) Chlorine <br />\r\nC) Calcium <br />\r\nD) Iron</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(816, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which functional group is present in an alcohol? <br />\r\nA) Carboxyl <br />\r\nB) Amine <br />\r\nC) Hydroxyl <br />\r\nD) Aldehyde</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(817, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the general formula for an alkane? <br />\r\nA) CnH2n+1 <br />\r\nB) CnH2n <br />\r\nC) CnH2n+2 <br />\r\nD) CnH2n-2</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(818, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the process called when a molecule gains an electron? <br />\r\nA) Oxidation <br />\r\nB) Reduction <br />\r\nC) Polymerization <br />\r\nD) Hydrolysis</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(819, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of an aromatic compound? <br />\r\nA) Methane <br />\r\nB) Ethanol <br />\r\nC) Benzene <br />\r\nD) Butanoic acid</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(820, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the functional group present in a carboxylic acid?<br />\r\n A) Aldehyde <br />\r\nB) Ketone <br />\r\nC) Carboxyl <br />\r\nD) Ester</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(821, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a primary alcohol? <br />\r\nA) Ethanol <br />\r\nB) Methanol <br />\r\nC) Propanol <br />\r\nD) Butanol <br />\r</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(822, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of isomerism is observed in compounds with the same molecular formula but different arrangement of atoms in space? <br />\r\nA) Structural isomerism<br />\r\n B) Geometric isomerism<br />\r\n C) Optical isomerism<br />\r\n D) Functional group isomerism</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(823, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the IUPAC name for CH3-CH2-CH2-CH3? <br />\r\nA) Butane <br />\r\nB) Ethane <br />\r\nC) Propane <br />\r\nD) Pentane</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(824, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which functional group is present in an aldehyde? <br />\r\nA) Carboxyl <br />\r\nB) Hydroxyl <br />\r\nC) Aldehyde <br />\r\nD) Ester</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(825, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the process called when a large molecule is broken down into smaller units by adding water? <br />\r\nA) Oxidation <br />\r\nB) Reduction <br />\r\nC) Polymerization <br />\r\nD) Hydrolysis</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(826, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a fundamental force of nature? <br />\r\nA) Electromagnetic force <br />\r\nB) Gravitational force <br />\r\nC) Nuclear force <br />\r\nD) Frictional force</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(827, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the SI unit of electric current? <br />\r\nA) Ampere <br />\r\nB) Volt <br />\r\nC) Watt <br />\r\nD) Ohm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(828, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following describes the resistance to change in an object\'s motion? <br />\r\nA) Velocity <br />\r\nB) Momentum <br />\r\nC) Inertia <br />\r\nD) Acceleration</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(829, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">According to Newton\'s first law of motion, an object at rest tends to stay at rest unless acted upon by a(n):<br />\r\n A) Unbalanced force <br />\r\nB) Frictional force<br />\r\n C) Electric force <br />\r\nD) Magnetic force</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(830, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes the process by which a gas changes directly into a solid without becoming a liquid? <br />\r\nA) Condensation <br />\r\nB) Evaporation <br />\r\nC) Sublimation <br />\r\nD) Fusion</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(831, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The bending of light as it passes from one medium to another is known as: <br />\r\nA) Reflection <br />\r\nB) Refraction <br />\r\nC) Diffraction <br />\r\nD) Dispersion</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(832, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a type of electromagnetic radiation? <br />\r\nA) X-rays <br />\r\nB) Ultraviolet <br />\r\nC) Sound waves <br />\r\nD) Gamma rays</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(833, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The energy stored in an object due to its position or condition is called: <br />\r\nA) Kinetic energy <br />\r\nB) Potential energy <br />\r\nC) Thermal energy <br />\r\nD) Chemical energy</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(834, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a renewable energy source? <br />\r\nA) Solar power <br />\r\nB) Wind power <br />\r\nC) Nuclear power <br />\r\nD) Hydroelectric power</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(835, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The process of converting a solid directly into a gas without passing through the liquid state is called: <br />\r\nA) Melting <br />\r\nB) Sublimation <br />\r\nC) Freezing <br />\r\nD) Condensation</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(836, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements about magnets is true? <br />\r\nA) Opposite poles attract, and like poles repel. <br />\r\nB) Opposite poles repel, and like poles attract. <br />\r\nC) Only magnets made of iron are attracted to each other. <br />\r\nD) Magnets can only attract non-magnetic materials.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(837, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The amount of matter in an object is referred to as its: <br />\r\nA) Mass <br />\r\nB) Weight <br />\r\nC) Volume <br />\r\nD) Density</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(838, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the unit of measurement for electric potential difference? <br />\r\nA) Volt <br />\r\nB) Ohm<br />\r\n C) Ampere <br />\r\nD) Watt</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(839, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements about sound waves is true? <br />\r\nA) Sound waves require a medium to propagate. <br />\r\nB) Sound waves travel faster in a vacuum than in air. <br />\r\nC) Sound waves are a form of electromagnetic radiation. <br />\r\nD) Sound waves always travel in a straight line.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(840, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for Pharmacy Technicians', '100', 'First', 'MOCK', 'MOCK', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">According to the law of reflection, the angle of incidence is equal to the angle of: <br />\r\nA) Reflection <br />\r\nB) Refraction <br />\r\nC) Diffraction <br />\r\nD) Absorption</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
