(1932, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An example of sex-linked trait is ..........</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. ability to roll the tongue</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. ability to taste PTC</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. baldness</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. blood group</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1933, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of these agencies do not have anything to do with conservation of natural resources?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Family Economics Advancement Programme</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Federal Environmental Protection Agency</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Nigerian Conservation Foundation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d.Nigerian Game Reserve Authorities</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1934, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of these is NOT a method of asexual reproduction?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. fission</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. fusion</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. fragmentation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. layering</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1935, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which is NOT an effect of the food shortage on a population?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Cannibalism</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Competition</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Increase in mortality</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Increase in natality</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1936, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The gradient of land can be measured with an instrument called a/an?...............</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Aneroid barometer</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Hygrometer</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Slope gauge</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Secchi disc</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1937, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What percentage of oxygen is contained in exhaled air?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. 21%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 16%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 4%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 0.04%</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1938, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which element is a micro element?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Iron</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Magnesium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Manganese</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Phosphorus</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1939, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The number of individuals of a species per unit area of the habitat can be best described as?.............&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Distribution</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Population density</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Population size</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Frequency</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1940, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Soil fertility is NOT conserved by...................</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. contour ridging</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. continuous cropping</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Crop rotation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Mulching</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1941, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of these organisms reproduces by budding?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Amoeba</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Euglena</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Hydra</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Paramecium</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1942, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The decreasing order of the oxidising power of the halogens is?..........</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Br&gt;I&gt;Cl&gt;F &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. &nbsp;F&gt;I&gt;Cl&gt;Br &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. &nbsp;F&gt;Cl&gt;Br&gt;l &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. &nbsp; I&gt;Br&gt;Cl&gt;F</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1943, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which statement BEST describes the process of oxidation?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a.addition of hydrogen</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. loss of oxygen</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. loss of electrons</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. decrease in oxidation number</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1944, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is TRUE of a catalyst?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">I. it alters the activation energy of a reaction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. it is effective in a reaction but cannot initiate a reaction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III, it affects the equilibrium of a reversible reaction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">IV. it affects the overall reaction.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. I and II only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. I, II and III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. II and III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. II, II and IV only</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1945, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The boiling point of water is higher than the boiling point of ethanol because.............</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. the bonding in water is electrovalent (ionic) whereas the bonding in ethanol is convalent</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. the hydrogen bonding between water molecules is stronger than the hydrogen bonding between ethanol molecules</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. water has a higher lattice energy than ethanol</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. water has hydrogen bonding between its molecules but ethanol has no hydrogen bonging between its molecules</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1946, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which is NOT a synthetic polymer?<br />\r\na. nylon</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. wool</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Perspex</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. polystyrene</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1947, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which element is the most electronegative?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Calcium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. fluorine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. iodine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. oxygen</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1948, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which metal bromide is widely used in photography?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. calcium bromide</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. magnesium bromide</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. potassium bromide</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. silver bromide</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1949, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many Faradays of electricity are required to liberate 9g of aluminium?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">[Al = 27]</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. 0.1</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 0.3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 1</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 2.7</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1950, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The type of reaction ethyne mainly undergoes is .........</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. addition</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. carboxylation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. esterification</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. substitution</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1951, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When dust particles collide randomly in a beam of Sunlight, the phenomenon observed is known as<br />\r\na. Tyndall effect</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Dialysis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Diffusion<br />\r\n<br />\r\nd. Osmosis</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1952, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a component of the car exhaust?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Aluminium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Calcium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Lead</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Iron</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1953, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The rate of a chemical reaction is NOT affected by one of these factors ..............</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. colour</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Concentration</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. presence of light</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Temperature</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1954, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pipe-borne water is usually chlorinated in order to.........</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. coagulate sediments in the water</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. improve taste of the water</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. kill harmful bacteria in the water</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. make it pure</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1955, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The action of zinc on an acid produces..............</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. chlorine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Hydrogen</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Nitrogen</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. sulphur</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1956, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">pH is define as?.......</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. [H+] &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. &nbsp; &ndash;log [H] &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. &nbsp;&ndash;log [H+] &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. log [H]</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1957, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Matter is neither created nor destroyed in the course of any chemical reactions is a statement of the law of.......</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. combining volumes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. conservation of mass</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. definite proportion</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. multiple proportion</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1958, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of these arrangement of elements is in order of increasing ionization energy?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Boron, Carbon, Flourine, Nitrogen</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Boron, Carbon, Nitrogen, Flourine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Carbon, Boron, Nitrogen, Flourine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Flourine, Nitro9en, Carbon, Boron</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1959, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A chemical system is at equilibrium when?.........</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. &delta; G is positive &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. &nbsp;&delta; G is zero &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. &nbsp;&delta; S is negative &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. &nbsp;&delta; S is positive</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1960, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of these is NOT a physical property of water?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Can be used to dissolve organic substances</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Has a boiling point of 100 &deg; C&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Has a density of 19cm3 at 40 &deg;C</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. Has a freezing point of 0 &deg; C&nbsp;</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1961, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A colourless gas with characteristics odour which dissolves in water to form an alkaline solution is.........</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. Ammonia</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. carbon(IV)oxide</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. hydrogen chloride</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. sulphur (IV) oxide</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1962, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A piece of stone weights 180 N in air and 150 N in a beaker containing 160 N of methylated spirit. What is the up thrust exerted on the stone?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. 50N</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 40N</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 30N</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 20N</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1963, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the coefficient of static friction between a load of mass 2kg and a horizontal surface, if the limiting frictional force is 10N? (g = 10 ms-2)</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. 0.2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 0.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 5</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1964, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is/areNOT affected by a magnetic field?</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">I. Alpha particle</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. Cathode rays</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III. Neutrons</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. I only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. II only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. I and II only</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1965, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The invisible part of the spectrum of white light consists of............<br />\r\na. Infra-red and ultra-violet only<br />\r\nb. Infra-red, ultra-violet and blue only<br />\r\nc. red, orange and green only<br />\r\nd. red and violet only</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1966, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which scientist discovered natural radioactivity?<br />\r\na. Enrico Fermi</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. Henri Becquerel</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. Marie Curie<br />\r\n<br />\r\nd. Micheal Faraday</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1967, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Notes of the same frequency sounded on a piano and on a flute may differ in</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">I. pitch</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. quality</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III. loudness</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"><br />\r\na. I only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. II only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. I and III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. II and III only</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1968, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Calculate the work done in charging a capacitor of capacitance 20&micro;F through a potential difference of 1000V.<br />\r\na. 0.02 J &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 0.10 J &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 0.20 J &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 10.00J&nbsp;</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1969, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The gravitational field intensity at a location X, in space, is two-fifths of its value on the earth&#39;s surface. If the weight of an object at X is 4.80N. what is its weight on the earth?<br />\r\na. 1.92N</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 2.88N</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 6.72N</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 12.00N<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1970, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Electric charges on the surface of a conductor would be most evenly distributed if the shape of the conductor is?.......<br />\r\na.. Conical</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. cubical</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. cylindrical</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. spherical</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1971, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following types of motion is/are exhibited by a cylindrical drum rolling down an incline plane?<br />\r\na. Random and rotational<br />\r\nb. Rotational and oscillatory<br />\r\nc. Translational and rotational<br />\r\nd. Translations only</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1972, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most suitable instrument for measuring the diameter of a thin wire is a<br />\r\na. meter rule</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. micrometer screw gauge</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. pair of dividers</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. pair of engineer&#39;s calipers</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
