(1974, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which material is best for making a permanent magnet?<br />\r\na. aluminium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. steel</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. cobalt</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. copper<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1975, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 220 V, 60 Hz alternating current supply is connected to an inductor of 3.5H. What is the current passing through the inductor?<br />\r\na. 0.0167 A</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 0.1670 A</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 1.6700 A</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 16.7000 A</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1976, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The lower and upper fixed points of a mercury-in-glass thermometer are marked X and 180 mm respectively. On a particular day the mercury meniscus in the thermometer rises to 60mm. If the corresponding reading on a Celsius scale is 20 &deg; C, what is the value X?<br />\r\na. 6.0mm &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 18.0mm &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 30.0mm &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 60.0mm</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1977, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An object is placed 15cm in front of a concave mirror of focal length 20cm. The image formed is?........<br />\r\na. real, inverted and diminished<br />\r\nb. real, inverted and magnified<br />\r\nc. virtual, erect and diminished<br />\r\nd. virtual, erect and magnified</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1978, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which statement is TRUE of a block of stone of mass m, with zero momentum?<br />\r\na. The acceleration of the stone is non-uniform<br />\r\nb. The stone is stationary<br />\r\nc. The stone moves at a constant velocity<br />\r\nd. The stone moves with maximum velocity</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1979, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which is NOT one of the laws of solid friction?<br />\r\na. The frictional force between two surfaces opposes their relative motion<br />\r\nb. The ratio of frictional force to the normal reaction varies for two given surfaces<br />\r\nc. The ratio of frictional force to the normal reaction is constant for two given surfaces<br />\r\nd. The limiting frictional force is independent of the area of surface in contact.</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1980, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The inside of a vacuum flask is usually coated with silver to reduce heat loss by...........<br />\r\na. condensation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. radiation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. convection</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. evaporation</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1981, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In an operating X-ray tube, a high p.d is applied between the cathode and the anode for the purpose of .................</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">a. concentrating electrons on the target<br />\r\nb. accelerating the electrons to a very high energy<br />\r\nc. heating the anode<br />\r\nd. heating the cathode</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1982, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mr Aborowa bought a car for N200,000.00 and later sold it for N170,000.00. What is the percentage loss?<br />\r\na. 11.60%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 7.60%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 15%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 17.65%</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(1983, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The first term of a G.P is 7. Find its 4th term, if its common ratio is 3.<br />\r\na. 567</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">b. 280</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">c. 189</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">d. 63</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
