(2298, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The girl has just come out of the fattening room and her waist is <strong><ins>adorned</ins></strong> with beads.<br />\r\nA. surrounded &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. decorated &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. besieged<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. defaced</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2299, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Ade is very winsome yet his neighbour finds it difficult to <strong><ins>put up</ins></strong> with him.<br />\r\nA. live with &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. tolerate &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. depend on &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. rely on</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2300, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">There are some drugs that could <strong><ins>exacerbate</ins></strong> a particular illness<br />\r\nA. heal &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. ameliorate &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. lengthen &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. worsen</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2301, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In accordance with the practice of his religion, Raman&#39;s body was <strong><ins>interred</ins></strong> the day he died<br />\r\nA. sanctified &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. preserved &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. cremated<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. buried</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2302, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Abidjan is 4 degree west of Accra and on the same circle of latitude. If the radius of this circle of latitude is 6370km, how far is Abidjan west of Accra, correct to the nearest kilometer? [Take &pi; = 22/7]<br />\r\nA. 222km &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 445km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 890km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5005km</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2303, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If Q = (all perfect squares less than 30) and P = (all odd numbers from 1 to 10). Find Q &cap; P.<br />\r\nA. (1, 4, 9, 16, 25) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. (1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9, 16, 25)</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. (1, 3, 5, 7, 9) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. (1, 9)</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2304, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If K28&minus;&minus;&radic;+63&minus;&minus;&radic;&minus;7&ndash;&radic;=0, find K.<br />\r\nA. -2 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. -1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2305, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A group of 11 people can speak either English or French or Both. Seven can speak English and six can speak French. What is the probability that a person chosen at random can speak both English and French?<br />\r\nA. 2/11 &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4/11 &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 5/11 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. &nbsp;11/13</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2306, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The interior angle of a regular polygon is twice the exterior angle. How many sides has the polygon?<br />\r\nA. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 6</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2307, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following figures have one line of symmetry only? I. Isosceles triangle II. Rhombus III. Kite<br />\r\nA. I and II only<br />\r\nB. II and III only<br />\r\nC. I and III only<br />\r\nD. I, II, and III</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2308, '2024/2025', 'Diploma for Health Technicians', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the 8th term of the A.P -3, -1, 1 ____<br />\r\nA. 13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 11</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. -8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. -11</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
