(2614, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sales girl gave a change of N1.15 to a customer instead of N1.25. Calculate her percentage error<br />\r\nA. 10%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8.0%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.4%</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2615, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Instead of recording the number 1.23cm of the radius of a tube, a student recorded 1.32cm. Find the percentage of error, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 6.8%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7.3%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9.6%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.4%</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2616, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If twice a certain integer is subtracted from 5 times the integer, the result is 63. Find the integer.<br />\r\nA. 21</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 4</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2617, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the median score?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2618, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the range of the distribution?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 10</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2619, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The angle of depression of a point on the ground from the top of a building is 20.3&deg;. If the foot of the building is 40m, calculate the height of the building, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 37.5m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 28.1m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 27.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.8m</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2620, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Given that 1/3log10 P = 1, find the value of P<br />\r\nA. 1/10</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 1000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 10</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 100</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2621, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mr Babalola is 4 times as old as his son, Adu. 7 years ago the sum of their ages was 76. How old is Adu?<br />\r\nA. 22years</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 12years</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 18years<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. 15 years</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2622, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sample of air that has been passed through caustic potash will....................<br />\r\nA. contain more oxygen than nitrogen<br />\r\nB. rekindle a glowing splint<br />\r\nC. have no action on lime water<br />\r\nD. contain no water vapour</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2623, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An acid present in proteins is..........<br />\r\nA. lactic acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. amino acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. propanoic acid<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. palmitic acid</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2624, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are uses of sulphur except......<br />\r\nA. manufacture of tetraoxosulphate (VI) acid<br />\r\nB. prevention of the growth of fungi<br />\r\nC. vulcanization rubber<br />\r\nD. coating of steel to prevent rusting</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2625, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A salt which loses mass when exposed to air is<br />\r\nA. hygroscopic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. deliquescent</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. efflorescent<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. fluorescent</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2626, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Detergents are better than soaps for laundry because..........<br />\r\nA. detergents are synthetic while soaps are not<br />\r\nB. detergents are more soluble in water than soaps<br />\r\nC. scum is precipitated when soaps are used with hard water but not with detergents<br />\r\nD. soaps from soluble salts with ions causing hardness of water while detergents do not</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2627, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is not correct?<br />\r\nA. Sulphur exhibits allotropy<br />\r\nB. Chlorine exhibits allotopy<br />\r\nC. Nitrogen is a gas<br />\r\nD. Argon is a noble gas</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2628, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are heavy chemicals except<br />\r\nA. tetraoxosulphate (IV) acid<br />\r\nB. caustic soda<br />\r\nC. ethene<br />\r\nD. dyes</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2629, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not decomposed by heat?<br />\r\nA. CaCO3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. CuCO3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. ZnCO3<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Na2CO3</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2630, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not true of the rusting of iron?<br />\r\nA. Rusting is a reduction process<br />\r\nB. Rusting of iron takes place in the presence of oxygen and moisture<br />\r\nC. the rust formed is reddish brown<br />\r\nD. the major constituent of rust is hydrated iron (lll) oxide</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2631, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following correctly explains why iodine crystals change directly into the gaseous state when heated?<br />\r\nA. lodine crystals sublime<br />\r\nB. lodine atoms are held together by strong forces<br />\r\nC. lodine molecules are held together by weak forces<br />\r\nD. lodine molecules are covalent</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2632, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements best explains cracking ? It is a process............<br />\r\nA. in which an alkene adds on itself repeatedly to form long chain polymers<br />\r\nB. in which large hydrocarbon molecules are broken into smaller units<br />\r\nC. for measuring theoctane number of petrol<br />\r\nD. in which carbon chain results in a zigzag arrangement</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2633, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most suitable method to use when separating an insoluble solid from a liquid is<br />\r\nA. evaporation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. filtration</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. magnetization<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. sublimation</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2634, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many carbon atoms are there in a benzene ring?<br />\r\nA. 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 7</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2635, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When an element can exist in two or more forms in the same physical state, the element is said to exhibit?.........<br />\r\nA. sublimation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. isomerism</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. allotropy<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. hygroscopy</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2636, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following carbohydrates does NOT usually occur in the crystalline form?<br />\r\nA. Cellulose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Glucose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Sucrose<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Maltose</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2637, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Locally produced soap in which wood ash is used as the base is usually soft because the wood ash contains a lot of............<br />\r\nA. sodium ions</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. potassium ions<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. lithium ions</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. calcium ions</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2638, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Catalytic hydrogenation of oils results in the production of?...........<br />\r\nA. margarine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. detergents</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. alkanes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. butter</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2639, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sample of orange juice is suspected to have been contaminated with a yellow dye. Which of the following methods can be used to detect the dye?<br />\r\nA. Decantation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Chromatography<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Distillation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Filtration</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2640, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When a solid melts and consequently boils, there is .....................<br />\r\nA. a gradual increase in the average kinetic energy of the particles<br />\r\nB. a sudden decrease in the kinetic energy of the particles<br />\r\nC. no change in the average kinetic energy of the particles<br />\r\nD. a rapid change in the nature of bonding of the components</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2641, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following pollutants is biodegradable ?<br />\r\nA. Sewage</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Plastics</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Metal scrape<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Lead compounds</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2642, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A man will exact the greatest pressure on a bench when he_____________<br />\r\nA. lies flat on his back<br />\r\nB. lies flat on his belly<br />\r\nC. stand on both feet<br />\r\nD. stand on toes of one foot</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2643, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The motion of a body is simple harmonic if the____<br />\r\nA. Acceleration is always directed towards a fixed point<br />\r\nB. path of motion is a striaght line<br />\r\nC. Acceleration is directed towards a fixed point and proportional to its distance from the point<br />\r\nD. Acceleration is proportional to the square of the distance from a fixed point</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2644, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The clinical thermometer is characterized by having a ____________<br />\r\nA. wide range of temperature</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. wide bore<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. long stem</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. constriction</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2645, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a reason why a concrete floor feels colder to the bare feet than a mat on the same floor during the rainy season?<br />\r\nA. A mat if s better conductor of heat than the feet<br />\r\nB. Mat losses heat to the bare feet at a faster rate than concrete floor<br />\r\nC. Mat losses heat to the bare feet while the concrete floor extracts heat from them<br />\r\nD. Concrete floor is a better conductor of heat than the mat.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2646, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best explains a person who suffers more severe burns when his skin is exposed to steam than when boiling water is poured onto his skin?<br />\r\nA. steam is at a higher temperature than boiling water<br />\r\nB. steam posses greater heat energy per unit-mass than boiling water<br />\r\nC. steam spreads more easily over a wider area of the skin than boiling water<br />\r\nD. steam panetrates more easily over a wider area of the skin than boiling water</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2647, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The temperature at which the water vapour present in the air is just sufficient to saturate it is called the<br />\r\nA. ice point</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. boiling point</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. steam point<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. dew point</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2648, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following will affect the saturation vapour pressure of a liquid?<br />\r\nA. Temperature of the liquid<br />\r\nB. Humidity of air<br />\r\nC. Volume of vapour<br />\r\nD. Volume of the liquidhich statement BEST</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2649, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transparent rectangular block 5.0cm thick is placed on a black dot. The dot when viewed from above is seem 3.0cm from the top of the block calculate the refractive index of the material of the block.<br />\r\nA. 2/5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5/3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 3/2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 3/5</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2650, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An object is placed 36cm from a converging lens of focal length 24cm.If a real image which is 4cm high is formed, Calculate the height of the object.<br />\r\nA. 2.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.0cm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2651, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ability of the eye to focus objects at different distances is called___________<br />\r\nA. power</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. accommodation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. normal vision<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. persistence of vision</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2652, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The change of the direction of a wave-front because of a change in the velocity of the wave in another medium is called?<br />\r\nA. refraction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. reflection</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. diffraction<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. interference</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2653, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A boy standing a distance from the foot of a tall cliff claps his hands and hears an echo 0.5s later. If the speed of sound is 340ms1, how far is he from the cliff?<br />\r\nA. 17m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 34m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 85m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 170m</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2654, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sounding tuning fork is brought near the end of a pipe containing an air column and the loudness of the sound increases. This effect is due to_______<br />\r\nA. diffraction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. an echo</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. resonance<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. interference</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2655, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transformer with 5500 turns in its primary is used between a 240V a. c supply and a 120V kettle. Calculate the number of turns in the secondary<br />\r\nA. 11000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2750</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 460</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 232</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2656, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">It takes 4 minutes to boil a quantity of water electrically. How long will it take to boil same quantity of water using the same heating coil but with the current doubled? (neglecting any external heat loss).<br />\r\nA. 1 minute</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 32 minutes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8 minutes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. 2 minutes</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(2657, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following particles of ray has the highest penetrating power?<br />\r\nA. Beta particles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Gamma particles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Electrons</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Neutrons</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2658, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is/are not correct about isotopes of an element? They have_______<br />\r\nA. the same neutron number<br />\r\nB. the same proton number<br />\r\nC. same number of electrons<br />\r\nD. same chemical properties</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2659, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not an electromagnetic radiation?<br />\r\nA. X-ray</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Radio waves</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Sunlight<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Sound waves</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2660, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During the same interval, it is observed that a train travels the same distance as does a lorry. The two vehicles therefore have the same<br />\r\nA. uniform accelation<br />\r\nB. instateneous velocity<br />\r\nC. initial velocity<br />\r\nD. average speed</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2661, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a derived unit?<br />\r\nA. Metre</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Coulomb</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Kilogram</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Second</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2662, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ability of organisms to maintain a constant internal environment is known as<br />\r\nA. homeostasis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. endosmosis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. plasmolysis<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. dialysis</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2663, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Double fertilization is said to occur in flowering pants because?<br />\r\nA. two embryos are formed<br />\r\nB. one egg is fertilized twice<br />\r\nC. two sperms and two pollen grains are involved<br />\r\nD. one embryo and endosperm nucleus are formed</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2664, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pulmonary artery carries___________</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A. deoxygenated blood from the right ventricles to the lungs<br />\r\nB. oxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs<br />\r\nC. oxygenated blood from the left ventricles to the ventricles to the right auricle<br />\r\nD. deoxygenated blood from the left ventricles to the right auricles</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2665, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following blood components has the greatest affinity for oxygen and carbondioxide?<br />\r\nA. Blood plasma</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Leucocytes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Thrombocytes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Erythrocyte</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2666, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The thoracic cavity is separated from the abdominal cavity by a sheet of muscle called<br />\r\nA. pleural membrane<br />\r\nB. intercostal muscles<br />\r\nC. diaphragm<br />\r\nD. pericardium</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2667, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements on urine production is not correct?<br />\r\nA. in the presence of antidiuretic hormone dilute urine is produced<br />\r\nB. The total volume of urine produced depends on the need for water excretion<br />\r\nC. if there is excess intake of water, dilute urine is expected<br />\r\nD. if there is a shortage of water in the body the volume of the urine produced is decreased</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2668, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pigment in the malphigian layer responsible for skin colouration is known as<br />\r\nA. haemoglobin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. haemocyanin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. melanin<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. haemoerythrin</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2669, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is correct of hormones? Hormones are<br />\r\nA. secreted into the blood through ducts<br />\r\nB. secreted directly into the blood streem<br />\r\nC. inactive chemical substance in the blood stream<br />\r\nD. non-specific in their mode of action</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2670, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pituitary is called &#39;master gland&#39; because<br />\r\nA. it is locatd in the brain<br />\r\nB. its secretion are the more numerous than those of the other gland<br />\r\nC. its secretion controls the other glands<br />\r\nD. it is the only organ that produces hormone</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2671, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The brain and the spinal cord make up the<br />\r\nA. pheripheral nervous system<br />\r\nB. automatic nervous system<br />\r\nC. central nervous system<br />\r\nD. somatic nervous system</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2672, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following specialized structures are stimulated by touch, pressure, pain, heat and cold?<br />\r\nA. Receptors</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Synapse</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cell bodies<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Myelin sheath</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2673, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not correct about a fruit? lt<br />\r\nA. may contain many seeds<br />\r\nB. is a mature ovary<br />\r\nC. is covered by the pericarp<br />\r\nD. may develop from the receptacle</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2674, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which structure in the maize grain stores food?<br />\r\nA. Endosperm.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Embryo</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cytoplasm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Seed coat</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2675, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Even though some flowering plants contain accessory pigments which give them colours they still contain<br />\r\nthe pigment<br />\r\nA. melanin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chlorophyll</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. xanthrophyll<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. carotene</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2676, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The relationship between a herbivore and the bacteria which live in its caecum is known as<br />\r\nA. parasitism</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. symbiosis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. predation<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. saprophytism</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2677, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Autotropic nutrition may be defined in terms of food obtained<br />\r\nA. from other organisms in exchange for some products.<br />\r\nB. by the breakdown of complex substances<br />\r\nC. by an organism utilizing its own store of energy<br />\r\nD. by synthesizing simple substances using energy from an external source</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2678, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following does not contribute to the biomass in an ecosystem?<br />\r\nA. Producers</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Food chains</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Consumers<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Micro-organisms</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2679, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a characteristic feature of tropical rain-forest habitat?<br />\r\nA. Trees with longer boles than those in Savannah<br />\r\nB. Fewer canopy strata than the savannah<br />\r\nC. Many more trees and climbers than savannah<br />\r\nD. Plenty of leaf litter on the ground</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2680, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factors is not associated with aquatic habitat?<br />\r\nA. Temperature</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Light intensity</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Humidity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Turbidity</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2681, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The causative organism of sleeping sickness is the?<br />\r\nA. Trypanosome</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Plasmodium<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Vibrio bacterium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. tsetse fly</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(2682, '2024/2025', 'Professional Certificate in Medical Image Processing/X-ray Technician', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Probably the motorist saw the - 1 -&nbsp;lorry too - 2 - to be able to - 3 - disaster. However, he realized that if he kept to the - 4 -, a probably - 5 - head on - 6 - would be unavoidable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The only alternative was to take the lesser risk of leaving the road. With great care therefore, he turned sharply - 87 - the road into the ditch by the - 88 -. The consequence was that, instead of being involved in a serious and probably fatal - 9 -, the - 10&nbsp;- escaped with a few minor - 11 - and bruises, while the only - 12 - to his car was a bent mudguard.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">By - 13 - into the roadside ditch to avoid what could have been a collision with the approaching lorry, he averted a - 14 - accident at the - 15 - of a few - 16 - to himself and the slight damage to his car.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"><strong>In numbered 1 above, choose the best option from letters A - D that best completes the gap</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"><br />\r\nA. incoming</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. oncoming</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. downcoming<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. offcoming</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
