(3001, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Complementary Health Sciences (Natural/Alternative Medicine)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In accordance with the practice of his religion, Raman&#39;s body was <strong><ins>interred</ins></strong> the day he died<br />\r\nA. sanctified &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. preserved &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. cremated<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. buried</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3002, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Abidjan is 4 degree west of Accra and on the same circle of latitude. If the radius of this circle of latitude is 6370km, how far is Abidjan west of Accra, correct to the nearest kilometer? [Take &pi; = 22/7]<br />\r\nA. 222km &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 445km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 890km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5005km</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3003, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If Q = (all perfect squares less than 30) and P = (all odd numbers from 1 to 10). Find Q &cap; P.<br />\r\nA. (1, 4, 9, 16, 25) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. (1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9, 16, 25)</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. (1, 3, 5, 7, 9) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. (1, 9)</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3004, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If K28&minus;&minus;&radic;+63&minus;&minus;&radic;&minus;7&ndash;&radic;=0, find K.<br />\r\nA. -2 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. -1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3005, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A group of 11 people can speak either English or French or Both. Seven can speak English and six can speak French. What is the probability that a person chosen at random can speak both English and French?<br />\r\nA. 2/11 &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4/11 &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 5/11 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. &nbsp;11/13</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3006, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The interior angle of a regular polygon is twice the exterior angle. How many sides has the polygon?<br />\r\nA. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 6</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3007, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following figures have one line of symmetry only? I. Isosceles triangle II. Rhombus III. Kite<br />\r\nA. I and II only<br />\r\nB. II and III only<br />\r\nC. I and III only<br />\r\nD. I, II, and III</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3008, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the 8th term of the A.P -3, -1, 1 ____<br />\r\nA. 13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 11</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. -8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. -11</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3009, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0 1 2 3 4 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">FREQUENCY&nbsp; 2 3 4 2 7 2<br />\r\nA group of students took a test and the following frequency table shows the scores above. Find the mode<br />\r\nA. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3010, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0 1 2 3 4 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">FREQUENCY&nbsp; 2 3 4 2 7 2<br />\r\nA group of students took a test and the following frequency table shows the scores above. The mean score is__________<br />\r\nA. 1.75</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 2.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.75</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3011, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A ladder 9m long leans against a vertical wall, making an angle of 64? with the horizontal ground. calculate correct to one decimal place, how far the foot of the ladder is from the wall.<br />\r\nA. 4.0m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7.1m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.1m</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3012, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The number 186,470 was corrected to 186,000. Which of the following describe the degree of approximation made?<br />\r\nI. to the nearest hundred</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. to the nearest thousand</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III. to 3 significant figures</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">IV. to 4 significant figures</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"><br />\r\nA. I &amp; III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. I &amp; IV only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. II &amp; III only<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. II &amp; IV only</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3013, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Points P and Q respectively 24m north and 7m east point R. Calculate |PQ| in meters<br />\r\nA. 20</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 24</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 25</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 31</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3014, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sales girl gave a change of N1.15 to a customer instead of N1.25. Calculate her percentage error<br />\r\nA. 10%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8.0%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.4%</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3015, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Instead of recording the number 1.23cm of the radius of a tube, a student recorded 1.32cm. Find the percentage of error, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 6.8%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7.3%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9.6%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.4%</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3016, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If twice a certain integer is subtracted from 5 times the integer, the result is 63. Find the integer.<br />\r\nA. 21</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 4</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3017, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the median score?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3018, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the range of the distribution?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 10</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3019, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The angle of depression of a point on the ground from the top of a building is 20.3&deg;. If the foot of the building is 40m, calculate the height of the building, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 37.5m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 28.1m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 27.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.8m</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3020, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Given that 1/3log10 P = 1, find the value of P<br />\r\nA. 1/10</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 1000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 10</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 100</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3021, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mr Babalola is 4 times as old as his son, Adu. 7 years ago the sum of their ages was 76. How old is Adu?<br />\r\nA. 22years</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 12years</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 18years<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. 15 years</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3022, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sample of air that has been passed through caustic potash will....................<br />\r\nA. contain more oxygen than nitrogen<br />\r\nB. rekindle a glowing splint<br />\r\nC. have no action on lime water<br />\r\nD. contain no water vapour</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3023, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An acid present in proteins is..........<br />\r\nA. lactic acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. amino acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. propanoic acid<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. palmitic acid</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3024, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are uses of sulphur except......<br />\r\nA. manufacture of tetraoxosulphate (VI) acid<br />\r\nB. prevention of the growth of fungi<br />\r\nC. vulcanization rubber<br />\r\nD. coating of steel to prevent rusting</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3025, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A salt which loses mass when exposed to air is<br />\r\nA. hygroscopic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. deliquescent</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. efflorescent<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. fluorescent</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3026, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Detergents are better than soaps for laundry because..........<br />\r\nA. detergents are synthetic while soaps are not<br />\r\nB. detergents are more soluble in water than soaps<br />\r\nC. scum is precipitated when soaps are used with hard water but not with detergents<br />\r\nD. soaps from soluble salts with ions causing hardness of water while detergents do not</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3027, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Health Promotion and education', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is not correct?<br />\r\nA. Sulphur exhibits allotropy<br />\r\nB. Chlorine exhibits allotopy<br />\r\nC. Nitrogen is a gas<br />\r\nD. Argon is a noble gas</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
