(3198, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Medical Social Work', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The girl has just come out of the fattening room and her waist is <strong><ins>adorned</ins></strong> with beads.<br />\r\nA. surrounded &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. decorated &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. besieged<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. defaced</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3199, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Medical Social Work', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Ade is very winsome yet his neighbour finds it difficult to <strong><ins>put up</ins></strong> with him.<br />\r\nA. live with &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. tolerate &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. depend on &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. rely on</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3200, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Medical Social Work', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">There are some drugs that could <strong><ins>exacerbate</ins></strong> a particular illness<br />\r\nA. heal &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. ameliorate &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. lengthen &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. worsen</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3201, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Medical Social Work', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In accordance with the practice of his religion, Raman&#39;s body was <strong><ins>interred</ins></strong> the day he died<br />\r\nA. sanctified &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. preserved &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. cremated<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. buried</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3202, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Abidjan is 4 degree west of Accra and on the same circle of latitude. If the radius of this circle of latitude is 6370km, how far is Abidjan west of Accra, correct to the nearest kilometer? [Take &pi; = 22/7]<br />\r\nA. 222km &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 445km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 890km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5005km</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3203, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If Q = (all perfect squares less than 30) and P = (all odd numbers from 1 to 10). Find Q &cap; P.<br />\r\nA. (1, 4, 9, 16, 25) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. (1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9, 16, 25)</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. (1, 3, 5, 7, 9) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. (1, 9)</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3204, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If K28&minus;&minus;&radic;+63&minus;&minus;&radic;&minus;7&ndash;&radic;=0, find K.<br />\r\nA. -2 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. -1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3205, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A group of 11 people can speak either English or French or Both. Seven can speak English and six can speak French. What is the probability that a person chosen at random can speak both English and French?<br />\r\nA. 2/11 &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4/11 &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 5/11 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. &nbsp;11/13</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3206, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The interior angle of a regular polygon is twice the exterior angle. How many sides has the polygon?<br />\r\nA. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 6</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3207, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following figures have one line of symmetry only? I. Isosceles triangle II. Rhombus III. Kite<br />\r\nA. I and II only<br />\r\nB. II and III only<br />\r\nC. I and III only<br />\r\nD. I, II, and III</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3208, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the 8th term of the A.P -3, -1, 1 ____<br />\r\nA. 13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 11</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. -8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. -11</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3209, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0 1 2 3 4 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">FREQUENCY&nbsp; 2 3 4 2 7 2<br />\r\nA group of students took a test and the following frequency table shows the scores above. Find the mode<br />\r\nA. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3210, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0 1 2 3 4 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">FREQUENCY&nbsp; 2 3 4 2 7 2<br />\r\nA group of students took a test and the following frequency table shows the scores above. The mean score is__________<br />\r\nA. 1.75</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 2.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.75</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3211, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A ladder 9m long leans against a vertical wall, making an angle of 64? with the horizontal ground. calculate correct to one decimal place, how far the foot of the ladder is from the wall.<br />\r\nA. 4.0m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7.1m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.1m</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3212, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The number 186,470 was corrected to 186,000. Which of the following describe the degree of approximation made?<br />\r\nI. to the nearest hundred</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. to the nearest thousand</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III. to 3 significant figures</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">IV. to 4 significant figures</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"><br />\r\nA. I &amp; III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. I &amp; IV only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. II &amp; III only<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. II &amp; IV only</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3213, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Points P and Q respectively 24m north and 7m east point R. Calculate |PQ| in meters<br />\r\nA. 20</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 24</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 25</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 31</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3214, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sales girl gave a change of N1.15 to a customer instead of N1.25. Calculate her percentage error<br />\r\nA. 10%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8.0%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.4%</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3215, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Instead of recording the number 1.23cm of the radius of a tube, a student recorded 1.32cm. Find the percentage of error, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 6.8%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7.3%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9.6%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.4%</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3216, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If twice a certain integer is subtracted from 5 times the integer, the result is 63. Find the integer.<br />\r\nA. 21</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 4</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3217, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the median score?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3218, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the range of the distribution?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 10</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3219, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The angle of depression of a point on the ground from the top of a building is 20.3&deg;. If the foot of the building is 40m, calculate the height of the building, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 37.5m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 28.1m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 27.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.8m</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3220, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Given that 1/3log10 P = 1, find the value of P<br />\r\nA. 1/10</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 1000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 10</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 100</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3221, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mr Babalola is 4 times as old as his son, Adu. 7 years ago the sum of their ages was 76. How old is Adu?<br />\r\nA. 22years</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 12years</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 18years<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. 15 years</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3222, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sample of air that has been passed through caustic potash will....................<br />\r\nA. contain more oxygen than nitrogen<br />\r\nB. rekindle a glowing splint<br />\r\nC. have no action on lime water<br />\r\nD. contain no water vapour</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3223, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An acid present in proteins is..........<br />\r\nA. lactic acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. amino acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. propanoic acid<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. palmitic acid</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3224, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are uses of sulphur except......<br />\r\nA. manufacture of tetraoxosulphate (VI) acid<br />\r\nB. prevention of the growth of fungi<br />\r\nC. vulcanization rubber<br />\r\nD. coating of steel to prevent rusting</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3225, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A salt which loses mass when exposed to air is<br />\r\nA. hygroscopic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. deliquescent</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. efflorescent<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. fluorescent</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3226, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Detergents are better than soaps for laundry because..........<br />\r\nA. detergents are synthetic while soaps are not<br />\r\nB. detergents are more soluble in water than soaps<br />\r\nC. scum is precipitated when soaps are used with hard water but not with detergents<br />\r\nD. soaps from soluble salts with ions causing hardness of water while detergents do not</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3227, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is not correct?<br />\r\nA. Sulphur exhibits allotropy<br />\r\nB. Chlorine exhibits allotopy<br />\r\nC. Nitrogen is a gas<br />\r\nD. Argon is a noble gas</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3228, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are heavy chemicals except<br />\r\nA. tetraoxosulphate (IV) acid<br />\r\nB. caustic soda<br />\r\nC. ethene<br />\r\nD. dyes</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3229, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not decomposed by heat?<br />\r\nA. CaCO3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. CuCO3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. ZnCO3<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Na2CO3</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3230, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not true of the rusting of iron?<br />\r\nA. Rusting is a reduction process<br />\r\nB. Rusting of iron takes place in the presence of oxygen and moisture<br />\r\nC. the rust formed is reddish brown<br />\r\nD. the major constituent of rust is hydrated iron (lll) oxide</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3231, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following correctly explains why iodine crystals change directly into the gaseous state when heated?<br />\r\nA. lodine crystals sublime<br />\r\nB. lodine atoms are held together by strong forces<br />\r\nC. lodine molecules are held together by weak forces<br />\r\nD. lodine molecules are covalent</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3232, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements best explains cracking ? It is a process............<br />\r\nA. in which an alkene adds on itself repeatedly to form long chain polymers<br />\r\nB. in which large hydrocarbon molecules are broken into smaller units<br />\r\nC. for measuring theoctane number of petrol<br />\r\nD. in which carbon chain results in a zigzag arrangement</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3233, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most suitable method to use when separating an insoluble solid from a liquid is<br />\r\nA. evaporation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. filtration</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. magnetization<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. sublimation</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3234, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many carbon atoms are there in a benzene ring?<br />\r\nA. 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 7</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3235, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When an element can exist in two or more forms in the same physical state, the element is said to exhibit?.........<br />\r\nA. sublimation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. isomerism</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. allotropy<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. hygroscopy</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3236, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following carbohydrates does NOT usually occur in the crystalline form?<br />\r\nA. Cellulose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Glucose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Sucrose<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Maltose</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3237, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Locally produced soap in which wood ash is used as the base is usually soft because the wood ash contains a lot of............<br />\r\nA. sodium ions</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. potassium ions<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. lithium ions</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. calcium ions</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3238, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Catalytic hydrogenation of oils results in the production of?...........<br />\r\nA. margarine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. detergents</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. alkanes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. butter</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3239, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sample of orange juice is suspected to have been contaminated with a yellow dye. Which of the following methods can be used to detect the dye?<br />\r\nA. Decantation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Chromatography<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Distillation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Filtration</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3240, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When a solid melts and consequently boils, there is .....................<br />\r\nA. a gradual increase in the average kinetic energy of the particles<br />\r\nB. a sudden decrease in the kinetic energy of the particles<br />\r\nC. no change in the average kinetic energy of the particles<br />\r\nD. a rapid change in the nature of bonding of the components</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3241, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following pollutants is biodegradable ?<br />\r\nA. Sewage</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Plastics</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Metal scrape<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Lead compounds</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3242, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A man will exact the greatest pressure on a bench when he_____________<br />\r\nA. lies flat on his back<br />\r\nB. lies flat on his belly<br />\r\nC. stand on both feet<br />\r\nD. stand on toes of one foot</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3243, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The motion of a body is simple harmonic if the____<br />\r\nA. Acceleration is always directed towards a fixed point<br />\r\nB. path of motion is a striaght line<br />\r\nC. Acceleration is directed towards a fixed point and proportional to its distance from the point<br />\r\nD. Acceleration is proportional to the square of the distance from a fixed point</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3244, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The clinical thermometer is characterized by having a ____________<br />\r\nA. wide range of temperature</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. wide bore<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. long stem</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. constriction</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3245, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a reason why a concrete floor feels colder to the bare feet than a mat on the same floor during the rainy season?<br />\r\nA. A mat if s better conductor of heat than the feet<br />\r\nB. Mat losses heat to the bare feet at a faster rate than concrete floor<br />\r\nC. Mat losses heat to the bare feet while the concrete floor extracts heat from them<br />\r\nD. Concrete floor is a better conductor of heat than the mat.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(3246, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best explains a person who suffers more severe burns when his skin is exposed to steam than when boiling water is poured onto his skin?<br />\r\nA. steam is at a higher temperature than boiling water<br />\r\nB. steam posses greater heat energy per unit-mass than boiling water<br />\r\nC. steam spreads more easily over a wider area of the skin than boiling water<br />\r\nD. steam panetrates more easily over a wider area of the skin than boiling water</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3247, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The temperature at which the water vapour present in the air is just sufficient to saturate it is called the<br />\r\nA. ice point</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. boiling point</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. steam point<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. dew point</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3248, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following will affect the saturation vapour pressure of a liquid?<br />\r\nA. Temperature of the liquid<br />\r\nB. Humidity of air<br />\r\nC. Volume of vapour<br />\r\nD. Volume of the liquidhich statement BEST</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3249, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transparent rectangular block 5.0cm thick is placed on a black dot. The dot when viewed from above is seem 3.0cm from the top of the block calculate the refractive index of the material of the block.<br />\r\nA. 2/5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5/3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 3/2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 3/5</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3250, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An object is placed 36cm from a converging lens of focal length 24cm.If a real image which is 4cm high is formed, Calculate the height of the object.<br />\r\nA. 2.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.0cm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3251, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ability of the eye to focus objects at different distances is called___________<br />\r\nA. power</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. accommodation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. normal vision<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. persistence of vision</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3252, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The change of the direction of a wave-front because of a change in the velocity of the wave in another medium is called?<br />\r\nA. refraction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. reflection</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. diffraction<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. interference</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3253, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A boy standing a distance from the foot of a tall cliff claps his hands and hears an echo 0.5s later. If the speed of sound is 340ms1, how far is he from the cliff?<br />\r\nA. 17m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 34m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 85m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 170m</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3254, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sounding tuning fork is brought near the end of a pipe containing an air column and the loudness of the sound increases. This effect is due to_______<br />\r\nA. diffraction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. an echo</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. resonance<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. interference</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3255, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transformer with 5500 turns in its primary is used between a 240V a. c supply and a 120V kettle. Calculate the number of turns in the secondary<br />\r\nA. 11000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2750</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 460</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 232</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3256, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">It takes 4 minutes to boil a quantity of water electrically. How long will it take to boil same quantity of water using the same heating coil but with the current doubled? (neglecting any external heat loss).<br />\r\nA. 1 minute</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 32 minutes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8 minutes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. 2 minutes</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3257, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following particles of ray has the highest penetrating power?<br />\r\nA. Beta particles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Gamma particles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Electrons</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Neutrons</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3258, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is/are not correct about isotopes of an element? They have_______<br />\r\nA. the same neutron number<br />\r\nB. the same proton number<br />\r\nC. same number of electrons<br />\r\nD. same chemical properties</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3259, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not an electromagnetic radiation?<br />\r\nA. X-ray</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Radio waves</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Sunlight<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Sound waves</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3260, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During the same interval, it is observed that a train travels the same distance as does a lorry. The two vehicles therefore have the same<br />\r\nA. uniform accelation<br />\r\nB. instateneous velocity<br />\r\nC. initial velocity<br />\r\nD. average speed</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3261, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a derived unit?<br />\r\nA. Metre</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Coulomb</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Kilogram</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Second</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3262, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ability of organisms to maintain a constant internal environment is known as<br />\r\nA. homeostasis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. endosmosis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. plasmolysis<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. dialysis</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3263, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Double fertilization is said to occur in flowering pants because?<br />\r\nA. two embryos are formed<br />\r\nB. one egg is fertilized twice<br />\r\nC. two sperms and two pollen grains are involved<br />\r\nD. one embryo and endosperm nucleus are formed</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3264, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pulmonary artery carries___________</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A. deoxygenated blood from the right ventricles to the lungs<br />\r\nB. oxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs<br />\r\nC. oxygenated blood from the left ventricles to the ventricles to the right auricle<br />\r\nD. deoxygenated blood from the left ventricles to the right auricles</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3265, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following blood components has the greatest affinity for oxygen and carbondioxide?<br />\r\nA. Blood plasma</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Leucocytes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Thrombocytes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Erythrocyte</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3266, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The thoracic cavity is separated from the abdominal cavity by a sheet of muscle called<br />\r\nA. pleural membrane<br />\r\nB. intercostal muscles<br />\r\nC. diaphragm<br />\r\nD. pericardium</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3267, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements on urine production is not correct?<br />\r\nA. in the presence of antidiuretic hormone dilute urine is produced<br />\r\nB. The total volume of urine produced depends on the need for water excretion<br />\r\nC. if there is excess intake of water, dilute urine is expected<br />\r\nD. if there is a shortage of water in the body the volume of the urine produced is decreased</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3268, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pigment in the malphigian layer responsible for skin colouration is known as<br />\r\nA. haemoglobin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. haemocyanin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. melanin<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. haemoerythrin</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3269, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is correct of hormones? Hormones are<br />\r\nA. secreted into the blood through ducts<br />\r\nB. secreted directly into the blood streem<br />\r\nC. inactive chemical substance in the blood stream<br />\r\nD. non-specific in their mode of action</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3270, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pituitary is called &#39;master gland&#39; because<br />\r\nA. it is locatd in the brain<br />\r\nB. its secretion are the more numerous than those of the other gland<br />\r\nC. its secretion controls the other glands<br />\r\nD. it is the only organ that produces hormone</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3271, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The brain and the spinal cord make up the<br />\r\nA. pheripheral nervous system<br />\r\nB. automatic nervous system<br />\r\nC. central nervous system<br />\r\nD. somatic nervous system</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3272, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following specialized structures are stimulated by touch, pressure, pain, heat and cold?<br />\r\nA. Receptors</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Synapse</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cell bodies<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Myelin sheath</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3273, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not correct about a fruit? lt<br />\r\nA. may contain many seeds<br />\r\nB. is a mature ovary<br />\r\nC. is covered by the pericarp<br />\r\nD. may develop from the receptacle</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3274, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which structure in the maize grain stores food?<br />\r\nA. Endosperm.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Embryo</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cytoplasm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Seed coat</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3275, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Even though some flowering plants contain accessory pigments which give them colours they still contain<br />\r\nthe pigment<br />\r\nA. melanin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chlorophyll</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. xanthrophyll<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. carotene</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3276, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The relationship between a herbivore and the bacteria which live in its caecum is known as<br />\r\nA. parasitism</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. symbiosis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. predation<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. saprophytism</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3277, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Autotropic nutrition may be defined in terms of food obtained<br />\r\nA. from other organisms in exchange for some products.<br />\r\nB. by the breakdown of complex substances<br />\r\nC. by an organism utilizing its own store of energy<br />\r\nD. by synthesizing simple substances using energy from an external source</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3278, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following does not contribute to the biomass in an ecosystem?<br />\r\nA. Producers</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Food chains</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Consumers<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Micro-organisms</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3279, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a characteristic feature of tropical rain-forest habitat?<br />\r\nA. Trees with longer boles than those in Savannah<br />\r\nB. Fewer canopy strata than the savannah<br />\r\nC. Many more trees and climbers than savannah<br />\r\nD. Plenty of leaf litter on the ground</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3280, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factors is not associated with aquatic habitat?<br />\r\nA. Temperature</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Light intensity</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Humidity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Turbidity</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3281, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Tourism and Hospitality Management', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The causative organism of sleeping sickness is the?<br />\r\nA. Trypanosome</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Plasmodium<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Vibrio bacterium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. tsetse fly</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
