(3354, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Newborns have a higher respiratory rate compared to older children and adults.<br />\r\n(A) True<br />\r\n(B) False</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3355, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which reflex is typically checked for reflex irritability in the Apgar score?<br />\r\n(A) Rooting reflex<br />\r\n(B) Moro reflex<br />\r\n(C) Grasp reflex<br />\r\n(D) Response to stimulation</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3356, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal respiratory rate range for a newborn?<br />\r\n(A) 20-30 breaths per minute<br />\r\n(B) 30-60 breaths per minute<br />\r\n(C) 40-80 breaths per minute<br />\r\n(D) 60-100 breaths per minute</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3357, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The closure of which structure is a critical component of the newborn&#39;s cardiovascular adaptation to extrauterine life?<br />\r\n(A) Foramen ovale<br />\r\n(B) Ductus arteriosus<br />\r\n(C) Ductus venosus<br />\r\n(D) All of the above</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3358, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of the fetal circulatory system allows blood to bypass the lungs?<br />\r\n(A) Foramen ovale<br />\r\n(B) Ductus venosus<br />\r\n(C) Ductus arteriosus<br />\r\n(D) Umbilical vein</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3359, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The initial breath of a newborn is stimulated by:<br />\r\n(A) Increased oxygen levels<br />\r\n(B) Decreased carbon dioxide levels<br />\r\n(C) Changes in temperature and environmental pressure<br />\r\n(D) Nutrient intake</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3360, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A completely pink baby would receive a score of:<br />\r\n(A) 0<br />\r\n(B) 1<br />\r\n(C) 2<br />\r\n(D) 3</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3361, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a primary function of surfactant in the newborn&#39;s lungs?<br />\r\n(A) Enhance lung compliance and prevent alveolar collapse<br />\r\n(B) Increase blood flow to the lungs<br />\r\n(C) Regulate heart rate<br />\r\n(D) Control body temperature</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3362, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are examples of epidemic-prone diseases?<br />\r\nA) HIV, Tuberculosis, Chickenpox<br />\r\nB) Cholera, Ebola, Yellow Fever<br />\r\nC) Diabetes, Hypertension, Asthma<br />\r\nD) Alzheimer&#39;s disease, Parkinson&#39;s disease, Multiple sclerosis</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3363, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which diseases are targeted for eradication and elimination efforts?<br />\r\nA) Common cold, Seasonal allergies, Headaches<br />\r\nB) Polio, Guinea worm disease, Measles<br />\r\nC) Diabetes, Hypertension, Asthma<br />\r\nD) Alzheimer&#39;s disease, Parkinson&#39;s disease, Multiple sclerosis</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3364, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What defines diseases of public health importance?<br />\r\nA) Diseases with high mortality rates<br />\r\nB) Diseases affecting specific age groups<br />\r\nC) Diseases that are reportable due to their significance<br />\r\nD) Chronic diseases with long-lasting effects</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3365, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary means of breaking the chain of infection?<br />\r\nA) Vaccination<br />\r\nB) Hand hygiene<br />\r\nC) Quarantine<br />\r\nD) Antibiotic treatment</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3366, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an infectious agent?<br />\r\nA) A disease vector<br />\r\nB) A reservoir for microorganisms<br />\r\nC) A means of disease transmission<br />\r\nD) A microorganism causing infectious disease</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3367, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Where do microorganisms thrive and reproduce in reservoirs?<br />\r\nA) Only in human beings<br />\r\nB) Only in animals<br />\r\nC) Only in inanimate objects<br />\r\nD) In human beings, animals, and inanimate objects</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3368, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a portal of exit?<br />\r\nA) A way for microorganisms to enter a new host<br />\r\nB) A way for microorganisms to leave the reservoir<br />\r\nC) A means of indirect transmission<br />\r\nD) A method of vector-borne transmission</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3369, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How are microorganisms carried from one place to another in the mode of transmission?<br />\r\nA) By contact only<br />\r\nB) By airborne particles only<br />\r\nC) By a combination of means<br />\r\nD) By vector-borne transmission only</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3370, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the portal of entry?<br />\r\nA) A way for microorganisms to leave the reservoir<br />\r\nB) A means by which microorganisms gain access to a new host<br />\r\nC) A method of transmission<br />\r\nD) A reservoir for microorganisms</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3371, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Who is a susceptible host?<br />\r\nA) A person with immunity to a disease<br />\r\nB) A person without physical resistance to a disease<br />\r\nC) A person with high pathogenicity<br />\r\nD) A person without exposure to microorganisms</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3372, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main mode of direct transmission?<br />\r\nA) Droplet transmission<br />\r\nB) Airborne transmission<br />\r\nC) Vector-borne transmission<br />\r\nD) Contact transmission</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3373, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does indirect contact transmission occur?<br />\r\nA) Through direct physical contact<br />\r\nB) Through large droplets in the air<br />\r\nC) Via transfer of microorganisms via an object<br />\r\nD) Through contaminated food or water</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3374, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is involved in droplet transmission?<br />\r\nA) Transfer of microorganisms via contaminated food<br />\r\nB) Transfer of microorganisms via large droplets from sneezing or coughing<br />\r\nC) Transfer of microorganisms via vectors<br />\r\nD) Transfer of microorganisms via direct physical contact</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3375, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How are microorganisms transmitted in airborne transmission?<br />\r\nA) Through contaminated objects<br />\r\nB) Through small particles suspended in the air<br />\r\nC) Through direct physical contact<br />\r\nD) Through droplets from sneezing or coughing</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3376, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does common vehicle transmission refer to?<br />\r\nA) Transmission through vectors<br />\r\nB) Transmission through airborne particles<br />\r\nC) Transmission through contaminated sources<br />\r\nD) Transmission through direct physical contact</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3377, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does vector-borne transmission occur?<br />\r\nA) Through contaminated objects<br />\r\nB) Through direct physical contact<br />\r\nC) Through animals and insects<br />\r\nD) Through small particles suspended in the air</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3378, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which mode of transmission involves transfer of microorganisms via an object?<br />\r\nA) Direct contact<br />\r\nB) Droplet transmission<br />\r\nC) Indirect contact<br />\r\nD) Airborne transmission</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3379, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a susceptible host lacking?<br />\r\nA) Immunity<br />\r\nB) Pathogenicity<br />\r\nC) Virulence<br />\r\nD) Resistance</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3380, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary method to control airborne transmission?<br />\r\nA) Hand hygiene<br />\r\nB) Quarantine<br />\r\nC) Ventilation systems<br />\r\nD) Vaccination</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3381, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can the chain of infection be effectively controlled?<br />\r\nA) By breaking one link in the chain<br />\r\nB) By vaccination only<br />\r\nC) By antibiotic treatment<br />\r\nD) By knowledge of specific diseases only</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3382, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Provision of essential drugs is an _________ of PHC<br />\r\nA) principle<br />\r\nB) Element<br />\r\nC) Goal<br />\r\nD) aims</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3383, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All are strategies of PHC except<br />\r\nA) provision of essential drugs<br />\r\nB )disease prevention<br />\r\nC) intrasectoral collaboration<br />\r\nD). Community participation</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3384, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All are benefits of Primary health care under one roof except<br />\r\nA) it enhances coordination<br />\r\nB) it eliminates constrains and fragmentation<br />\r\nC) it reduces wastages of resources<br />\r\nD) it dissociate the environment from the implementation of the proposed health act.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3385, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Medical sociology is linked to the following except<br />\r\nA) the sociological analysis of medical organizations and institutions<br />\r\nB) , the actions and interactions of healthcare professionals<br />\r\nC) the social or cultural effects of medical practice.<br />\r\nD) The reproduction of knowledge and selection of methods</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
