(3924, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the number whose logarithm to base 10 is 2.6025<br />\r\nA. 400.4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 0.4004</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 0.04004</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 0.004004</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3925, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Solve: 6(x - 4) + 3(x + 7) = 3<br />\r\nA. 3/2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2/3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1/2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1/3</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3926, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If 2x + y = 7 and 3x - 2y = 3, by how much is 7x greater than 10?<br />\r\nA. 1</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 10</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3927, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A cylinder of base radius 4cm is open at one end . If the ratio of the area of its base to that of its curved surface is 1:4, calculate the height of the cylinder<br />\r\nA. 8cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 4cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1cm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3928, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A headmaster contributes 7% of his income into a fund and his wife contributes 4% of her income. If the husband earns N5,500 per annum (p.a) and the wife earns N4,000 (P.a), find the sum of their annual contribution to the fund<br />\r\nA. N1045</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. N605</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. N545</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. N490</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3929, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A car is travelling at an average speed of 80km/hr. Its speed in meters per second (m/s) is<br />\r\nA. 13.3m/s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 22.2m/s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 133.3m/s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 222.2m/s</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3930, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mrs. Kofi sold an article for C7.50 instead of C12.75. Calculate her percentage of error, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 41.2%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 18.3%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 5.3%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1.7%</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3931, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a measure of dispersion?<br />\r\nA. Mode</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Mean deviation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Range</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. interquartile range</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3932, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If events X and Y are mutually exclusive,&nbsp;P(X) = 1/3 and P(Y) = 2/5, P(XnY) is<br />\r\nA. 0</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2/15</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 11/15</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 4/15</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3933, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A box contains 2 white and 3 blue identical marbles. If two marbles are picked at random, one after the other without replacement, what is the probability of picking two marbles of different colors?<br />\r\nA. 2/3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 3/5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 2/5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 7/20</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(3934, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following about a rhombus may not be true?<br />\r\nA. The diagonals are equal<br />\r\nB. The diagonals bisect the angles through which they pass<br />\r\nC. the diagonals bisect each other<br />\r\nD. The adjacent sides are equal</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3935, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">S = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}, T = {2,4,5,7} and R = {1,4, 5}. Find (SnT) U&nbsp;R<br />\r\nA. {1, 4, 5}</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. {2, 4, 5}</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. {1, 2, 4, 5}</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. {2, 3, 4, 5}</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3936, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Solve the inequality: 3m + 3 &gt; 9<br />\r\nA. m &gt; 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. m &gt; 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. m&gt;4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. m&gt;6</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3937, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The angle of a sector of a circle radius 10.5cm is 120&deg;. Find the perimeter of the sector [Take pie&nbsp;= 22/7]<br />\r\nA. 22cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 33.5cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 43cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 66cm</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3938, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Given that tan x = 5/12, what is the value of sin x + cos x ?<br />\r\nA. 5/13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7/13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 12/13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 17/13</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3939, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At a point 500m from the base of a water tank the angle of elevation of the top of the tank is 45&deg;. Find the height of the tank,<br />\r\nA. 250m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 353m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 500m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 433m</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3940, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the median of the following set of numbers: 28, 29, 39, 38, 33, 37, 26, 20, 15, 25<br />\r\nA. 33</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 29.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 29</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 28.5</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3941, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If the 2nd and 5th terms of a G.P are 6 and 48 respectively, find the sum of the first four for term<br />\r\nA. - 45</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 45</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 15</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 33</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3942, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a scalar quantity?<br />\r\nA. Momentum</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Acceleration</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Displacement</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Distance</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3943, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A barometer can be used in determining the</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">I. height of a mountain</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. depth of a mine</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III. dew point.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is/are correct?<br />\r\nA. I, II and III</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. II and III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. I and III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. I and II only</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3944, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following colours of surfaces will radiate heat energy best?<br />\r\nA. Red</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. White</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Black</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Yellow</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3945, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which of the following simple machines is the effort applied between the load and the fulcrum?<br />\r\nA. Scissors</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Pliers</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Wheel barrow</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Sugar tongs</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3946, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When two objects P and Q are supplied with the same quantity of heat,the temperature change in P is observed to be twice that in Q. If the masses of P and Q are the same,calculate the ratio of the specific heat capacities of P and Q<br />\r\nA. 1:2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 1:3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1:4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1:1</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3947, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The instrument used in the measurement of atmospheric pressure is?<br />\r\nA. Hydrometer</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Barometer</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Photometer</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Manometer</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3948, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A simple magnifying glass is used to view an object. At what distance from the lens must the object be placed so that an image 5 times the size of the object is produced 20cm from the lens?<br />\r\nA. 2cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 15cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 4cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 25cm</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3949, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An object is placed 36cm from a converging lens of focal length 24cm.If a real image which is 4cm high is formed, Calculate the height of the object.<br />\r\nA. 2.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.0cm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3950, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The electrical energy supplied by a Leclanche cell is obtained from the?_________<br />\r\nA. Nuclear energy</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Magnetic energy</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Solar energy</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Chemical energy</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3951, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a part of an A.C generator?<br />\r\nA. Carbon brushes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Slip rings</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Commutator</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Field magnet</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3952, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A car fuse is marked 15A and operates normally on a 12V battery. Calculate the resistance of the fuse wire<br />\r\nA. 0.8 ohm&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 27&nbsp;ohm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 3&nbsp;ohm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1.3 ohm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3953, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a stringed instrument?<br />\r\nA. Flute</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Trumpet</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Piano</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Organ</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3954, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transformer with 5500 turns in its primary is used between a 240V a. c supply and a 120V kettle. Calculate the number of turns in the secondary<br />\r\nA. 11000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2750</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 460</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 232</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3955, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following substances is not an insulator?<br />\r\nA. Clay</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Glass</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Plastic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Aluminium</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3956, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The nucleon number and the proton number of a neutral atom of an element are 238 and 92 respectively. What is the number of neutrons in the atom?<br />\r\nA. 330</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 238</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 146</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 119</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3957, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A student found out from a simple pendulum experiment that 20 oscillations were completed in 38 seconds. What is the period of oscillation of the pendulum?<br />\r\nA. 8.0s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 3.8 s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 2.0 s</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1.9 s</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3958, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The heating element in an electric kettle is usually located near the bottom of the kettle because<br />\r\nA. water is a good conductor of heat<br />\r\nB. heat can be more quickly radiated to all parts of the water<br />\r\nC. no heat can be lost to the surroundings<br />\r\nD. the convectional currents which are set up can carry heat to all parts of the water</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3959, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The saturated vapour pressure of a liquid increases as the___________<br />\r\nA. volume of the liquid increases</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. volume of the liquid decreases</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. temperature of the liquid increases</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. temperature of the liquid decreases</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3960, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Cloud formation is the direct result of ________<br />\r\nA. precipitation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. fusion</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. sublimation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. vaporization</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3961, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Water boils at a lower temperature when heated at the top of a mountain than at sea-level because at the top of the mountain the<br />\r\nA. saturation vapour pressure of water is higher than at sea-level</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. pressure of the atmosphere is lower</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. temperature is lower than at sea- level</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. relative humidity of the atmosphere is lower</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3962, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The metal extracted from cassiterite is__________<br />\r\nA. tin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. copper</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. calcium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. sodium</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3963, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The separation of a mixture of calcium trioxocarbonate (lV) and sodium trioxocarbonate (IV) is most easily carried out by using the differences in their_________<br />\r\nA. physical states</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. melting points</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Rf. Values</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. solubility</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3964, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Brass is an alloy of copper and __________<br />\r\nA. iron</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chromium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. zinc</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. tin</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3965, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following modes of motion is exhibited by the particles of a solid?<br />\r\nA. Vibrational and random motion</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Vibrational and translational motion</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Translational and random motion</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Vibrational motion only</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3966, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is not correct? Group 7 elements____________<br />\r\nA. are diatomic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. are good oxidizing agents</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. are highly electronegative</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. have relatively low ionization potentials</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3967, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When starch undergoes complete enzyme-catalyzed hydrolysis, the resulting product is<br />\r\nA. glucose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. maltose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. sucrose</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. fructose</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3968, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a direct petroleum product?<br />\r\nA. Methane</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Ethanol</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Petrol</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Vaseline</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3969, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Compounds that have the same molecular formula but different structures are said to be<br />\r\nA. allotropic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. polymorphic</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. polymeric</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. isomeric</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3970, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which of the following crystals are the particles held by van der Waal&#39;s forces only?<br />\r\nA. Sodium chloride</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Ice</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Diamond</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Iodine</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3971, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A current of 4.0 amperes was passed through copper (ll) tetraoxosulphate (IV) solution for one hour using copper electrodes. What was the mass of copper deposited? (Cu = 64, 1F = 96500 C)<br />\r\nA. 3.2g</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4.8g</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6.4g</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 48g</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3972, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When a crystal was added to its solution, it did not dissolve and the solution remained unchanged, showing that the solution was___________<br />\r\nA. concentrated</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. supersaturated</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. unsaturated</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. saturated</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3973, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">river contaminated by alkali waste will have a pH of about.<br />\r\nA. 1</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3974, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Hydrogen is used for the following except<br />\r\nA. manufacturing of ammonia</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. synthesis of hydrochloric acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. extinguishing fire</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. conversion of coal to petrol</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3975, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Methanol is obtained from wood by<br />\r\nA. esterification</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. bacterial decomposition</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. destructive distillation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. fractional distillation</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3976, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following acids are monobasic except_______<br />\r\nA. methanoic acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. dioxonitrate lll acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. ethanedioic acid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. oxochlorate (l) acid</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3977, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The reactions ethyne are mainly<br />\r\nA. substitution reactions</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. addition reactions</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. addition polymerization</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. catalytic hydrogenation</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3978, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the quantity of electricity produced when a current of 0.5A is passed for 5 hours 45 mins? (1F = 9650&deg;C)<br />\r\nA. 0. 11F</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 0.12F</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 0.22F</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 1.1F</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3979, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When iron rusts, it undergoes________<br />\r\nA. deliquescence</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chemical decomposition</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. hydrolysis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. redox reaction</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3980, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When sucrose is warmed with Fehling&#39;s solution<br />\r\nA. a silver mirror is produced</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. the solution turns milky</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. a brick-red precipitate is formed</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. there is no precipitate</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3981, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The energy required to remove the most loosely bound electron from an atom in the gaseous state is known as the___________<br />\r\nA. bond energy</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. ionization energy</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. potential energy</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. activation energy</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3982, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The organ which is sensitive to light in Euglena is the<br />\r\nA. gullet</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chloroplast</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. eye spot</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. contractile vacuole</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3983, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a similarity between a typical animal cell and a typical plant cell? presence of_______<br />\r\nA. cellulose cell wall</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chlorophyll</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. centrally-placed nucleus</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. cell membrane</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3984, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which of the following parts of a cell is the chromosome fund?<br />\r\nA. Nucleus</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Golgi body</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cytoplasm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Cell membrane</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3985, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following diseases is caused by deficiency of insulin in the body?<br />\r\nA. Malaria</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Diabetes mellitus</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Hepatitis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Gonorrhoea</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3986, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is the medium of transportation of nutrients with unicellular organisms?<br />\r\nA. Blood</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Serum</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Protoplasm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Plasma</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3987, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The respiratory organ found in the cockroach is the____________<br />\r\nA. air sac</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. trachea</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. lung book</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. lung</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3988, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Ultrafiltration in the kidney takes place in the _________<br />\r\nA. loop of Henle</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. renal vein</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Bowman&#39;s capsule</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. pelvic</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3989, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The groups of sensory cells found on the upper surface of the tongue are called<br />\r\nA. ampullae</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. taste buds</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. nerve cells</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. somatic cells</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3990, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a courtship behaviour exhibited by animals<br />\r\nA. Pairing</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Display</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Seasonal migration</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Hibernation</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3991, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes a marine habitat?<br />\r\nA. large body of water</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. which has no distinctive color or taste</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. with high concentration of salt</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. with little suspended materials</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3992, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following explains the term pyramid of numbers?<br />\r\nA. the number of organisms in a trophic level</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. progressive decrease in the number of individuals from lower to higher trophic level</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. the number of saprophytes and parasites in a habitat</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. the number of predators in a habitat</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3993, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not an adaptation of plants or animals to desert environment?<br />\r\nA. Well developed tap root system</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Broad leaves for storage</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Stems with spike-like leaves</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Metabolic waste in the form of uric acid in some animals</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3994, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a characteristic of overcrowding in plant and animal community?<br />\r\nA. Population outstripping available space</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Population exceeding available food</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Competition within the population</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. increase in primary production</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3995, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following substances cannot control the growth of harmful microoganisms?<br />\r\nA. isotonic sugar solution</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Hypertonic salt solution</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. disinfectants</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Antiseptics</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3996, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The largest game reserve in Nigeria is the ___________<br />\r\nA. Kainji Game Reserve in Niger State</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Zamfara Forest Reserve in Sokoto State</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Yankari Game Reserve in Bauchi State</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Borgu Game Reserve in Niger State</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3997, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The table below indicates the result of an experiment during which grains of different colours in two maize cobs were counted.<br />\r\nMaize Cob Colours of Maize Grains<br />\r\nWhite Pink Red<br />\r\nl. 30 60 30<br />\r\nII. 50 99 49<br />\r\nWhich of the following ratios agrees with the result?<br />\r\nA. 9:3:3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 1:2:1</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1:3:1</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2:1:1</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3998, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the major criticisms against Mendelian laws is that they do not recognise that _______<br />\r\nA. one trait is often controlled by many pairs of genes<br />\r\nB. single factor inheritance is never a reality<br />\r\nC. complete dominance is always possible<br />\r\nD. hybrids exist in living organisms</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(3999, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The offspring produced when pure strains interbreed is descried as<br />\r\nA. dominance</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. phenotype</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. hybrid</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. genotype</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(4000, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The division of labour in social insects is an example of___________<br />\r\nA. structural adaptation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. physiological adaptation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. behavioural adaptation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. commensalism</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(4001, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '100', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Lamarck&#39;s evolution theory could be summarised by the statement that__________<br />\r\nA. only the fittest can survive in a challenging environment<br />\r\nB. species that are unable to adapt become extinct<br />\r\nC. new characteristics do not arise in organisms in time of need<br />\r\nD. the changing environment imposes structural physiological and behavioural changes in organisms</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(4002, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech names a person, place, thing, or idea?<br />\na) Verb<br />\nb) Adjective<br />\nc) Noun<br />\nd) Adverb<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4003, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech describes a noun or pronoun?<br />\na) Verb<br />\nb) Adjective<br />\nc) Preposition<br />\nd) Conjunction<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4004, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech expresses action or being?<br />\na) Adverb<br />\nb) Preposition<br />\nc) Verb<br />\nd) Conjunction<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4005, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech modifies a verb, adjective, or another adverb?<br />\na) Pronoun<br />\nb) Adverb<br />\nc) Conjunction<br />\nd) Interjection<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4006, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech takes the place of a noun?<br />\na) Adverb<br />\nb) Adjective<br />\nc) Pronoun<br />\nd) Preposition<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4007, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech shows the relationship between a noun (or pronoun) and other words in a sentence?<br />\na) Verb<br />\nb) Conjunction<br />\nc) Interjection<br />\nd) Preposition<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4008, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech connects words, phrases, or clauses?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Adverb<br />\nc) Conjunction<br />\nd) Pronoun<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4009, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which part of speech expresses strong emotion?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Adjective<br />\nc) Interjection<br />\nd) Preposition<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4010, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Happily\" is an example of which part of speech?<br />\na) Verb<br />\nb) Adjective<br />\nc) Adverb<br />\nd) Conjunction<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4011, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Under\" in the sentence \"The cat is under the table\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Pronoun<br />\nc) Preposition<br />\nd) Adverb<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4012, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"She\" in the sentence \"She went to the store\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Pronoun<br />\nb) Adverb<br />\nc) Verb<br />\nd) Conjunction<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4013, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Quickly\" in the sentence \"She ran quickly\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Adverb<br />\nc) Adjective<br />\nd) Preposition<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4014, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"And\" in the sentence \"She bought apples and oranges\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Conjunction<br />\nc) Verb<br />\nd) Adverb<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4015, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Beautiful\" in the sentence \"She is beautiful\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Verb<br />\nc) Adjective<br />\nd) Conjunction<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4016, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Wow!\" in the sentence \"Wow! That\'s amazing\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Interjection<br />\nb) Verb<br />\nc) Adverb<br />\nd) Noun<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4017, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Teacher\" in the sentence \"The teacher is speaking\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Adjective<br />\nc) Pronoun<br />\nd) Adverb<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4018, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"But\" in the sentence \"I want to go, but I can\'t\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Adjective<br />\nb) Verb<br />\nc) Conjunction<br />\nd) Preposition<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4019, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Gently\" in the sentence \"He spoke gently\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Noun<br />\nb) Verb<br />\nc) Adverb<br />\nd) Pronoun<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4020, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"We\" in the sentence \"We are going to the park\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Pronoun<br />\nb) Noun<br />\nc) Adjective<br />\nd) Conjunction<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4021, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">\"Into\" in the sentence \"She walked into the room\" is which part of speech?<br />\na) Verb<br />\nb) Preposition<br />\nc) Adverb<br />\nd) Pronoun<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4022, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech compares two unlike things using \"like\" or \"as\"?<br />\na) Metaphor<br />\nb) Simile<br />\nc) Personification<br />\nd) Hyperbole<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4023, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech gives human qualities to non-human things?<br />\na) Metaphor<br />\nb) Simile<br />\nc) Personification<br />\nd) Irony<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4024, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech is an exaggerated statement not meant to be taken literally?<br />\na) Hyperbole<br />\nb) Understatement<br />\nc) Irony<br />\nd) Simile<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4025, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech involves a direct comparison without using \"like\" or \"as\"?<br />\na) Simile<br />\nb) Metaphor<br />\nc) Hyperbole<br />\nd) Alliteration<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4026, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech involves the repetition of the initial consonant sounds in words?<br />\na) Alliteration<br />\nb) Assonance<br />\nc) Onomatopoeia<br />\nd) Simile<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4027, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech imitates the natural sound of a thing?<br />\na) Metaphor<br />\nb) Onomatopoeia<br />\nc) Personification<br />\nd) Alliteration<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4028, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech places two opposite ideas together to create an effect?<br />\na) Metaphor<br />\nb) Simile<br />\nc) Oxymoron<br />\nd) Hyperbole<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4029, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech is a statement that appears contradictory but reveals a truth?<br />\na) Paradox<br />\nb) Irony<br />\nc) Simile<br />\nd) Alliteration<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4030, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech uses a part to represent the whole or vice versa?<br />\na) Metaphor<br />\nb) Synecdoche<br />\nc) Irony<br />\nd) Hyperbole<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
(4031, '2024/2025', 'Certificate for  Medical Laboratory Technicians(MLT)', '100', 'Second', 'USE OF ENGLISH II', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which figure of speech is a play on words that produces a humorous effect?<br />\na) Irony<br />\nb) Hyperbole<br />\nc) Pun<br />\nd) Alliteration<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 14:22:45', '2024-07-09 14:22:45'),
