(4293, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">According to the WHO, disability is:<br />\na) A health issue, to which medical solutions should be applied when possible.<br />\nb) A socially and environmentally defined issue, rather than a purely biological issue.<br />\nc) Neither purely biological nor social, but instead the interaction between health conditions and environmental and personal factors<br />\nd) usability is the interaction between health conditions and environmental and personal factors.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4294, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">According to the social and human rights model of disability, if a person in a wheelchair is unable to reach a ballot box and exercise the right to vote, it is because?<br />\na) The person?s physical abilities prevent her/him from accessing the ballot box.<br />\nb) Environmental barriers prevent them from reaching the ballot box.<br />\nc) That person does not have the right to vote.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4295, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Equity and inclusion for children with disabilities means equal?<br />\na) Opportunities<br />\nb) Treatment<br />\nc) Rights<br />\nd) Participation<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4296, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">According to the person-first terminology, which expression is appropriate?<br />\na) Child with disabilities<br />\nb) Disabled child<br />\nc) Child with a handicap<br />\nd) Handicapped Child<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4297, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When asking a person with disabilities a question, you should:<br />\na) Address the question to the person?s assistant<br />\nb) Ask someone for help<br />\nc) Speak to the person with disabilities directly<br />\nd) All the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4298, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Person with low vision means<br />\na) Legal blind with residual vision.<br />\nb) b. refractive error <br />\nc) impairment of visual functioning even after treatment or standard refractive correction <br />\nd) functional vision loss<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4299, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the requirement and needs of the disabled.<br />\na) Peer support<br />\nb) Housing <br />\nc) Transport <br />\nd) All the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4300, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is the peer important ?<br />\na) As disabled people experience barriers in society,<br />\nb) it is important that we are able to support each other and come together as a group of marginalized people to share information,<br />\nc) This enables both individual support<br />\nd) All the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4301, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Housing is the primary requirement for the disabled. True or false <br />\na) True <br />\nb) False <br />\nc) Non of the above <br />\nd) All the above <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4302, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the advantage of housing need for the disabled?<br />\na) live in society, and <br />\nb) be able to live an inclusive life as part of their local community. It is also important to note that as people become older,<br />\nc) they can often experience changes which limit their mobility, which causes their homes to become inaccessible to them.<br />\nd) All the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4303, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does equipment help  disabled people?<br />\na) Equipment, aids and adaptations can enable us to do things without assistance.<br />\nb) easy access to both home and work environments<br />\nc) Some of these adaptations also make everyday life much safer for disabled people.<br />\nd) D All the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4304, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">33. What are the means of transports includes for the disabled people ?<br />\na) buses,<br />\nb) trains,<br />\nc) taxis<br />\nd) All the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4305, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why does accessible transport desirable for the disabled?<br />\na) disabled people to be able to leave their homes and lead a full, inclusive life as part of their community, and society as a whole<br />\nb) Without accessible transport, disabled people become isolated, segregated and limited by society?s barrier<br />\nc) Participating in education, leisure activities, living an independent life (carrying out our own shopping,<br />\nd) All the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4306, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which among the following is not the problem of the disabled ?<br />\na) Transportation<br />\nb) Social Stigma <br />\nc) Day care center<br />\nd) Financial crisis<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4307, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following may cause partial or complete visual impairment ?<br />\nA. Glaucoma<br />\nB. Cataracts<br />\nC. Macular Degeneration<br />\nD. More than one of the above   <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4308, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">37. Cross disability advocacy aims to:<br />\nA. Promote the superiority of one disability over others<br />\nB. Advocate for the exclusion of certain disability types from public spaces.<br />\nC. Advocate for the inclusion, rights and accessibility of all individuals with disability<br />\nD. Discourage individuals with disability from seeking support and services<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4309, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which one is true?<br />\nA. In Autism Spectrum Disorder, children have a strong sensory issues.<br />\nB. In Autism Sensory Disorder, children have a strong sensory issues.<br />\nC. In Autism specific disorder, children have a strong sensory issues.<br />\nD. In Autism special disorder, children have a strong sensory issues.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4310, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">39. What are the common Intellectual and Developmental symptoms of down syndrome?<br />\nA. Decreased or poor muscle tone Short neck, with excess skin at the back of the neck Flattened facial profile and nose Small head, ears, and mouth <br />\nB. Short attention span Poor judgment Impulsive behaviour Slow learning Delayed language and speech development<br />\nC. Simple motor tics include: eye blinking, shoulder rotation or elevation, head jerking, Complex motor tics include: jumping, kicking Simple phonic tics include: grunting, clearing throat, Complex phonic tics include: complex and loud sounds, phrases out of context <br />\nD. Nausea, Headaches, Cranky and agitated Gains weight too quickly<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:16', '2024-07-09 17:05:16'),
(4311, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the causes of Hearing Impairment is: <br />\nA. Congenital Cause<br />\nB. Hereditary Cause<br />\nC. Physiological Cause<br />\nD. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4312, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">41. The primary characteristic of children with ?dyslexia? includes <br />\nA. attention deficit disorders<br />\nB. divergent thinking; fluency in reading<br />\nC. inability to read fluently<br />\nD. engaging in repetitive locomotor actions<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4313, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">42. Optimizing access to tools and assistive technologies will help in inclusion of:<br />\n(i) students with loss of vision<br />\n(ii) students with Attention Deficit Hyperactive Disorder<br />\n(iii) students with Cerebral Palsy <br />\n(iv) students with extraordinary talent <br />\nChoose the correct option. <br />\nA. (i)<br />\nB. (ii), (iii)<br />\nC. (i), (ii), (iii)<br />\nD. (i), (ii), (iii), (iv) <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4314, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">43. Which of the following is a physical scheduled disability among children?<br />\nI. Cerebral palsy<br />\nII. Muscular dystrophy<br />\nIII. Dwarfism<br />\nA. I and II <br />\nB. Only I <br />\nC. I, II and III <br />\nD. Only II<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4315, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">44. The term mental retardation is replaced with which term?<br />\nA. Intellectual disability<br />\nB. Mental weakness<br />\nC. Intellectual backwardness<br />\nD. Intellectual disadvantage<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4316, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">45. Which of the following practices promotes inclusion in the context of children with disabilities?<br />\ni. Barrier free access<br />\nii. Assistive devices and appropriate technology- based tools<br />\niii. Choice of regular or special schooling as well as home - based education<br />\niv. Uniform structured curriculum and means of assessment<br />\nA. (i), (ii), (iii)<br />\nB. (i), (ii), (iv)<br />\nC. (i), (iii), (iv)<br />\nD. (ii), (iii), (iv)<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4317, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">46. If the child repeatedly finds it difficult to tell the time from wall clock despite having proper sight and physique, it best demonstrates that the child is:<br />\nA. Dyslexic<br />\nB. Dull<br />\nC. Disgraphic<br />\nD. Dyspraxic<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4318, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">47. Identify the type of sensory disability:<br />\nA. Dwarfism<br />\nB. Autism S pectrum Disorder<br />\nC. Speech and language disability <br />\nD. Specific learning disability<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4319, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">48. DISHA is a scheme of early intervention for which specified Disabilities?<br />\nA. Autism<br />\nB. ADHD<br />\nC. Cerebral Palsy<br />\nD. MR<br />\nE. Multiple Disabilities<br />\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:<br />\nA. A, C, D Only<br />\nB. B, C, D, E and A  <br />\nC. A, C, D & E only  <br />\nD. A, B, C & D Only<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4320, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">49. The term ?special needs? refers to:<br />\na) Children who are exceptionally talented<br />\nb) Children with disabilities or learning difficulties<br />\nc) Children from low-income families<br />\nd) Children with behavioral challenges<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4321, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">50. The process of identifying children with special needs involves:<br />\na) Assessing their academic performance only<br />\nb) Assessing their physical appearance and characteristics<br />\nc) Assessing their overall development and learning abilities<br />\nd) Assessing their social popularity and peer interactions<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4322, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">51. Which of the following is an example of a developmental delay?<br />\na) Autism spectrum disorder (ASD)<br />\nb) Down syndrome<br />\nc) Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD)<br />\nd) Speech and language impairment<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4323, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">52. A child with a learning disability may exhibit difficulties in:<br />\na) Physical coordination and motor skills<br />\nb) Social interactions and communication<br />\nc) Attention and concentration<br />\nd) Reading, writing, or math skills<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4324, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">53. Characteristics of children with intellectual disabilities include:<br />\na) Advanced cognitive abilities and problem-solving skills<br />\nb) Age-appropriate language and communication skills<br />\nc) Significant limitations in intellectual functioning and adaptive behavior<br />\nd) High levels of attention and focus<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4325, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">54. Which of the following is a possible indicator of autism spectrum disorder (ASD)?<br />\na) Poor eyesight or hearing impairment<br />\nb) Difficulty with fine motor skills and coordination<br />\nc) Repetitive behaviors and restricted interests<br />\nd) Excessive talkativeness and social engagement<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4326, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">55. A child with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) may display:<br />\na) High levels of focus and attention to detail<br />\nb) Impulsivity and difficulty controlling impulses<br />\nc) Advanced language and communication skills<br />\nd) Highly organized and structured behavior<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4327, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">56. Children with speech and language impairments may have difficulty with:<br />\na) Physical coordination and motor skills<br />\nb) Reading and writing skills<br />\nc) Understanding and using language effectively<br />\nd) Social interactions and peer relationships<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4328, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">57. Children with visual impairments may require:<br />\na) Augmentative and alternative communication (AAC) systems<br />\nb) Adaptive seating and positioning devices<br />\nc) Assistive listening devices<br />\nd) Accessible learning materials and techniques<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4329, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">58. Which of the following is a possible indicator of a hearing impairment in a child?<br />\na) Difficulty with fine motor skills and coordination<br />\nb) Poor eyesight or visual impairments<br />\nc) Delayed language development or difficulty understanding speech<br />\nd) Hyperactivity and impulsivity<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4330, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">59. Children with physical disabilities may require:<br />\na) Adaptive seating and positioning devices<br />\nb) Assistive listening devices<br />\nc) Augmentative and alternative communication (AAC) systems<br />\nd) Social skills training programs<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4331, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">60. Characteristics of children with emotional and behavioral disorders include:<br />\na) High levels of social popularity and peer acceptance<br />\nb) Consistent and appropriate emotional regulation<br />\nc) Impaired social interactions and difficulty emotions<br />\nd) Advanced cognitive abilities and problem-solving skills<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
(4332, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CARE OF PEOPLE WITH SPECIAL NEEDS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 90, 90, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Children with dyslexia may experience difficulties in:<br />\na) Physical coordination and motor skills<br />\nb) Reading and spelling skills<br />\nc) Understanding and using language effectively<br />\nd) Attention and concentration<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 17:05:17', '2024-07-09 17:05:17'),
