(4471, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some benefits of integrating referral systems with outreach services?<br />\n    a) Increased healthcare costs for patients<br />\n    b) Improved coordination between providers<br />\n    c) Decreased access to specialized care<br />\n    d) Limited communication between healthcare professionals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4472, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one common problem affecting referral systems in healthcare?<br />\n    a) Lack of access to specialized care<br />\n    b) Excessive communication between healthcare providers<br />\n    c) Patients? reluctance to follow through with referrals<br />\n    d) Limited coordination between providers<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4473, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role does inadequate communication play in referral system problems?<br />\n    a) It facilitates smooth coordination between providers<br />\n    b) It ensures patients always follow through with referrals<br />\n    c) It can lead to delays or errors in the referral process<br />\n    d) It has no impact on the effectiveness of referrals<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4474, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does limited access to specialized care affect referral systems?<br />\n    a) It improves the efficiency of the referral process<br />\n    b) It decreases the need for referrals<br />\n    c) It can result in long wait times or unmet patient needs<br />\n    d) It ensures all patients receive timely care<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4475, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role does patient education play in addressing referral system problems?<br />\n    a) It exacerbates patient confusion about referrals<br />\n    b) It ensures patients always follow through with referrals<br />\n    c) It empowers patients to understand the importance of referrals and actively participate in their care<br />\n    d) It limits patients? access to specialized care<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4476, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a consequence of inadequate follow-up mechanisms in referral systems?<br />\n    a) Improved continuity of care<br />\n    b) Decreased patient satisfaction<br />\n    c) Timely access to specialized care<br />\n    d) Increased coordination between providers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4477, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role do healthcare disparities play in referral system problems?<br />\n    a) They have no impact on referral system effectiveness<br />\n    b) They can exacerbate challenges in accessing specialized care<br />\n    c) They ensure equal access to healthcare for all patients<br />\n    d) They decrease the need for referrals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4478, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does a lack of clear referral criteria contribute to referral system problems?<br />\n    a) It ensures that only appropriate patients are referred<br />\n    b) It can lead to inconsistent or inappropriate referrals<br />\n    c) It improves communication between healthcare providers<br />\n    d) It decreases the need for referrals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4479, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What impact can inadequate referral protocols have on patient care?<br />\n    a) They ensure timely access to specialized care<br />\n    b) They improve patient satisfaction with the referral process<br />\n    c) They can result in delays in diagnosis and treatment<br />\n    d) They decrease the likelihood of patient follow-through with referrals<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4480, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can limited provider networks affect referral system effectiveness?<br />\n    a) They ensure patients have access to a wide range of specialists<br />\n    b) They decrease the need for referrals<br />\n    c) They can result in long wait times or difficulty accessing specialists<br />\n    d) They improve communication between providers<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4481, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one strategy for addressing problems affecting referral systems?<br />\n    a) Increasing patient confusion about referrals<br />\n    b) Ignoring the need for patient education<br />\n    c) Implementing clear referral criteria and protocols<br />\n    d) Decreasing communication between healthcare providers<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4482, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role does inadequate coordination between healthcare providers play in referral system problems?<br />\n    a) It ensures smooth transitions for patients between providers<br />\n    b) It can lead to fragmented care and delays in treatment<br />\n    c) It improves patient satisfaction with the referral process<br />\n    d) It decreases the need for referrals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4483, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does limited patient awareness of available services impact referral system effectiveness?<br />\n    a) It ensures patients always follow through with referrals<br />\n    b) It can lead to missed opportunities for accessing appropriate care<br />\n    c) It decreases the likelihood of errors in the referral process<br />\n    d) It improves communication between healthcare providers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4484, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a consequence of inadequate feedback mechanisms in referral systems?<br />\n    a) Improved patient satisfaction with the referral process<br />\n    b) Decreased coordination between providers<br />\n    c) Difficulty in tracking patient outcomes and system performance<br />\n    d) Decreased need for referrals<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4485, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does language and cultural barriers affect referral system problems?<br />\n    a) They ensure effective communication between patients and providers<br />\n    b) They can lead to misunderstandings and decreased patient follow-through with referrals<br />\n    c) They decrease the need for referrals<br />\n    d) They improve patient access to specialized care<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4486, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What impact can financial constraints have on referral system effectiveness?<br />\n    a) They ensure equitable access to specialized care for all patients<br />\n    b) They decrease the need for referrals<br />\n    c) They can limit patients? ability to access recommended services<br />\n    d) They improve communication between healthcare providers<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4487, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does the lack of follow-up mechanisms contribute to referral system problems?<br />\n    a) It ensures patients always receive timely care<br />\n    b) It can lead to patients being lost to follow-up and unmet healthcare needs<br />\n    c) It improves communication between healthcare providers<br />\n    d) It decreases the need for referrals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4488, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a consequence of inadequate referral tracking systems?<br />\n    a) Improved coordination between providers<br />\n    b) Difficulty in monitoring patient progress and outcomes<br />\n    c) Increased patient satisfaction with the referral process<br />\n    d) Decreased need for referrals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4489, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does patient mistrust in the healthcare system affect referral system problems?<br />\n    a) It ensures patients always follow through with referrals<br />\n    b) It can lead to reluctance to seek care or follow through with recommendations<br />\n    c) It decreases the need for referrals<br />\n    d) It improves patient access to specialized care<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4490, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one strategy for addressing language and cultural barriers in referral systems?<br />\n    a) Ignoring the need for cultural competence training for healthcare providers<br />\n    b) Ensuring all patient communication is conducted in English<br />\n    c) Providing language interpretation services and culturally sensitive care<br />\n    d) Limiting access to specialized care for certain populations<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4491, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can inadequate provider networks impact referral system problems?<br />\n    a) They ensure patients have access to a wide range of specialists<br />\n    b) They decrease the need for referrals<br />\n    c) They can result in long wait times or difficulty accessing specialists<br />\n    d) They improve communication between providers<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4492, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are mobile health services?<br />\n   a) Services provided exclusively in hospitals<br />\n   b) Healthcare services delivered through mobile devices<br />\n   c) Services accessible only to individuals with smartphones<br />\n   d) Services provided by traditional healthcare providers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4493, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of a mobile health service?<br />\n   a) Traditional in-person doctor visits<br />\n   b) Telemedicine consultations via smartphone apps<br />\n   c) Healthcare services provided only through desktop computers<br />\n   d) Healthcare services exclusively delivered through postal mail<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4494, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary advantage of mobile health services?<br />\n   a) Limited access to healthcare for patients<br />\n   b) Increased convenience and accessibility of healthcare<br />\n   c) Higher cost of healthcare services<br />\n   d) Decreased use of technology in healthcare delivery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4495, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do mobile health services benefit underserved populations?<br />\n   a) By limiting access to healthcare services<br />\n   b) By increasing barriers to healthcare access<br />\n   c) By providing access to healthcare services in remote areas<br />\n   d) By excluding underserved populations from healthcare services<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4496, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common feature of mobile health apps?<br />\n   a) Limited functionality and usability<br />\n   b) Accessibility only to healthcare providers<br />\n   c) Remote monitoring of health parameters<br />\n   d) Requirement of physical presence in healthcare facilities<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4497, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role does telemedicine play in mobile health services?<br />\n   a) Telemedicine is not part of mobile health services<br />\n   b) Telemedicine allows for remote medical consultations and diagnosis<br />\n   c) Telemedicine can only be accessed through traditional healthcare settings<br />\n   d) Telemedicine is limited to in-person consultations<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4498, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do mobile health services contribute to preventive healthcare?<br />\n   a) By increasing barriers to accessing preventive care<br />\n   b) By limiting communication between patients and healthcare providers<br />\n   c) By providing access to health education and wellness resources<br />\n   d) By excluding preventive healthcare from their offerings<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4499, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a challenge associated with mobile health services?<br />\n   a) Increased access to healthcare for underserved populations<br />\n   b) Limited access to mobile devices and internet connectivity<br />\n   c) Decreased convenience and flexibility for patients<br />\n   d) Higher cost of healthcare services<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4500, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can mobile health services support chronic disease management?<br />\n   a) By limiting access to healthcare for individuals with chronic conditions<br />\n   b) By providing remote monitoring and management tools<br />\n   c) By requiring frequent in-person visits to healthcare facilities<br />\n   d) By excluding individuals with chronic conditions from their services<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4501, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of data privacy and security in mobile health services?<br />\n    a) Data privacy and security are not relevant to mobile health services<br />\n    b) Data privacy and security are critical to protecting patients? personal health information<br />\n    c) Data privacy and security are primarily the responsibility of patients<br />\n    d) Data privacy and security are not important considerations in healthcare delivery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4502, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one of the primary constraints faced by community health practitioners in implementing a referral system?<br />\n   a) Lack of training<br />\n   b) Excessive funding<br />\n   c) Overabundance of resources<br />\n   d) Minimal patient load<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4503, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common challenge for community health practitioners when referring patients to higher-level healthcare facilities?<br />\n   a) Excessive staffing<br />\n   b) Seamless communication<br />\n   c) Limited transportation options<br />\n   d) Abundant medical supplies<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4504, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What often hinders the effectiveness of a referral system for community health practitioners in rural areas?<br />\n   a) Adequate infrastructure<br />\n   b) High population density<br />\n   c) Geographic isolation<br />\n   d) Advanced medical technology<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4505, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which factor contributes to the difficulty of establishing trust between community health practitioners and higher-level healthcare providers?<br />\n   a) Transparent communication<br />\n   b) Mutual respect<br />\n   c) Cultural differences<br />\n   d) Shared resources<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4506, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a significant barrier to the timely transfer of patient information between community health practitioners and referral facilities?<br />\n   a) Secure digital platforms<br />\n   b) Efficient data management systems<br />\n   c) Language barriers<br />\n   d) Access to medical records<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4507, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factors often leads to delays in the referral process for community health practitioners?<br />\n   a) Streamlined administrative procedures<br />\n   b) Efficient coordination among healthcare facilities<br />\n   c) Limited availability of specialists<br />\n   d) Accessible healthcare facilities<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4508, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What frequently impedes the continuity of care for patients referred by community health practitioners?<br />\n   a) Comprehensive treatment plans<br />\n   b) Regular follow-up appointments<br />\n   c) Fragmented healthcare systems<br />\n   d) Integrated electronic health records<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4509, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which aspect of socioeconomic status commonly affects a patient?s ability to adhere to referrals made by community health practitioners?<br />\n   a) Higher education levels<br />\n   b) Lower income levels<br />\n   c) Access to private healthcare facilities<br />\n   d) Robust social support systems<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4510, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What often complicates the process of obtaining prior authorization for referrals from insurance providers?<br />\n   a) Clear communication channels<br />\n   b) Expedited approval processes<br />\n   c) Complex bureaucratic requirements<br />\n   d) Flexible coverage options<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4511, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which factor can contribute to the reluctance of patients to follow through with referrals from community health practitioners?<br />\n    a) Adequate health literacy<br />\n    b) Fear of stigmatization<br />\n    c) Strong social networks<br />\n    d) Trust in the healthcare system<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4512, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common challenge for community health practitioners when coordinating referrals for patients with multiple comorbidities?<br />\n    a) Limited access to specialized care<br />\n    b) Comprehensive electronic health records<br />\n    c) Robust interdisciplinary collaboration<br />\n    d) Adequate time for patient consultations<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4513, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factors can hinder the timely transfer of diagnostic test results between community health practitioners and referral facilities?<br />\n    a) Advanced telemedicine technology<br />\n    b) Efficient laboratory facilities<br />\n    c) Geographic proximity<br />\n    d) Logistical challenges<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4514, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What often prevents community health practitioners from receiving timely feedback on the outcomes of referred patients?<br />\n    a) Open communication channels<br />\n    b) Collaborative quality improvement initiatives<br />\n    c) Overlapping referral networks<br />\n    d) Limited feedback mechanisms<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4515, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common barrier to the implementation of standardized referral protocols among community health practitioners?<br />\n    a) Tailored patient care plans<br />\n    b) Flexibility in decision-making<br />\n    c) Inconsistent referral criteria<br />\n    d) Extensive clinical guidelines<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4516, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What frequently challenges the establishment of effective referral networks among community health practitioners and specialty care providers?<br />\n    a) Adequate financial incentives<br />\n    b) Mutual professional respect<br />\n    c) Competition for patients<br />\n    d) Shared patient-centered goals<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4517, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary objective of outreach services in healthcare?<br />\n   a) Maximizing profits<br />\n   b) Providing preventive care<br />\n   c) Expanding administrative tasks<br />\n   d) Limiting patient access<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4518, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following populations is often targeted by outreach services?<br />\n   a) Only individuals with high incomes<br />\n   b) Exclusively urban residents<br />\n   c) Rural and underserved communities<br />\n   d) Only those with private insurance<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4519, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common method used to deliver outreach services to remote areas?<br />\n   a) Only in-person visits<br />\n   b) Telemedicine and mobile clinics<br />\n   c) Only traditional mail services<br />\n   d) Utilizing social media platforms<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4520, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do outreach services contribute to reducing healthcare disparities?<br />\n   a) By limiting access to care<br />\n   b) By focusing only on urban areas<br />\n   c) By targeting specific demographic groups<br />\n   d) By providing care to underserved populations<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4521, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a benefit of outreach services for individuals with limited mobility?<br />\n   a) Increased isolation<br />\n   b) Improved access to healthcare<br />\n   c) Limited communication options<br />\n   d) Higher transportation costs<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4522, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a potential challenge faced by healthcare providers when conducting outreach services?<br />\n   a) Limited community engagement<br />\n   b) Excessive funding<br />\n   c) Abundant healthcare resources<br />\n   d) Strong patient advocacy<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4523, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do outreach services contribute to public health initiatives?<br />\n   a) By excluding marginalized populations<br />\n   b) By providing only curative services<br />\n   c) By promoting health education and prevention<br />\n   d) By focusing solely on individual treatment<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4524, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What often motivates healthcare organizations to invest in outreach services?<br />\n   a) Minimizing patient engagement<br />\n   b) Reducing preventive care<br />\n   c) Improving community health outcomes<br />\n   d) Ignoring underserved populations<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4525, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a potential barrier to the effectiveness of outreach services?<br />\n   a) Strong community partnerships<br />\n   b) Seamless communication channels<br />\n   c) Limited funding and resources<br />\n   d) Comprehensive healthcare coverage<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4526, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a key advantage of using technology in outreach services?<br />\n    a) Increased social isolation<br />\n    b) Limited access to healthcare information<br />\n    c) Enhanced reach and efficiency<br />\n    d) Excessive reliance on traditional methods<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4527, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a primary constraint faced by mobile health clinics?<br />\n   a) Limited access to medical supplies<br />\n   b) Lack of trained healthcare professionals<br />\n   c) Inadequate funding<br />\n   d) Poor communication infrastructure<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4528, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factors contributes to logistical constraints for mobile health clinics?<br />\n   a) Availability of parking spaces<br />\n   b) Distance to healthcare facilities<br />\n   c) Frequency of community events<br />\n   d) Availability of volunteer staff<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4529, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common technological constraint faced by mobile health clinics?<br />\n   a) Limited battery life of medical equipment<br />\n   b) Slow internet connection<br />\n   c) Inadequate storage space for patient records<br />\n   d) Lack of mobile health apps<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4530, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a regulatory constraint for mobile health clinics?<br />\n   a) Requirements for medical licensure<br />\n   b) Standards for vehicle maintenance<br />\n   c) Restrictions on operating hours<br />\n   d) Guidelines for patient confidentiality<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4531, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'REFERAL', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 80, 80, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a socio-cultural constraint faced by mobile health clinics?<br />\n   a) Language barriers<br />\n   b) Availability of public transportation<br />\n   c) Accessibility for people with disabilities<br />\n   d) Compliance with local dietary customs<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-09 19:51:52', '2024-07-09 19:51:52'),
(4532, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The definition of health according to the World Health Organization (WHO) connotes? <br />\nA)The absence of disease or infirmity.<br />\nB)Complete physical, mental, and social well-being.<br />\nC)The presence of positive mental factors.<br />\nD) Optimal functioning of physical domains only<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4533, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> Which of the following is NOT a direct factor influencing health?<br />\nA) Genetics<br />\nB) Lifestyle behaviors<br />\nC) Economic status<br />\nD) Individual beliefs<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4534, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What branch of mathematics involves collecting, analyzing, interpreting, presenting, and organizing data?<br />\nA) Algebra<br />\nB) Geometry<br />\nC) Statistics<br />\nD) Calculus<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4535, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which measure is NOT used to describe data in statistics?<br />\nA) Mean<br />\nB) Mode<br />\nC) Variance<br />\nD) Frequency<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4536, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of statistical inference?<br />\nA) To describe data<br />\nB) To make predictions about populations based on sample data<br />\nC) To validate research findings<br />\nD) To summarize data<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4537, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What do vital statistics NOT typically include?<br />\nA) Births<br />\nB) Employment rates<br />\nC) Deaths<br />\nD) Marriages<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4538, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">7. Which of the following is not a main vital event recorded in vital statistics?<br />\nA) Births<br />\nB) Marriages<br />\nC) Educational attainment<br />\nD) Fetal deaths<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4539, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following data is NOT routinely collected at healthcare institutions in Nigeria?<br />\nA) Patient demographic information<br />\nB) Medical history and clinical assessments<br />\nC) Household income data<br />\nD) Quality improvement data<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4540, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Nigeria National Cancer Registry (NNCR) collects data on:<br />\nA) Metastatictreatment.<br />\nb) Cancer incidence and mortality.<br />\nC) Malignancy treatment outcomes.<br />\nD) HIV/AIDS prevalence.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4541, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a use of vital statistics?<br />\nA) Monitoring population health<br />\nB) Providing individual health diagnoses<br />\nC) Supporting public health surveillance<br />\nD) Informing health policy<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4542, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Vital statistics help in identifying disparities in health outcomes among different population groups. This promotes:<br />\nA) Health equity<br />\nB) Economic growth<br />\nC) Political stability<br />\nD) Technological advancement<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4543, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which measure is used to describe the central tendency of data?<br />\nA) Variance<br />\nB) Standard deviation<br />\nC) Median<br />\nD) Correlation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4544, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">13. What is the main goal of health promotion and disease prevention efforts?<br />\nA) To cure existing diseases<br />\nB) To enhance individuals\' capacity to lead healthy lives<br />\nC) To provide free healthcare to all<br />\nD) To conduct epidemiological research<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4545, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What type of event is a stillbirth considered in vital statistics?<br />\nA) Birth<br />\nB) Death<br />\nC) Fetal death<br />\nD) Marriage<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4546, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which agency in Nigeria is responsible for implementing health insurance programs?<br />\nA) NPHCDA<br />\nB) NCDC<br />\nC) NHIA<br />\nD) NACA<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4547, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Federal Ministry of Health (FMOH) in Nigeria is responsible for:<br />\nA) Collecting demographic data<br />\nB) Regulating food and drugs<br />\nC) Formulating health policies<br />\nD) Conducting malaria surveys<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4548, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What type of health data is collected to assess hospital performance indicators?<br />\nA) Surgical procedures<br />\nb) Hospital admissions and discharges<br />\nC) Patient demographics<br />\nD) Infectious disease surveillance<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4549, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Vital statistics are crucial for epidemiological research because they:<br />\nA) Reduce healthcare costs.<br />\nb) Provide data for investigating disease determinants.<br />\nC) Promote economic growth.<br />\nD) Ensure patient confidentiality.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4550, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In health policy and planning, vital statistics help to:<br />\nA) Increase population density.<br />\nb) Inform strategic health decisions.<br />\nC) Provide entertainment.<br />\nD) Monitor weather patterns.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4551, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">20. Which of the following is an application of vital statistics in public health surveillance?<br />\nA) Enhancing cultural activities.<br />\nB) Detecting and responding to health emergencies.<br />\nC) Improving health workers  performance <br />\nD) Promoting fashion trends.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4552, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">21. What is the formula for calculating the Crude Birth Rate (CBR)?<br />\na). Number of live births/Total population X 1000<br />\nB). Total population/Number of live births X 1000<br />\nC). Number of deaths/Total populations X 1000<br />\nD). Total Population/number of deaths X 1000<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4553, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">22. The Crude Death Rate (CDR) is calculated using which of the following formulas?<br />\na). Number of deaths/Total populations X 1000<br />\nB). Number of deaths /Total populations X10000<br />\nC). Total population/Number of death X1000<br />\nD). Total population/Number of live births X 1000<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4554, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">23. Which of the following steps is NOT involved in calculating the Infant Morbidity Rate?<br />\nA) Determine the time period<br />\nb) Identify the number of neonatal deaths<br />\nC) Identify the number of infants with morbidity<br />\nD) Determine the total number of live births<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4555, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">To calculate the Infant Morbidity Rate (IMR), the number of infants with morbidity is multiplied by?<br />\nA) 10<br />\nB) 100<br />\nC) 1000<br />\nD) 10000<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4556, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes the Infant Mortality Rate (IMR)?<br />\nAa) Number of deaths of infants under one year per 1000 live births<br />\nB) Number of deaths of infants under five years per 1000 live births<br />\nC) Number of deaths of infants under one year per 10000 live births<br />\nD) Number of deaths of infants under five years per 10000 live births<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4557, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the formula for calculating the Maternal Mortality Ratio (MMR)?<br />\nA). Number of maternal deaths/Number of live births X 1000<br />\nB). Number of maternal deaths/Total population X100000<br />\nC). Number of maternal deaths/number of live births X 100000<br />\nD). Number of maternal deaths/number of live births X 10000<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4558, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Life expectancy is commonly calculated at which of the following life stages?<br />\nA) Adolescence<br />\nB) Birth<br />\nC) Middle age<br />\nD) Senior age<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4559, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT considered a common measure of rates in public health?<br />\nA) Birth rates<br />\nB) Death rates<br />\nC) Employment rates<br />\nD) Morbidity rates<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4560, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The attack rate is used specifically for measuring the frequency of new cases in what context?<br />\nA) Chronic diseases<br />\nB) Acute conditions<br />\nC) Outbreaks or epidemics<br />\nD) General population health<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4561, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In an outbreak, if 50 out of 200 people develop a disease, what is the attack rate?  <br />\nA) 20%<br />\nB) 25%<br />\nC) 30%<br />\nD) 40%<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4562, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which sampling method ensures every member of the population has an equal chance of being selected?<br />\nA) Convenience sampling<br />\nB) Simple random sampling<br />\nC) Snowball sampling<br />\nD) Purposive sampling<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4563, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Stratified sampling involves dividing the population into subgroups based on what?<br />\nA) Convenience<br />\nB) Specific characteristics<br />\nC) Random choice<br />\nD) Judgment<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4564, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Systematic sampling selects members of the population at what intervals?<br />\nA) Every 5th member<br />\nB) Every 10th member<br />\nC) Every nth member<br />\nD) Every 20th member<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4565, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In cluster sampling, the population is divided into what?<br />\nA) Subgroups<br />\nB) Clusters<br />\nC) Quotas<br />\nD) Layers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4566, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which non-probability sampling method involves selecting samples based on referrals from initial participants?<br />\nA) Convenience sampling<br />\nB) Purposive sampling<br />\nC) Snowball sampling<br />\nD) Quota sampling<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4567, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Quota sampling divides the population based on what criteria?<br />\nA) Accessibility<br />\nB) Specific characteristics<br />\nC) Random selection<br />\nD) Convenience<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4568, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT an advantage of using sampling in research?<br />\nA) Efficiency<br />\nB) Feasibility<br />\nC) Generalizability<br />\nD) Absolute accuracy<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4569, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary goal of probability sampling methods?<br />\nA) To ensure subjective selection<br />\nB) To guarantee convenience<br />\nC) To ensure every member has an equal chance of being selected<br />\nD) To select participants based on judgment<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4570, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Convenient sampling often results in which type of sample?<br />\nA) Unbiased<br />\nB) Representative<br />\nC) Random<br />\nDd) Biased<br />\n</p>', '', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4571, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Purposive sampling is also known as:<br />\nA) Random sampling<br />\nB) Judgmental sampling<br />\nC) Snowball sampling<br />\nD) Systematic sampling<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4572, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which rate measures the number of deaths in a population per 1,000 individuals?<br />\nA) Crude Birth Rate<br />\nB) Crude Death Rate<br />\nC) Infant Mortality Rate<br />\nD) Maternal Mortality Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4573, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of statistics in health research?<br />\nA) To present qualitative data.<br />\nB) To summarize and make inferences from data.<br />\nC) To increase sample data in statistics <br />\nD) To avoid data collection.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4574, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The formula for calculating the Infant Mortality Rate includes which denominator?<br />\nA) Total number of live births<br />\nB) Total number of deaths<br />\nC) Total population<br />\nD) Number of infant deaths<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4575, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the Maternal Mortality Ratio measure?<br />\nA) Number of maternal deaths per 1000 live births<br />\nB) Number of maternal deaths per 100000 live births<br />\nC) Number of maternal deaths per 10000 live births<br />\nD) Number of maternal deaths per 100 live births<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4576, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The attack rate is typically expressed as a:<br />\nA) Ratio<br />\nB) Percentage<br />\nC) Fraction<br />\nD) Whole number<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4577, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Sampling that uses a random process to select members from a population is known as?<br />\nA) Non-probability sampling<br />\nB) Convenience sampling<br />\nC) Probability sampling<br />\nD) Quota sampling<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4578, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Cluster sampling is best used when?<br />\nA) The population is homogenous<br />\nB) The population is scattered and diverse<br />\nC) The population size is small<br />\nD) The population is easily accessible<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4579, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In a study using snowball sampling, the initial participants are called?<br />\nA) Seeds<br />\nB) Nodes<br />\nC) Roots<br />\nD) Branches<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4580, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which sampling method is likely to be the most time-efficient?<br />\nA) Simple random sampling<br />\nB) Stratified sampling<br />\nC) Convenience sampling<br />\nD) Systematic sampling<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4581, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which method divides the population into subgroups and randomly samples within each subgroup?<br />\nA) Cluster sampling<br />\nB) Quota sampling<br />\nC) Stratified sampling<br />\nD) Simple random sampling<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4582, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary advantage of using stratified sampling over simple random sampling?<br />\nA) It is easier to implement.<br />\nB) It ensures a representative sample by including subgroups.<br />\nC) It is more cost-effective.<br />\nD) It requires fewer participants.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4583, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The systematic sampling method begins with which crucial step?<br />\nA) Dividing the population into strata.<br />\nB) Selecting a random starting point.<br />\nC) Grouping the population into clusters.<br />\nD) Choosing participants based on convenience.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4584, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of sampling technique is most likely to introduce bias into a study?<br />\nA) Simple random sampling<br />\nB) Stratified sampling<br />\nC) Systematic sampling<br />\nD) Convenience sampling<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4585, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In cluster sampling, what happens after selecting the random clusters?<br />\nA) Only a few members from each cluster are sampled.<br />\nB) All members within the selected clusters are included in the sample.<br />\nC) Clusters are further divided into subclusters.<br />\nD) A random sample is taken from each cluster.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4586, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a characteristic of non-probability sampling?<br />\nA) Each member has an unknown chance of being selected.<br />\nB) It allows for easy generalization to the population.<br />\nC) Selection is based on subjective criteria or convenience.<br />\nD) It minimizes selection bias.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4587, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Purposive sampling is often used in qualitative research for what purpose?<br />\nA) To ensure a random sample.<br />\nB) To select participants who meet specific criteria.<br />\nC) To minimize research costs.<br />\nD) To increase the sample size.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4588, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which measure is typically used to assess the impact of infectious diseases during an outbreak?<br />\nA) Incidence rate<br />\nB) Prevalence rate<br />\nC) Attack rate<br />\nD) Crude birth rate<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4589, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The calculation of the Crude Death Rate (CDR) involves which of the following elements?<br />\nA) Total number of live births<br />\nB) Total number of deaths<br />\nC) Number of deaths under one year of age<br />\nD) Number of maternal deaths<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4590, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What distinguishes cluster sampling from stratified sampling?<br />\nA) Cluster sampling divides the population into homogeneous subgroups.<br />\nB) Stratified sampling includes all members of the selected clusters.<br />\nC) In cluster sampling, entire clusters are randomly selected and all members included.<br />\nD) Stratified sampling uses every nth member after a random starting point.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4591, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which sampling technique involves selecting a sample that is easiest to access and recruit?<br />\nA) Snowball sampling<br />\nB) Purposive sampling<br />\nC) Convenient sampling<br />\nD) Quota sampling<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4592, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is the Crude Birth Rate (CBR) typically expressed?<br />\nA) Per 100 population<br />\nB) Per 1000 population<br />\nC) Per 10,000 population<br />\nD) Per 100,000 population<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4593, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes life expectancy?<br />\nA) The number of years a newborn is expected to live based on current mortality rates.<br />\nB) The average age at which people die in a population.<br />\nC) The median age of death in a given population.<br />\nD) The number of years a person is expected to live past retirement age<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4594, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A maternal mortality ratio of 150 means:<br />\nA) 150 maternal deaths per 1,000 live births.<br />\nB) 150 maternal deaths per 100,000 live births.<br />\nC) 150 maternal deaths per 10,000 live births.<br />\nD) 150 maternal deaths per 1,000,000 live births.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4595, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a key step in calculating the Infant Morbidity Rate?<br />\nA) Determine the time period.<br />\nB) Identify the number of infant deaths.<br />\nC) Identify the number of infants with morbidity.<br />\nD) Determine the total number of live births.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4596, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In research, why is sampling often preferred over studying an entire population?<br />\nA) It is always more accurate.<br />\nB) It eliminates the need for data analysis.<br />\nC) It is more efficient and feasible.<br />\nD) It guarantees a representative sample.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4597, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The attack rate during an outbreak is useful for which of the following purposes?<br />\nA) Measuring the lifetime prevalence of a disease.<br />\nB) Determining the chronic disease burden.<br />\nC) Assessing the spread and impact of an infectious disease.<br />\nD) Calculating annual mortality rates.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4598, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one major limitation of convenience sampling?<br />\nA) It is too time-consuming.<br />\nB) It requires extensive statistical analysis.<br />\nC) It often leads to biased samples.<br />\nD) It ensures a representative sample.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4599, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which sampling method involves initial participants referring other potential participants?<br />\nA) Purposive sampling<br />\nB) Snowball sampling<br />\nC) Quota sampling<br />\nD) Cluster sampling<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4600, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When calculating the Infant Mortality Rate, which population is considered in the denominator?<br />\nA) Total population<br />\nB) Number of infants born that year<br />\nC) Number of infants under one year<br />\nD) Number of live births<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4601, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following describes the concept of generalizability in sampling?<br />\nA) The ability to apply findings from a sample to the entire population.<br />\nB) The ease of collecting data from the sample.<br />\nC) The precision of measurements within the sample.<br />\nD) The variability of sample characteristics.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4602, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A study that uses systematic sampling must first determine:<br />\nA) The size of the strata.<br />\nB) The total population size.<br />\nC) A random starting point.<br />\nD) The specific subgroups of interest.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4603, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which measure reflects the frequency of new cases in a population over a specified time period?<br />\nA) Prevalence rate<br />\nB) Incidence rate<br />\nC) Mortality rate<br />\nD) Life expectancy<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4604, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When using cluster sampling, why might researchers choose this method?<br />\nA) To increase the precision of the sample estimates.<br />\nB) To reduce travel and logistical costs.<br />\nC) To ensure a completely random selection process.<br />\nD) To guarantee equal representation of all subgroups.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4605, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The primary goal of non-probability sampling methods is to:<br />\nA) Ensure equal probability of selection.<br />\nB) Maximize sample diversity.<br />\nC) Select samples based on ease and specific criteria.<br />\nD) Minimize sampling bias.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4606, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In public health, which rate would be most useful for understanding the spread of an acute infectious disease?<br />\nA) Crude birth rate<br />\nB) Infant mortality rate<br />\nC) Attack rate<br />\nD) Maternal mortality ratio<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4607, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What distinguishes a rate from a ratio in public health statistics?<br />\nA) Rates measure static quantities, while ratios measure dynamic quantities.<br />\nB) Rates measure the occurrence of events over time, while ratios compare two quantities.<br />\nC) Rates are always expressed as percentages, while ratios are not.<br />\nD) Rates and ratios are interchangeable terms in public health.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4608, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of an independent variable?<br />\nA) Temperature<br />\nB) Height<br />\nC) Time<br />\nD) Treatment group in an experiment<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4609, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What type of variable is manipulated by the researcher?<br />\nA) Dependent variable<br />\nB) Continuous variable<br />\nC) Independent variable<br />\nD) Discrete variable<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4610, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of variable represents different categories with no inherent order?<br />\nA) Ordinal variable<br />\nB) Nominal variable<br />\nC) Continuous variable<br />\nD) Ratio variable<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4611, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Socioeconomic status (low, middle, high) is an example of a?<br />\nA) Nominal variable<br />\nB) Interval variable<br />\nC) Ratio variable<br />\nD) Ordinal variable<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4612, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which variable is expected to change as a result of manipulations to the independent variable?<br />\nA) Dependent variable<br />\nB) Control variable<br />\nC) Nominal variable<br />\nD) Continuous variable<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4613, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What type of variable has equal intervals between values but no true zero point?<br />\nA) Ratio variable<br />\nB) Nominal variable<br />\nC) Interval variable<br />\nD) Ordinal variable<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4614, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Temperature measured in Celsius is an example of which level of measurement?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4615, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of variable can be counted but not measured with precision?<br />\nA) Continuous variable<br />\nB) Discrete variable<br />\nC) Interval variable<br />\nD) Ratio variable<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4616, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which level of measurement involves categorical data without a natural order?<br />\nA) Interval<br />\nB) Nominal<br />\nC) Ordinal<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4617, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Educational attainment (e.g., high school diploma, bachelor\'s degree) is classified as which level of measurement?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4618, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What distinguishes ratio variables from interval variables?<br />\nA) Ratio variables have a true zero point.<br />\nB) Interval variables have a true zero point.<br />\nC) Ratio variables do not have equal intervals.<br />\nD) Interval variables represent categorical data.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4619, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Gender (male, female) is an example of which level of measurement?<br />\nA) Interval<br />\nB) Ratio<br />\nC) Ordinal<br />\nD) Nominal<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4620, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which level of measurement allows for the calculation of meaningful ratios?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4621, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">IQ scores (Genius, Brilliant, low level intelligence ) fall under which level of measurement?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4622, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At the ordinal level of measurement, which of the following is true?<br />\nA) Categories have a natural order.<br />\nB) Intervals between categories are equal.<br />\nC) Mathematical operations are meaningful.<br />\nD) There is a true zero point.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4623, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which level of measurement involves equal intervals but lacks a true zero point?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4624, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Height is an example of a variable measured at which level?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4625, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Calendar dates are classified under which level of measurement?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4626, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the four variables that are present in a typical research topic <br />\nA) Independent, Dependent, Target population, Moderating variable <br />\nB) Independent, Interveining, Moderating and Outcome variable <br />\nC) Independent, Dependent, Target population, Location <br />\nD) Independent, Dependent, Target population, extraneous variable <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4627, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of variable represents quantities with a true zero point, allowing for meaningful ratios?<br />\nA) Nominal variable<br />\nB) Ordinal variable<br />\nC) Interval variable<br />\nD) Ratio variable<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4628, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A researcher is studying the effect of a new teaching method on student performance. What would the student performance be classified as in this study?<br />\nA) Independent variable<br />\nB) Dependent variable<br />\nC) Continuous variable<br />\nD) Nominal variable<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4629, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which level of measurement includes variables that can be categorized and ranked, but where the intervals between ranks are not equal?<br />\nA) Nominal<br />\nB) Ordinal<br />\nC) Interval<br />\nD) Ratio<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4630, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When a dataset has an outlier(extreme number), which measure of central tendency is most likely to remain unaffected?<br />\nA) Mean<br />\nB) Median<br />\nC) Mode<br />\nD) Standard deviation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4631, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HEALTH STATISTICS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Percentages are mainly used in?<br />\nA). Formation of data <br />\nB). Tabulation of data<br />\nC). Cancelling of data <br />\nD). Removing of data <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:34:29', '2024-07-10 15:34:29'),
(4632, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does HIV stand for?<br />\na. Human Impaired Virus<br />\nb. Human Immunodeficiency Virus<br />\nc. Human Inflammatory Virus<br />\nd. Human Influenza Virus<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4633, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of CD4 cells in the body?<br />\na. Digestion<br />\nb. Fighting off infections and diseases<br />\nc. Blood circulation<br />\nd. Vision<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4634, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following best describe AIDS?<br />\na. An advanced stage of HIV infection<br />\nb. An early stage of HIV infection<br />\nc. A virus that attacks CD4 cells<br />\nd. A type of cancer<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4635, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All but One is not a common signs and symptoms of HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. Muscle pain<br />\nb. Nausea<br />\nc. Rash<br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4636, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What percentage of HIV/AIDS transmissions occurs through sexual intercourse?<br />\na. 50%<br />\nb. 70%<br />\nc. 80%<br />\nd. 100%<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4637, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common mode of transmission of HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. Sharing of clipper, razor blade<br />\nb. Scarification (Tattoos)<br />\nc. Pregnancy, delivery and breast feeding<br />\nd. Sexual intercourse<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4638, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is not a factor that predispose the transmission of HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. Infectiousness of host and high sexual activities<br />\nb. Use of infected sharp object and exposure to blood<br />\nc. Presence of semen & genital secretions and breastfeeding of HIV positive mother<br />\nd. Careful use of sharps<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4639, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Who are the vulnerable groups to HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. Young adult<br />\nb. Commercial sex worker, MSM, gay, serial monogamy, Polygamy<br />\nc. Individuals with multiple sexual partners<br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4640, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not animpacts of HIV/AIDS on health?<br />\na. Increase morbidity and mortality<br />\nb. Weakness, sicknesses of varying degree and death<br />\nc. Opportunistic infections<br />\nd. Non-deteriorating health and wellbeing<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4641, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most severe stage of HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. Stage I: Asymptomatic, generalized lymphadenopathy<br />\nb. Stage II: Weight loss <10%, prurigo, fungal nail infection, herpes zoster, recurrent URTIs<br />\nc. Stage III: Weight loss > 10%, chronic diarrhea or fever, oral candidiasis/hairy leukoplakia, pulmonary TB, severe bacterial infections<br />\nd. Stage IV: AIDS-defining illnesses<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4642, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the source of HIV infection in humans?<br />\na. Monkeys<br />\nb. Dogs<br />\nc. Cats<br />\nd. Apes<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4643, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the period of initial infection and manifestation of AIDS?<br />\na. 1-12months<br />\nb. 1-10years<br />\nc. 5-10years<br />\nd. 6-12 months<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4644, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many types of HIV cause HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. One type<br />\nb. Two types<br />\nc. Three types<br />\nd. Four types<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4645, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The stages of HIV life cycle is divided into how many part? <br />\na. 5 stages <br />\nb. 8 stages <br />\nc. 4 stages <br />\nd. 12 stages <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4646, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main target of HIV in the body? <br />\na. T-cells <br />\nb. B-cells <br />\nc. Natural Killer cells <br />\nd. Red blood cells <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4647, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term given to the period between acquiring HIV and development of detectable antibodies called? <br />\na. Incubation period <br />\nb. Burden period <br />\nc. Window period <br />\nd. Acute period <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4648, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All but one are factors that affect HIV disease progression? <br />\na. Age, Gender and Genetics <br />\nb. Co-infections, Access to health care and Lifestyle factors <br />\nc. Viral load, Immune response and Time of infection <br />\nd. Body weight, and high CD4 count<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4649, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the process of testing and analyzing samples from individuals suspected of having HIV infection called? <br />\na. HIV diagnosis <br />\nb. Antibody detection assay <br />\nc. Viral load test <br />\nd. HIV laboratory investigation <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4650, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is a method to detect antibodies to the virus HIV? <br />\na. Viral load test<br />\nb. Rapid test <br />\nc. Saliva test <br />\nd. Urine test <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4651, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the goal of HIV/AIDS counseling and testing? <br />\na. To provide psychosocial support <br />\nb. To prevent HIV infection and its transmission to others <br />\nc. To provide medical treatment <br />\nd. To determine the exact type of HIV strain <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4652, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the difference between advising and counseling? <br />\na. Advising is more effective than counseling <br />\nb. Counseling focuses on making informed decisions <br />\nc. Advising is giving instructions <br />\nd. Counseling involves open discussion about death <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4653, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the unique feature of HIV counseling that makes it different from other types of counseling? <br />\na. It involves open discussion about sexual matters <br />\nb. It provides medical treatment <br />\nc. It requires paying attention to psychological reactions of clients <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4654, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a benefit of HIV counseling and testing? <br />\na. It helps clients explore their feelings and thoughts <br />\nb. It enables clients to take negative action <br />\nc. It helps the health worker to gain more control over the clients<br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4655, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the key elements in counseling? <br />\na. Accessibility <br />\nb. Consistency and accuracy <br />\nc. Trust and confidentiality <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4656, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is post-test counseling? <br />\na. Counseling provided before an HIV test <br />\nb. Counseling provided after an HIV test result is released <br />\nc. Counseling provided during the maturation stage of HIV <br />\nd. Counseling provided during the integration stage of HIV <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4657, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is ongoing counseling? <br />\na. Counseling provided only once <br />\nb. Counseling provided periodically <br />\nc. Counseling provided before an HIV test <br />\nd. Counseling provided after an HIV test result is released <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4658, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the difference between pre-test and post-test counseling? <br />\na. Pre-test is counseling provided before an HIV test, while post-test is counseling provided after the test result is released. <br />\nb. Post-test is counseling provided before an HIV test, while pre-test is counseling provided after the test result is released. <br />\nc. Pre-test is counseling provided during the acute phase of HIV, while post-test is counseling provided during the maturation stage of HIV. <br />\nd. Pre-test is counseling provided to prevent transmission of HIV, while post-test is counseling provided to deal with the death of a loved one. <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4659, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the rapid test? <br />\na. A test that produces results in 5-15 minutes <br />\nb. A test that does not requires a blood sample <br />\nc. A test that requires a spinal fluid sample <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4660, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the non-reactive test result mean? <br />\na. Antibodies detected <br />\nb. HIV negative <br />\nc. Exposed with detectable antibody <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4661, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main goal of HIV/AIDS counseling? <br />\na. To provide medical treatment <br />\nb. To prevent the spread of HIV <br />\nc. To cure HIV <br />\nd. To provide financial assistance to individuals with HIV<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4662, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the attributes of a good counsellor?<br />\na. Good listener, confidant, judgemental, dishonest<br />\nb. Good listener, confidant, able to relate well with people, trustworthy<br />\nc. Good listener, confidant, unapproachable, judgemental<br />\nd. Good listener, confidant, reluctant, disrespectful<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4663, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are concordant couples in HIV and AIDS management?<br />\na. Concordant couples are couples where one is negative and the other has invalid result.<br />\nb. Concordant couples are couples where one partner is HIV negative and the other is HIV positive.<br />\nc. Concordant couples are couples where both partners are HIV positive.<br />\nd. Concordant couples are couples that one has Syphilis and the other is HIV positive.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4664, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the goals of ARV therapy?<br />\na. To kill the virus completely<br />\nb. To reduce viral load, prevent opportunistic infections and boost immune system<br />\nc. To cause side effects on the patient<br />\nd. To prevent HIV transmission from mother to child.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4665, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is adherence in HIV prevention and treatment?<br />\na. The resistance of HIV to ARV drugs<br />\nb. The faithfulness of a person to participate in HIV prevention, care, and treatment<br />\nc. The duration someone is on ARV drugs<br />\nd. The capacity of a person to spread HIV.<br />\n<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4666, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is adherence important in HIV care and treatment?<br />\na. It determines the success of HIV care and treatment programs<br />\nb. It causes drug resistance resulting in increased morbidity and mortality and further infections<br />\nc. It makes people to be prone to the spread of HIV<br />\nd. It increases the number of pills in a person\'s regimen.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4667, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What factors enhance adherence to HIV prevention and treatment plan?<br />\na. Travel and migration<br />\nb. Mental illness, like depression<br />\nc. Acceptance of HIV status, ability to disclose<br />\nd. Poor referral systems<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4668, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one strategy for improving adherence from a patient\'s point of view?<br />\na. Taking medicines to prevent opportunistic infections<br />\nb. Picking up medications when scheduled and before running out<br />\nc. Being judgmental and confrontational with the multidisciplinary care team<br />\nd. Avoiding attending appointments and tests.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4669, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT an attribute of a good counsellor?<br />\na. Not judgemental<br />\nb. Trustworthy<br />\nc. Dishonest<br />\nd. Able to respect client<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4670, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the two types of couples in HIV and AIDS management?<br />\na. Positive couples and negative couples<br />\nb. Discordant couples and concordant couples<br />\nc. Infected couples and non-infected couples<br />\nd. Complicated couples and simple couples<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4671, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are clinical environment factors associated with poor adherence to HIV prevention and treatment plan?<br />\na. Acceptance of HIV status, ability to disclose<br />\nb. Provider language<br />\nc. Shared decision-making process between client and health care providers<br />\nd. Distance to clinic and transportation costs<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4672, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a strategy for improving adherence from a service point of view?<br />\na. Good linkages between different services<br />\nb. Reduce waiting times for the clinic<br />\nc. Distance to the clinic and transportation costs<br />\nd. Lack of referral systems<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4673, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of cultural/religious in effective HIV and AIDS counselling and testing?<br />\na. It improves the effectiveness of counselling and testing<br />\nb. It creates language barriers<br />\nc. It causes gender discrimination<br />\nd. It inhibits counselling and testing<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4674, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are opportunistic infections? <br />\na. Infections that occur in individuals with stronger immune systems <br />\nb. Infections that occur in individuals with weakened immune systems <br />\nc. Infections that occur due to poor hygiene <br />\nd. Infections that occur after vaccination <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4675, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some examples of OIs commonly associated with HIV? <br />\na. Malaria and typhoid fever <br />\nb. Pneumonia and tuberculosis <br />\nc. Measles and chickenpox <br />\nd. Influenza and common cold <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4676, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some factors that can make PLHAs to be susceptible to OIs? <br />\na. A strong immune system and balanced nutrition <br />\nb. Physical exercise and regular sleep patterns <br />\nc. Psychological stress and depletion of nutritional status <br />\nd. Avoiding contact with animals and avoiding public places <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4677, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many grading of adverse drug reactions by WHO? <br />\na. 5<br />\nb. 3<br />\nc. 4<br />\nd. 2<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4678, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first lineof recommended prophylaxis for pneumocystis pneumonia? <br />\na. Cotrimoxazole <br />\nb. Fluconazole <br />\nc. Isoniazid Preventive Treatment <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4679, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some general prevention measures for HIV/AIDS? <br />\na. Not sharing sharps<br />\nb. Using barrier methods during sexual activity <br />\nc. Abstinence<br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4680, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is universal precaution? <br />\na. A set of standardized precautions designed to prevent the transmission ofHIV, HBV, bloodborne pathogens,and other micro-organisms <br />\nb. A set of precautions designed to prevent airborne pathogens <br />\nc. A set of precautions designed to prevent foodborne pathogens <br />\nd. A set of precautions designed to prevent waterborne pathogens <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4681, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most important practice for reducing the transmission of microorganisms? <br />\na. Use of protective barriers <br />\nb. Isolating and discriminating patients<br />\nc. Immunization <br />\nd. Use of prophylaxis<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4682, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is surveillance in the context of infection control? <br />\na. The purpose of immunization <br />\nb. The practice of reducing unnecessary procedures <br />\nc. Detecting infections, planning control/protocol improvement activities, and reporting outbreaks <br />\nd. The practice of disposing of soiled bandages and dressings<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4683, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of community organizations in the care and support of HIV and AIDS clients? <br />\na. Providing medical care and medicines including social support<br />\nb. Providing spiritual counseling only<br />\nc. Providing food, housing, and clothing only<br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4684, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some examples of viral infections commonly associated with HIV? <br />\na. Cytomegalovirus and tuberculosis<br />\nb. Candidiasis and pneumonia <br />\nc. Hepatitis and herpes simplex <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4685, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of prophylaxis for OIs? <br />\na. To prevent HIV infection <br />\nb. To prevent the spread of OIs <br />\nc. To improve immune system function <br />\nd. To prevent OIs in individuals with weakened immune systems<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4686, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some examples of OI prophylaxis regimens? <br />\na. Cotrimoxazole and fluconazole <br />\nb. Isoniazid Preventive Treatment for TB <br />\nc. Both A and B <br />\nd. None of the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4687, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can healthcare workers reduce transmission of microorganisms? <br />\na. Regular hand-washing <br />\nb. Use of protective barriers <br />\nc. Avoiding unnecessary procedures <br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4688, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the effect of HIV on the body\'s ability to absorb nutrients?<br />\na. increases nutrient absorption<br />\nb. decreases nutrient absorption<br />\nc. doesn\'t affect nutrient absorption<br />\nd. unknown<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4689, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What factors contribute to HIV-associated weight loss?<br />\na. overeating and lack of exercise<br />\nb. loss of muscle tissues and body fat, and mineral and vitamin deficiencies<br />\nc. excessive nutrient absorption<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4690, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does good nutrition benefit people living with HIV?<br />\na. helps prevent malnutrition and wasting<br />\nb. fights opportunistic infections<br />\nc. improves medication effectiveness<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4691, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should nutritional assessment, counseling and support begin for people living with HIV?<br />\na. during the late phase of HIV infection<br />\nb. early in the course of HIV infection<br />\nc. only when experiencing symptoms<br />\nd. not necessary for overall health<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4692, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a recommended diet for people with HIV?<br />\na. low calorie/low protein diet<br />\nb. high calorie/high protein diet<br />\nc. high fat/low protein diet<br />\nd. low carbohydrate/low protein diet<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4693, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do you prevent HIV transmission to vulnerable children?<br />\na. promoting HIV education and awareness<br />\nb. ensuring access to HIV testing and counseling<br />\nc. promoting safe sexual practices<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4694, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some recommended measures for EMTCT?<br />\na. antiretroviral therapy (ART) for pregnant women<br />\nb. promoting safe sex practices<br />\nc. offering pre-conception counseling and testing<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4695, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not an ethical principle for HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. confidentiality, informed consent, maleficence, justice<br />\nb. autonomy, informed consent, confidentiality, beneficence, non-maleficence, judgemental.<br />\nc. autonomy, confidentiality, benevolence, non-maleficence, justice<br />\nd. autonomy, informed consent, beneficence, non-maleficence<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4696, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a referral network in healthcare?<br />\na. a group of patients who refer others to healthcare providers<br />\nb. a group of healthcare providers who reject patients<br />\nc. a group of professional colleagues who transfer clients to another health facility for care<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4697, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the steps in implementing and strengthening a referral network?<br />\na. identifying key stakeholders, establishing communication channels, developing referral protocols, training healthcare providers, and monitoring and evaluating<br />\nb. identifying key patients, establishing communication channels, developing patient protocols, training healthcare providers, and monitoring and evaluating<br />\nc. identifying key healthcare providers, establishing communication channels, developing provider protocols, training clients, and monitoring and evaluating<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4698, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of monitoring and evaluation (M&E) in healthcare?<br />\na. to measure progress towards achieving specific goals and objectives<br />\nb. to ensure privacy and confidentiality<br />\nc. to monitor the use of funds by healthcare providers<br />\nd. to identify key stakeholders<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4699, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What practices ensure data quality assurance for HIV/AIDS monitoring and evaluation?<br />\na. standardized data collection tools and protocols<br />\nb. training and capacity building<br />\nc. data validation and verification<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4700, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factorshinders successful referral networks?<br />\na. lack of funds from the patient\'s end<br />\nb. good communication network<br />\nc. willingness of patients/relatives to leave a secure environment<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4701, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the benefits of shared decision-making in healthcare?<br />\na. ensures privacy and confidentiality<br />\nb. improves patient outcomes<br />\nc. reduces healthcare costs<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4702, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which is not one of the reasons for referral in healthcare?<br />\na. lack of experts to manage such a case<br />\nb. patient\'s persistent request for referral<br />\nc. high healthcare provider\'s management skills<br />\nd. condition not spelled out in the standing order<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4703, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the types of referral pathways?<br />\na. normal referral and emergency referral<br />\nb. basic referral and advanced referral<br />\nc. outpatient referral and inpatient referral<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4704, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is a common health issues affecting nutritional intake by people living with HIV?<br />\na. diarrhea and vomiting<br />\nb. weight gain and muscle mass gain<br />\nc. lactose intolerance<br />\nd. high nutrient absorption<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4705, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does HIV contribute to weight loss and loss of muscle tissues and body fat?<br />\na. by changing body metabolism<br />\nb. through opportunistic infections/illness (TB)<br />\nc. by causing HIV-associated wasting syndrome<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4706, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the benefits of good nutrition for people living with HIV?<br />\na. prolongs good health<br />\nb. improves quality of life<br />\nc. prevent HIV progression to AIDS<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4707, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should a healthcare provider decide on a healthcare decision for a patient?<br />\na. based solely on their knowledge and experience<br />\nb. by considering the values and preferences of the patient<br />\nc. by ignoring the patient\'s opinions<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4708, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the rights of people living with HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. right to confidentiality, right to non-discrimination, right to informed consent, right to access healthcare, right to privacy<br />\nb. right to privacy, right to discrimination, right to informed consent, right to healthcare, right to freedom<br />\nc. right to confidentiality, right to non-discrimination, right to coerced consent, right to healthcare, right to freedom<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4709, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Who is a vulnerable child?<br />\na. a child above the age of 18<br />\nb. a child who has experienced physical or emotional harm<br />\nc. a child who is at risk of achieving poor outcomes due to factors in their lives<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4710, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What measures can be taken to prevent HIV transmission to vulnerable children?<br />\na. promote HIV education and awareness<br />\nb. provide access to HIV treatment and care<br />\nc. address stigma and discrimination<br />\nd. all of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4711, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are some interventions for vulnerable children?<br />\na. access to education, non-social protection programs, healthcare and nutrition support, psychosocial support<br />\nb. access to education, financial support programs, healthcare and nutrition support, foster care and alternative care arrangements<br />\nc. lack access to education, social protection programs, healthcare and nutrition support, legal protection<br />\nd. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4712, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of referral or medical consultation in healthcare?<br />\na. to transfer responsibility temporarily or permanently to another health professional<br />\nb. to provide confidential and legal advice to patients<br />\nc. to provide medication for patients<br />\nd. none of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4713, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of monitoring and evaluation (M&E)?<br />\na. Collecting and analyzing data to measure progress toward achieving specific goals and objectives<br />\nb. Providing legal advice to organizations<br />\nc. Ensuring transparency and accountability<br />\nd. Eliminating diversity of thought and opinions<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4714, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a benefit of M&E?<br />\na. Helps organizations learn from their mistakes<br />\nb. Encourages innovation<br />\nc. Encourages anonymity<br />\nd. Improves decision-making<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4715, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the five thematic areas of the National Strategic Framework for healthcare in Nigeria?<br />\na. Prevention of HIV, cancer, asthma, diabetes, and lupus<br />\nb. Prevention of HIV among general and key populations, HIV Testing Services, HIV Treatment, Care, Support and Adherence, and eMTCT<br />\nc. Prevention of heart disease, arthritis, Alzheimer\'s, Parkinson\'s, and dementia<br />\nd. Prevention of malaria, cholera, typhoid, Ebola, and yellow fever<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4716, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All but one are data quality issues to be considered in quality assurance<br />\na. Completeness<br />\nb. Accuracy<br />\nc. Frequency<br />\nd. Energy<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4717, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Basic elements of referral include all but one of the following<br />\na. Initiating facility<br />\nb. Receiving facility<br />\nc. Supervision and capacity building<br />\nd. The route of referral<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4718, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are vulnerable children except<br />\na. Neglected children<br />\nb. Orphans<br />\nc. Children infected with HIV<br />\nd. School children<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4719, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">HIV/AIDS has ?????.. progressive stages<br />\na. 5<br />\nb. 3<br />\nc. 4<br />\nd. 2<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4720, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">ARVS means<br />\na. Anti-retroverals<br />\nb. Anti-retrovirals<br />\nc. Auto-retrovirals<br />\nd. Ante-retrovirals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4721, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is one of the benefits of peer counseling?<br />\na. Less intimidating source of support<br />\nb. Increases medical interventions<br />\nc. Reduces the effectiveness of social support<br />\nd. Increases stigma<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4722, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the benefit of sharing experiences in peer counseling?<br />\na. Reduces isolation<br />\nb. Lessens the importance of social support<br />\nc. Increases fear of stigma<br />\nd. Provides medical advice<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4723, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is HIV primarily transmitted?<br />\na. Through casual contact like hugging or sharing utensils<br />\nb. Through respiratory droplets in the air<br />\nc. Through sexual contact or sharing of needles<br />\nd. Through contaminated food or water<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4724, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In what ways can HIV be prevented?<br />\na. Abstinence from sexual activity or not sharing needles and sharps, consistent and correct use of condoms, pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP)<br />\nb. Consuming only organic food and drink, taking vitamins, meditating<br />\nc. None, as HIV cannot be prevented<br />\nd. Only by abstaining from sharing needles<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4725, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common HIV test?<br />\na. Blood test<br />\nb. Urine test<br />\nc. Saliva test<br />\nd. X-ray test<br />\n<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4726, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT an opportunistic infection associated with HIV?<br />\na. Tuberculosis<br />\nb. Kaposi\'s Sarcoma<br />\nc. Herpes Simplex Virus<br />\nd. Oral hairy leukoplakia <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4727, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main difference between HIV and AIDS?<br />\na. HIV is the virus that causes AIDS<br />\nb. HIV is a curable condition, AIDS is not<br />\nc. HIV always leads to AIDS<br />\nd. There is no difference between HIV and AIDS<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4728, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the function of antiretroviral therapy (ART) in HIV treatment?<br />\na. It cures HIV<br />\nb. It suppresses the virus, helping to prevent transmission and lengthening the life of the infected individual<br />\nc. It kills the virus<br />\nd. It causes the immune system to stop attacking the HIV virus<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4729, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can HIV transmission from mother to child during pregnancy or breastfeeding be prevented?<br />\na. By administering antiretroviral treatment to the mother and child<br />\nb. By avoiding breastfeeding altogether<br />\nc. By reducing the number of prenatal visits<br />\nd. There is no way to prevent transmission from mother to child<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4730, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a common stigma associated with HIV/AIDS?<br />\na. People with HIV/AIDS are promiscuous and engage in risky behaviors<br />\nb. Children with HIV/AIDS are born with it because of their mother\'s immoral activity<br />\nc. People with HIV/AIDS cannot have families or normal relationships<br />\nd. People with HIV/AIDS can be cured with a simple prescription.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
(4731, '2024/2025', 'Certificate in Community Health(JCHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'HIVAIDS MANAGEMENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">___________is one of the 5Cs in Counseling in management of HIV and AIDS <br />\na. Correct test result<br />\nb. Conclusion<br />\nc. Configuration<br />\nd. Consolidation<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-10 15:35:12', '2024-07-10 15:35:12'),
