(5627, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ANATOMY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mouth, Pharynx, oesophagus and stomach are called <br />\n(a)tubular  organs <br />\n(b)layer  organs <br />\n(c) accessory  organs <br />\n(d)visceral  organs <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 17:17:26', '2024-07-15 17:17:26'),
(5628, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ANATOMY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For easy description, the abdominal cavity is divided into how many regions?<br />\n(a)nine <br />\n(b)seven <br />\n(c)five <br />\n (d)eight<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 17:17:26', '2024-07-15 17:17:26'),
(5629, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ANATOMY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">___________is the largest cavity and  it is oval in shape <br />\n(a)abdominal cavity  <br />\n(b)carnial  cavity  <br />\n(c)thoracic  cavity  <br />\n(d)pelvic cavity <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 17:17:26', '2024-07-15 17:17:26'),
(5630, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ANATOMY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Buccal means <br />\n(a) cheek <br />\n(b)leg <br />\n(c)front <br />\n(d) head<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 17:17:26', '2024-07-15 17:17:26'),
(5631, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ANATOMY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Plantar  means <br />\n(a)sole <br />\n(b)shoulder <br />\n(c)head <br />\n(d) heel.   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 17:17:26', '2024-07-15 17:17:26'),
(5632, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> ____________,___________ and _______ are to be examined when doing chest examination. <br />\n(a). Pulse, Chest and Heart. <br />\n(b). Respiration,  Lungs and Heart. <br />\n(c) Respiration, Heat and breath<br />\n(d) Lungs, chest and Heart.                 <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5633, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All but one is instrument for checking blood pressure <br />\n(a). Sphygmomanometer and Stethoscope<br />\n(b)   Sphygmomanometer and Stetoscope  <br />\n(c) Sphymomanometer and Stethoscope <br />\n(d) Sthetocope and Sphygmomanometer.             <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(5634, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In 1979 the standing order was reviewed with the aim of expanding it to cover other ------------------ conditions <br />\n(a). Elderly <br />\n(b) Childhood <br />\n(c) Preschool <br />\n(d) Adult<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5635, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The first Standing orders was  published in ------- and named------------<br />\n(a) 1976, Pediatrics standing order <br />\n(b). 1967, Pediatics Standing Orders. <br />\n(c) 1976, Gynecology Standing order. <br />\n(d). 1977, Pediatrics standing order.                             <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5636, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All referred cases must be followed up for continuity of care and ------------- <br />\n(a) Feedback.<br />\n(b) Accountability <br />\n(c)Learning process. <br />\n(d) Specialised care.  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5637, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> _________is the process of obtaining information from patient in relation to his or her health problem. <br />\n(a)Physical Examination <br />\n(b). History Talking. <br />\n(c) Inspection <br />\n(d) History Taking.    <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5638, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">_________ are rapid involuntary muscle contraction that causes uncontrollable shaking and limb movement. <br />\n(a) Poliomyelitis. <br />\n(b) Tuberculosis <br />\n(c) Convulsion <br />\n(d) Epilepsy<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5639, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Health care is supervised and controlled by the state government. <br />\n(a) Jericho Nursing Home <br />\n(b). OAUTHC <br />\n(c) Eleyele Health Centre <br />\n(d)Los Angeles<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5640, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">__________is the expulsion of the fetus before 28 weeks of gestation <br />\n(a) Labour <br />\n(b) Preterm Labour <br />\n(c) Abortion <br />\n(d) True Labour               <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5641, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">__________ is the rhythmatic movement in the arteries caused by the beating of the heart as it pumps the blood through the arteries <br />\n(a) Pulse Rate <br />\n(b) Respiratory Rate <br />\n(c) Blood Pressure <br />\n(d) Temperature rate                    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5642, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">____________ Is a case of emergency where by one or two referral facility are bye-passed in order to get the patient to the referral centre and for prompt attention <br />\n(a) Two-way Referral <br />\n(b) Emmergency rate <br />\n(c) Normal Pathway <br />\n(d) Emergency Route.               <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5643, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">___________Is very important before referring  patient to another level of health care <br />\n(a) Referral form <br />\n(b) Hospital bills <br />\n(c). Health Education <br />\n(d) provision of transportation fees to the referring centre                  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5644, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mrs Adeyinka was rushed to your health facility from her place of work on 4/06/24 with the complaint of heavy bleeding for the past 2days, Abdominal pain, weakness of the body, on examination LMP was : 25/04/24 and the cervical OS is close. What is her condition <br />\n(a) Uterine Fibroid <br />\n(b) Threatened Abortion <br />\n(c)Haemophilia <br />\n(d) Menstruation         <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5645, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All of the following are the  purpose for follow up of patient  except  <br />\n(a) To ensure regular treatment<br />\n(b)To ensure that patients or clients do not default in clinic <br />\n(c) For accountability of patient fees <br />\n(d) To review treatment carefully.    <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5646, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Referral system should be practiced in the following facilities:<br />\n(a) Hospitals <br />\n(b) All of the above <br />\n(c) None of the above <br />\n(d) Primary healthcare centers   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5647, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Infertility is <br />\n(a) inability of couple to achieve pregnancy <br />\n(b) is the inability of couple to achieve pregnancy after regular unprotected sexual intercourse<br />\n(c) is the inability of couple to achieve pregnancy after regular protected sexual intercourse <br />\n(d) is the inability of couple to achieve pregnancy after regular unprotected sexual intercourse for at least one year.     <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5648, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All of these are ways of managing infertility except???<br />\n(a). Surgery to correct abnormality <br />\n(b). Adoption <br />\n(c). procrastination <br />\n(d). Special drugs to stimulate ovulation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5649, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is the first procedure in carrying out physical examination on patient <br />\n(a) Palpation <br />\n(b)Percussion <br />\n(c) Inspection <br />\n(d) Inspecsion <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5650, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> ____ is the gaseous interchange between the tissues cells and the atmosphere <br />\n(a) pulse <br />\n(b) respiration <br />\n(c) blood pressure <br />\n(d) temperature<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5651, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the Assumption of Standing orders state that the hospital referral facilities will be available in the national health care system. <br />\n(a) Second <br />\n(b) Third <br />\n(c) Fist <br />\n(d) First    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5652, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The process of bringing down high body  temperature by dipping small towels in to  Lukewarm water to the body of patient is called <br />\n(a) Tepig sponge <br />\n(b) Tepid sponging <br />\n(c) tepis spongen <br />\n(d) tepi sponging<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5653, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The average menstrual cycle takes about _____ days  <br />\n(a) 22 <br />\n(b) 35 <br />\n(c) 25 <br />\n(d) 28     <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5654, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are standing orders primarily designed to achieve in community health practice (a) increase health care costs <br />\n(b) Standardize clinical procedures and improve quality of care <br />\n(c) Provide administrative guidelines <br />\n(d) Limit the scope of practice for health practitioners  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5655, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which body regulates the implementation and adherence to standing orders for Community Health Practitioners in Nigeria?<br />\n( a) Nigerian Medical Association   <br />\n(b) Nigerian Nursing and Midwifery Council   <br />\n(c) Community Health Practitioners Registration Board of Nigeria <br />\n(d) Ministry of Health<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5656, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes the primary purpose of standing orders?<br />\n(a) To provide financial incentives for healthcare practitioners<br />\n(b) To establish legal frameworks for community health work<br />\n(c) To ensure standardized care and improve patient outcomes<br />\n(d) To replace traditional healthcare practices<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5657, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders are typically updated to incorporate:  <br />\n(a) New administrative policies  <br />\n(b) Innovations in medical research and best practices <br />\n(c) Changes in political leadership <br />\n(d) Patient feedback and preferences<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5658, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What significant impact did the introduction of standing orders have on community health practitioners?<br />\n(a) It reduced the need for advanced training<br />\n( b) It provided clear protocols, enhancing the consistency and quality of care<br />\n(c) It increased the administrative workload <br />\n(d) It limited the practitioners\' scope of practice<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5659, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which aspect of healthcare is most directly influenced by standing orders? <br />\n(a) Financial management  <br />\n(b) Clinical decision-making and procedural consistency <br />\n(c) Health policy development <br />\n(d) Community outreach programs.    <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5660, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important for standing orders to be evidence-based?  <br />\n(a) To comply with legal requirement <br />\n(b) To ensure practices are aligned with the latest and most effective healthcare standards.  <br />\n(c) To make community health work easier  <br />\n(d) To attract funding and support     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5661, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do standing orders benefit patient care in community health settings?     <br />\n(a) By allowing practitioners to operate independently of physicians <br />\n(b) By ensuring timely, consistent, and appropriate medical interventions <br />\n(c) By reducing the overall healthcare costs <br />\n(d) By limiting the services provided to essential treatments only  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5662, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Engaging patients in their care plans can lead to -------------<br />\n(a). Improved health outcomes and patient satisfaction   <br />\n(b). Increased confusion and dissatisfaction <br />\n(c). Reduced compliance with treatment <br />\n(d). Less efficient use of healthcare resources  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5663, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Patients should be informed about the rationale behind standing orders to----------<br />\n(a). Increase their adherence to treatment  <br />\n(b). Encourage them to develop their own protocols <br />\n(c). Ensure they do not ask question <br />\n(d). Limit their understanding of medical procedures               <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5664, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">To ensure adherence to standing orders, team members should:    <br />\n(a). Independently review and sign off on protocols <br />\n(b). Collaborate and support each other <br />\n(c). Ignore protocols when convenient <br />\n(d). Only follow orders from their direct supervisor                <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5665, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders should be communicated to new team members:  <br />\n(a). During their orientation and training <br />\n(b). After they have started working independently <br />\n(c). Only if they ask about them<br />\n(d). Never, to avoid confusion    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5666, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Key components of a standing order evaluation plan include:   <br />\n(a). Regular data collection, analysis, and reporting <br />\n(b). Sporadic and informal assessments  <br />\n(c). Exclusive focus on financial outcomes  <br />\n(d). Ignoring staff and patient feedback                                            <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5667, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When implementing changes to standing orders, it is important to:  <br />\n(a). Make changes without informing staff <br />\n(b). Involve all stakeholders in the process  <br />\n(c). Delay updates as long as possible <br />\n(d). Ensure changes are minor and infrequent              <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5668, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a benefit of interdisciplinary collaboration in the use of standing orders? <br />\n(a) Improved patient outcomes <br />\n(b) Comprehensive care approaches <br />\n(c) Enhanced communication among healthcare providers <br />\n(d) All of the above                        <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5669, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How often should standing orders be reviewed to ensure they remain current and effective?   <br />\n(a) Annually   <br />\n(b) Every five years  <br />\n(c) Whenever there is a change in guidelines  <br />\n (d) Both A and C          <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5670, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which is an example of a preventive care standing order? <br />\n(a) Emergency surgery protocols  <br />\n(b) Routine vaccination schedules <br />\n(c) Intensive care unit procedure  <br />\n(d) Dietary management for acute illness                                         <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5671, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders for hypertension management might include:<br />\n(a) Automatic medication prescriptions<br />\n(b) Blood pressure monitoring protocols<br />\n(c) Weight loss programs<br />\n(d) Surgery schedules              <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5672, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In terms of patient autonomy, standing orders must ensure which of the following?       (a) Patient consent is implied  <br />\n(b) Patients are informed and can refuse treatment   <br />\n(c) Only mandatory treatments are included <br />\n(d) No patient input is needed                           <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5673, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When a standing order is implemented, who holds the legal responsibility for the outcomes?  <br />\n(a) The nurse executing the order <br />\n(b) The physician or licensed healthcare provider who authorized it     <br />\n(c) The administrative staff  <br />\n(d) The patient                         <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5674, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In an emergency situation, standing orders can help by:  <br />\n(a) Delaying care until a physician is available  <br />\n(b) Allowing immediate and standardized interventions <br />\n(c) Reducing the role of nurses  <br />\n(d) None of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5675, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following was an outcome of using standing orders in a diabetes management program?   <br />\n(a) Reduced hospital admission <br />\n(b) Increased patient confusion <br />\n(c) Higher healthcare costs <br />\n(d) None of the above           <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5676, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common method for ensuring that all healthcare staff are aware of current standing orders?  <br />\n(a) Verbal announcements    <br />\n(b) Email newsletters          <br />\n(c) Regular staff training sessions       <br />\n(d) Social media updates           <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5677, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT typically included in a standing order for a vaccination? <br />\n(a) Type of vaccine to be administered   <br />\n(b) Dosage and route of administration   <br />\n(c) Financial cost of the vaccine  <br />\n(d) Contraindications and precaution           <br />\n\'</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5678, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders can be particularly useful in managing which of the following conditions?        <br />\n(a) Chronic diseases  <br />\n(b) Acute infection  <br />\n(c) Preventive care services    <br />\n(d) All of the above           <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5679, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When implementing standing orders, it is crucial to provide training to which group of individuals?  <br />\n(a) Patients   <br />\n(b) Healthcare provider  <br />\n(c) Administrative staff only   <br />\n(d) Visitors to the health center             <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5680, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a standing order in healthcare?    <br />\n(a)To facilitate administrative tasks   <br />\n(b)To authorize certain medical interventions without direct physician involvement   (c)To manage hospital finance  <br />\n(d)To ensure patient follow-up<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5681, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders should be documented in which part of the health care setting?  (a)Patient\'s financial record  <br />\n(b) Patient\'s medical records <br />\n(c)Community health center\'s marketing materials  <br />\n(d)None of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5682, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">51. Which of the following best describes the purpose of standing orders in a community health setting? <br />\n(a). To provide a guideline for scheduling patient appointments <br />\n(b). To offer a framework for routine patient care without the need for direct physician orders <br />\n(c). To manage the financial aspects of a healthcare practice <br />\n(d). To ensure compliance with insurance regulations.   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5683, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first step a Community Health Practitioner should take when implementing a standing order? <br />\n(a). Document the patient\'s consent <br />\n(b). Verify the patient\'s identity and medical history. <br />\n(c). Administer the required medication <br />\n(d). Record the procedure in the patient\'s medical record.           <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5684, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should be included in a standing order to ensure clarity and effectiveness?  <br />\n(a). A list of potential side effects of medications <br />\n(b). Detailed instructions for the specific clinical action to be taken <br />\n(c). A description of the patient\'s insurance plan <br />\n(d). The contact information of the healthcare practitioner   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5685, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role do community health practitioners play in the effectiveness of standing orders? <br />\n(a). They develop standing orders independently <br />\n(b). They ensure standing orders are followed precisely and document any deviations <br />\n(c). They review standing orders only at the request of a physician <br />\n(d). They monitor patient financial transactions    <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5686, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a critical step in documenting the execution of a standing order? <br />\n(a). Noting the weather conditions during the visit <br />\n(b). Recording the patient\'s next appointment date <br />\n(c). Documenting the specific actions taken and patient responses <br />\n(d). Listing all medications the patient is currently taking.   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5687, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What can be a potential consequence of inadequate communication in the referral process? <br />\n(a). Improved patient satisfaction <br />\n(b). Delays in patient care and potential medical errors <br />\n(c). Increased patient trust <br />\n(d). Reduced need for  consultations<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5688, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can primary care providers ensure continuity of care during the referral process? (a). By maintaining regular communication with the specialist and the patient.   <br />\n(b).By referring the patient and then disengaging from the process  <br />\n(c). By scheduling unnecessary follow-up appointments <br />\n(d). By only documenting the initial referral.    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5689, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should be done if a patient does not follow through with a referral? <br />\n(a). Dismiss the patient from the practice. <br />\n(b). Follow up with the patient to understand the barriers and encourage compliance.  (c). Refer the patient to another specialist <br />\n(d). Ignore the issue and move on<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5690, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can primary care providers ensure that referrals are appropriate and necessary? <br />\n(a) By referring all patients for specialist care <br />\n(b).By using generic referral forms <br />\n(c). By relying solely on patient requests. <br />\n(d). By conducting thorough assessments and discussing options with the patient        </p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5691, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main objective of follow-up appointments in the referral process? <br />\n(a). To increase revenue for the healthcare facility <br />\n(b). To ensure the patient?s condition is monitored and managed appropriately <br />\n(c). To reduce the specialist?s workload <br />\n(d). To verify patient insurance information.     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5692, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a two-way referral system in primary health care?<br />\n(a) . To facilitate communication and continuity of care between primary and secondary care providers <br />\n(b)To manage patient billing efficiently  <br />\n(c). To reduce the workload of primary care practitioners <br />\n(d). To ensure all patients are referred to specialists.   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5693, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a key benefit of an effective two-way referral system? <br />\n(a). Increased hospital admissions <br />\n(b). Better patient outcomes through coordinated care. <br />\n(c). Reduced need for medical records. <br />\n(d). Higher patient co-pays.       <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5694, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What essential information should be included in a referral from a primary care provider to a specialist? <br />\n(a). Patient\'s insurance details <br />\n (b). Patient\'s employment history. <br />\n(c). Patient\'s complete medical history and reason for referral <br />\n(d). Patient\'s dietary preferences.     <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5695, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In a two-way referral system, what is expected from the specialist after seeing the referred patient? <br />\n(A). Bill the primary care provider directly <br />\n(b).Schedule follow-up appointments without informing the primary care provider. <br />\n(c). Keep the referral information confidential <br />\n(d). Send a detailed report back to the primary care provider<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5696, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes a successful referral process? <br />\n(a). The patient only visits the specialist <br />\n(b). Continuous communication between the referring and receiving providers <br />\n(c). The primary care provider remains uninvolved after the referral <br />\n(d). The specialist takes over all aspects of the patient?s care      <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5697, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important for primary care providers to follow up with patients after a referral? (a). To ensure the patient received the bill <br />\n(b). To assess the effectiveness of the referral and plan further care <br />\n(c). To promote the primary care provider\'s services <br />\n(d). To check if the patient prefers another specialist.     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5698, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can electronic health records (EHRs) improve the referral process? <br />\n(a).  By facilitating faster and more accurate information exchange between providers (b)By automating patient billing. <br />\n(c). By eliminating the need for patient appointments <br />\n(d). By reducing the workload of administrative staff.   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5699, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a critical component of a referral form? <br />\n(a). Patient\'s favorite color <br />\n(b). Detailed patient symptoms and preliminary diagnosis <br />\n(c). List of patient\'s hobbies <br />\n(d). Patient\'s vacation history.   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5700, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which statement best describes a \"closed-loop\" referral system? <br />\n(a). It involves referring patients only within a single healthcare organization <br />\n(b). It ensures that all referrals are tracked and feedback is provided to the referring provider <br />\n(c). It limits patient referrals to one specialist <br />\n(d). It excludes patient involvement in the referral process.     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5701, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a key feature of an effective two-way referral communication system? <br />\n(a). It involves only the primary care provider <br />\n(b). It is one-way, with information flowing from the primary care provider to the specialist only <br />\n(c). It is bi-directional, ensuring feedback and updates between providers<br />\n(d). It avoids using electronic systems.                     <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:14:51', '2024-07-15 18:14:51'),
(5702, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> ____________,___________ and _______ are to be examined when doing chest examination. <br />\n(a). Pulse, Chest and Heart. <br />\n(b). Respiration,  Lungs and Heart. <br />\n(c) Respiration, Heat and breath<br />\n(d) Lungs, chest and Heart.                 <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5703, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All but one is instrument for checking blood pressure <br />\n(a). Sphygmomanometer and Stethoscope<br />\n(b)   Sphygmomanometer and Stetoscope  <br />\n(c) Sphymomanometer and Stethoscope <br />\n(d) Sthetocope and Sphygmomanometer.             <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5704, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In 1979 the standing order was reviewed with the aim of expanding it to cover other ------------------ conditions <br />\n(a). Elderly <br />\n(b) Childhood <br />\n(c) Preschool <br />\n(d) Adult<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5705, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The first Standing orders was  published in ------- and named------------<br />\n(a) 1976, Pediatrics standing order <br />\n(b). 1967, Pediatics Standing Orders. <br />\n(c) 1976, Gynecology Standing order. <br />\n(d). 1977, Pediatrics standing order.                             <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5706, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All referred cases must be followed up for continuity of care and ------------- <br />\n(a) Feedback.<br />\n(b) Accountability <br />\n(c)Learning process. <br />\n(d) Specialised care.  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5707, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> _________is the process of obtaining information from patient in relation to his or her health problem. <br />\n(a)Physical Examination <br />\n(b). History Talking. <br />\n(c) Inspection <br />\n(d) History Taking.    <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5708, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">_________ are rapid involuntary muscle contraction that causes uncontrollable shaking and limb movement. <br />\n(a) Poliomyelitis. <br />\n(b) Tuberculosis <br />\n(c) Convulsion <br />\n(d) Epilepsy<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5709, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Health care is supervised and controlled by the state government. <br />\n(a) Jericho Nursing Home <br />\n(b). OAUTHC <br />\n(c) Eleyele Health Centre <br />\n(d)Los Angeles<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5710, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">__________is the expulsion of the fetus before 28 weeks of gestation <br />\n(a) Labour <br />\n(b) Preterm Labour <br />\n(c) Abortion <br />\n(d) True Labour               <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5711, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">__________ is the rhythmatic movement in the arteries caused by the beating of the heart as it pumps the blood through the arteries <br />\n(a) Pulse Rate <br />\n(b) Respiratory Rate <br />\n(c) Blood Pressure <br />\n(d) Temperature rate                    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5712, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">____________ Is a case of emergency where by one or two referral facility are bye-passed in order to get the patient to the referral centre and for prompt attention <br />\n(a) Two-way Referral <br />\n(b) Emmergency rate <br />\n(c) Normal Pathway <br />\n(d) Emergency Route.               <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5713, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">___________Is very important before referring  patient to another level of health care <br />\n(a) Referral form <br />\n(b) Hospital bills <br />\n(c). Health Education <br />\n(d) provision of transportation fees to the referring centre                  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5714, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mrs Adeyinka was rushed to your health facility from her place of work on 4/06/24 with the complaint of heavy bleeding for the past 2days, Abdominal pain, weakness of the body, on examination LMP was : 25/04/24 and the cervical OS is close. What is her condition <br />\n(a) Uterine Fibroid <br />\n(b) Threatened Abortion <br />\n(c)Haemophilia <br />\n(d) Menstruation         <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5715, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All of the following are the  purpose for follow up of patient  except  <br />\n(a) To ensure regular treatment<br />\n(b)To ensure that patients or clients do not default in clinic <br />\n(c) For accountability of patient fees <br />\n(d) To review treatment carefully.    <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5716, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Referral system should be practiced in the following facilities:<br />\n(a) Hospitals <br />\n(b) All of the above <br />\n(c) None of the above <br />\n(d) Primary healthcare centers   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5717, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Infertility is <br />\n(a) inability of couple to achieve pregnancy <br />\n(b) is the inability of couple to achieve pregnancy after regular unprotected sexual intercourse<br />\n(c) is the inability of couple to achieve pregnancy after regular protected sexual intercourse <br />\n(d) is the inability of couple to achieve pregnancy after regular unprotected sexual intercourse for at least one year.     <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5718, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All of these are ways of managing infertility except???<br />\n(a). Surgery to correct abnormality <br />\n(b). Adoption <br />\n(c). procrastination <br />\n(d). Special drugs to stimulate ovulation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5719, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is the first procedure in carrying out physical examination on patient <br />\n(a) Palpation <br />\n(b)Percussion <br />\n(c) Inspection <br />\n(d) Inspecsion <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5720, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> ____ is the gaseous interchange between the tissues cells and the atmosphere <br />\n(a) pulse <br />\n(b) respiration <br />\n(c) blood pressure <br />\n(d) temperature<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5721, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the Assumption of Standing orders state that the hospital referral facilities will be available in the national health care system. <br />\n(a) Second <br />\n(b) Third <br />\n(c) Fist <br />\n(d) First    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5722, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The process of bringing down high body  temperature by dipping small towels in to  Lukewarm water to the body of patient is called <br />\n(a) Tepig sponge <br />\n(b) Tepid sponging <br />\n(c) tepis spongen <br />\n(d) tepi sponging<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(5723, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The average menstrual cycle takes about _____ days  <br />\n(a) 22 <br />\n(b) 35 <br />\n(c) 25 <br />\n(d) 28     <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5724, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are standing orders primarily designed to achieve in community health practice (a) increase health care costs <br />\n(b) Standardize clinical procedures and improve quality of care <br />\n(c) Provide administrative guidelines <br />\n(d) Limit the scope of practice for health practitioners  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5725, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which body regulates the implementation and adherence to standing orders for Community Health Practitioners in Nigeria?<br />\n( a) Nigerian Medical Association   <br />\n(b) Nigerian Nursing and Midwifery Council   <br />\n(c) Community Health Practitioners Registration Board of Nigeria <br />\n(d) Ministry of Health<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5726, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes the primary purpose of standing orders?<br />\n(a) To provide financial incentives for healthcare practitioners<br />\n(b) To establish legal frameworks for community health work<br />\n(c) To ensure standardized care and improve patient outcomes<br />\n(d) To replace traditional healthcare practices<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5727, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders are typically updated to incorporate:  <br />\n(a) New administrative policies  <br />\n(b) Innovations in medical research and best practices <br />\n(c) Changes in political leadership <br />\n(d) Patient feedback and preferences<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5728, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What significant impact did the introduction of standing orders have on community health practitioners?<br />\n(a) It reduced the need for advanced training<br />\n( b) It provided clear protocols, enhancing the consistency and quality of care<br />\n(c) It increased the administrative workload <br />\n(d) It limited the practitioners\' scope of practice<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5729, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which aspect of healthcare is most directly influenced by standing orders? <br />\n(a) Financial management  <br />\n(b) Clinical decision-making and procedural consistency <br />\n(c) Health policy development <br />\n(d) Community outreach programs.    <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5730, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important for standing orders to be evidence-based?  <br />\n(a) To comply with legal requirement <br />\n(b) To ensure practices are aligned with the latest and most effective healthcare standards.  <br />\n(c) To make community health work easier  <br />\n(d) To attract funding and support     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5731, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How do standing orders benefit patient care in community health settings?     <br />\n(a) By allowing practitioners to operate independently of physicians <br />\n(b) By ensuring timely, consistent, and appropriate medical interventions <br />\n(c) By reducing the overall healthcare costs <br />\n(d) By limiting the services provided to essential treatments only  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5732, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Engaging patients in their care plans can lead to -------------<br />\n(a). Improved health outcomes and patient satisfaction   <br />\n(b). Increased confusion and dissatisfaction <br />\n(c). Reduced compliance with treatment <br />\n(d). Less efficient use of healthcare resources  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5733, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Patients should be informed about the rationale behind standing orders to----------<br />\n(a). Increase their adherence to treatment  <br />\n(b). Encourage them to develop their own protocols <br />\n(c). Ensure they do not ask question <br />\n(d). Limit their understanding of medical procedures               <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5734, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">To ensure adherence to standing orders, team members should:    <br />\n(a). Independently review and sign off on protocols <br />\n(b). Collaborate and support each other <br />\n(c). Ignore protocols when convenient <br />\n(d). Only follow orders from their direct supervisor                <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5735, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders should be communicated to new team members:  <br />\n(a). During their orientation and training <br />\n(b). After they have started working independently <br />\n(c). Only if they ask about them<br />\n(d). Never, to avoid confusion    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5736, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Key components of a standing order evaluation plan include:   <br />\n(a). Regular data collection, analysis, and reporting <br />\n(b). Sporadic and informal assessments  <br />\n(c). Exclusive focus on financial outcomes  <br />\n(d). Ignoring staff and patient feedback                                            <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5737, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When implementing changes to standing orders, it is important to:  <br />\n(a). Make changes without informing staff <br />\n(b). Involve all stakeholders in the process  <br />\n(c). Delay updates as long as possible <br />\n(d). Ensure changes are minor and infrequent              <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5738, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a benefit of interdisciplinary collaboration in the use of standing orders? <br />\n(a) Improved patient outcomes <br />\n(b) Comprehensive care approaches <br />\n(c) Enhanced communication among healthcare providers <br />\n(d) All of the above                        <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5739, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How often should standing orders be reviewed to ensure they remain current and effective?   <br />\n(a) Annually   <br />\n(b) Every five years  <br />\n(c) Whenever there is a change in guidelines  <br />\n (d) Both A and C          <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5740, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which is an example of a preventive care standing order? <br />\n(a) Emergency surgery protocols  <br />\n(b) Routine vaccination schedules <br />\n(c) Intensive care unit procedure  <br />\n(d) Dietary management for acute illness                                         <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5741, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders for hypertension management might include:<br />\n(a) Automatic medication prescriptions<br />\n(b) Blood pressure monitoring protocols<br />\n(c) Weight loss programs<br />\n(d) Surgery schedules              <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5742, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In terms of patient autonomy, standing orders must ensure which of the following?       (a) Patient consent is implied  <br />\n(b) Patients are informed and can refuse treatment   <br />\n(c) Only mandatory treatments are included <br />\n(d) No patient input is needed                           <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5743, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When a standing order is implemented, who holds the legal responsibility for the outcomes?  <br />\n(a) The nurse executing the order <br />\n(b) The physician or licensed healthcare provider who authorized it     <br />\n(c) The administrative staff  <br />\n(d) The patient                         <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5744, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In an emergency situation, standing orders can help by:  <br />\n(a) Delaying care until a physician is available  <br />\n(b) Allowing immediate and standardized interventions <br />\n(c) Reducing the role of nurses  <br />\n(d) None of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5745, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following was an outcome of using standing orders in a diabetes management program?   <br />\n(a) Reduced hospital admission <br />\n(b) Increased patient confusion <br />\n(c) Higher healthcare costs <br />\n(d) None of the above           <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5746, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common method for ensuring that all healthcare staff are aware of current standing orders?  <br />\n(a) Verbal announcements    <br />\n(b) Email newsletters          <br />\n(c) Regular staff training sessions       <br />\n(d) Social media updates           <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5747, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT typically included in a standing order for a vaccination? <br />\n(a) Type of vaccine to be administered   <br />\n(b) Dosage and route of administration   <br />\n(c) Financial cost of the vaccine  <br />\n(d) Contraindications and precaution           <br />\n\'</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5748, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders can be particularly useful in managing which of the following conditions?        <br />\n(a) Chronic diseases  <br />\n(b) Acute infection  <br />\n(c) Preventive care services    <br />\n(d) All of the above           <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5749, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When implementing standing orders, it is crucial to provide training to which group of individuals?  <br />\n(a) Patients   <br />\n(b) Healthcare provider  <br />\n(c) Administrative staff only   <br />\n(d) Visitors to the health center             <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5750, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a standing order in healthcare?    <br />\n(a)To facilitate administrative tasks   <br />\n(b)To authorize certain medical interventions without direct physician involvement   (c)To manage hospital finance  <br />\n(d)To ensure patient follow-up<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5751, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Standing orders should be documented in which part of the health care setting?  (a)Patient\'s financial record  <br />\n(b) Patient\'s medical records <br />\n(c)Community health center\'s marketing materials  <br />\n(d)None of the above<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5752, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">51. Which of the following best describes the purpose of standing orders in a community health setting? <br />\n(a). To provide a guideline for scheduling patient appointments <br />\n(b). To offer a framework for routine patient care without the need for direct physician orders <br />\n(c). To manage the financial aspects of a healthcare practice <br />\n(d). To ensure compliance with insurance regulations.   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5753, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first step a Community Health Practitioner should take when implementing a standing order? <br />\n(a). Document the patient\'s consent <br />\n(b). Verify the patient\'s identity and medical history. <br />\n(c). Administer the required medication <br />\n(d). Record the procedure in the patient\'s medical record.           <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5754, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should be included in a standing order to ensure clarity and effectiveness?  <br />\n(a). A list of potential side effects of medications <br />\n(b). Detailed instructions for the specific clinical action to be taken <br />\n(c). A description of the patient\'s insurance plan <br />\n(d). The contact information of the healthcare practitioner   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5755, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What role do community health practitioners play in the effectiveness of standing orders? <br />\n(a). They develop standing orders independently <br />\n(b). They ensure standing orders are followed precisely and document any deviations <br />\n(c). They review standing orders only at the request of a physician <br />\n(d). They monitor patient financial transactions    <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5756, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a critical step in documenting the execution of a standing order? <br />\n(a). Noting the weather conditions during the visit <br />\n(b). Recording the patient\'s next appointment date <br />\n(c). Documenting the specific actions taken and patient responses <br />\n(d). Listing all medications the patient is currently taking.   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5757, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What can be a potential consequence of inadequate communication in the referral process? <br />\n(a). Improved patient satisfaction <br />\n(b). Delays in patient care and potential medical errors <br />\n(c). Increased patient trust <br />\n(d). Reduced need for  consultations<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5758, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can primary care providers ensure continuity of care during the referral process? (a). By maintaining regular communication with the specialist and the patient.   <br />\n(b).By referring the patient and then disengaging from the process  <br />\n(c). By scheduling unnecessary follow-up appointments <br />\n(d). By only documenting the initial referral.    <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5759, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should be done if a patient does not follow through with a referral? <br />\n(a). Dismiss the patient from the practice. <br />\n(b). Follow up with the patient to understand the barriers and encourage compliance.  (c). Refer the patient to another specialist <br />\n(d). Ignore the issue and move on<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5760, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can primary care providers ensure that referrals are appropriate and necessary? <br />\n(a) By referring all patients for specialist care <br />\n(b).By using generic referral forms <br />\n(c). By relying solely on patient requests. <br />\n(d). By conducting thorough assessments and discussing options with the patient        </p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5761, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main objective of follow-up appointments in the referral process? <br />\n(a). To increase revenue for the healthcare facility <br />\n(b). To ensure the patient?s condition is monitored and managed appropriately <br />\n(c). To reduce the specialist?s workload <br />\n(d). To verify patient insurance information.     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5762, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a two-way referral system in primary health care?<br />\n(a) . To facilitate communication and continuity of care between primary and secondary care providers <br />\n(b)To manage patient billing efficiently  <br />\n(c). To reduce the workload of primary care practitioners <br />\n(d). To ensure all patients are referred to specialists.   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5763, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a key benefit of an effective two-way referral system? <br />\n(a). Increased hospital admissions <br />\n(b). Better patient outcomes through coordinated care. <br />\n(c). Reduced need for medical records. <br />\n(d). Higher patient co-pays.       <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5764, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What essential information should be included in a referral from a primary care provider to a specialist? <br />\n(a). Patient\'s insurance details <br />\n (b). Patient\'s employment history. <br />\n(c). Patient\'s complete medical history and reason for referral <br />\n(d). Patient\'s dietary preferences.     <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5765, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In a two-way referral system, what is expected from the specialist after seeing the referred patient? <br />\n(A). Bill the primary care provider directly <br />\n(b).Schedule follow-up appointments without informing the primary care provider. <br />\n(c). Keep the referral information confidential <br />\n(d). Send a detailed report back to the primary care provider<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5766, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes a successful referral process? <br />\n(a). The patient only visits the specialist <br />\n(b). Continuous communication between the referring and receiving providers <br />\n(c). The primary care provider remains uninvolved after the referral <br />\n(d). The specialist takes over all aspects of the patient?s care      <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5767, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important for primary care providers to follow up with patients after a referral? (a). To ensure the patient received the bill <br />\n(b). To assess the effectiveness of the referral and plan further care <br />\n(c). To promote the primary care provider\'s services <br />\n(d). To check if the patient prefers another specialist.     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5768, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can electronic health records (EHRs) improve the referral process? <br />\n(a).  By facilitating faster and more accurate information exchange between providers (b)By automating patient billing. <br />\n(c). By eliminating the need for patient appointments <br />\n(d). By reducing the workload of administrative staff.   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5769, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a critical component of a referral form? <br />\n(a). Patient\'s favorite color <br />\n(b). Detailed patient symptoms and preliminary diagnosis <br />\n(c). List of patient\'s hobbies <br />\n(d). Patient\'s vacation history.   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5770, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which statement best describes a \"closed-loop\" referral system? <br />\n(a). It involves referring patients only within a single healthcare organization <br />\n(b). It ensures that all referrals are tracked and feedback is provided to the referring provider <br />\n(c). It limits patient referrals to one specialist <br />\n(d). It excludes patient involvement in the referral process.     <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5771, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'STANDING ORDER', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 70, 70, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a key feature of an effective two-way referral communication system? <br />\n(a). It involves only the primary care provider <br />\n(b). It is one-way, with information flowing from the primary care provider to the specialist only <br />\n(c). It is bi-directional, ensuring feedback and updates between providers<br />\n(d). It avoids using electronic systems.                     <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-15 18:17:09', '2024-07-15 18:17:09'),
(5772, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is the primary function of hemoglobin?<br />\n (a) Transporting nutrients<br />\n(b)Transporting oxygen<br />\n(c) Producing white blood cells<br />\n(d) Clotting blood   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5773, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which method is most commonly used for hemoglobin estimation in clinical laboratories? <br />\n(a) Sahli?s method <br />\n(b) Hematocrit method <br />\n(c) Cyanmethemoglobin method <br />\n(d) Western blotting <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5774, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range of hemoglobin for adult males? <br />\n(a) 10.5 to 12.5 g/dL <br />\n(b) 13.8 to 17.2 g/dL <br />\n(c) 18.5 to 20.5 g/dL<br />\n(d) 21.0 to 23.0 g/dL <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5775, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range of hemoglobin for adult females? <br />\n(a) 9.0 to 11.0 g/dL <br />\n(b) 11.5 to 13.5 g/dL <br />\n(c) 12.1 to 15.1 g/dL <br />\n(d) 15.5 to 17.5 g/dL <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5776, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is anemia? <br />\n(a) A condition of high blood sugar levels <br />\n(b) A condition characterized by a deficiency in the number or quality of red blood cells or hemoglobin (c) A condition where blood clotting is impaired <br />\n(d) A condition of high white blood cell count<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5777, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which instrument is commonly used to measure hemoglobin concentration in blood?<br />\n(a) Microscope <br />\n(b) Hemoglobinometer <br />\n(c) Centrifuge <br />\n(d) Autoclave   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5778, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important to estimate hemoglobin levels in patients? <br />\n(a) To diagnose and monitor liver function <br />\n(b) To diagnose and monitor conditions like anemia and polycythemia <br />\n(c) To determine blood clotting ability <br />\n(d) To measure kidney function<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5779, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first step in managing a minor wound? <br />\n(a) Apply antibiotic ointment <br />\n(b) Clean the wound with water <br />\n(c) Cover the wound with a bandage <br />\n(d) Take pain medication<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5780, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of wound is characterized by the skin being torn or jagged? <br />\n(a) Abrasion <br />\n(b) Laceration <br />\n(c) Puncture <br />\n(d) Contusion   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5781, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a wound dressing? <br />\n(a) To decorate the wound <br />\n(b) To keep the wound dry <br />\n(c) To protect the wound from infection <br />\n(d) To help the wound bleed more<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5782, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of wound is most likely to require stitches?<br />\n(a) Superficial abrasion<br />\n(b) Minor laceration <br />\n(c) Deep cut with jagged edges <br />\n(d) Small puncture wound  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5783, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a sign of infection in a wound? <br />\n(a) Decreased swelling <br />\n(b) Clear, odorless drainage <br />\n(c) Redness and warmth around the wound <br />\n(d) Itching    <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5784, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the best way to control bleeding from a wound? <br />\n(a) Apply ice directly to the wound <br />\n(b) Elevate the wound above heart level <br />\n(c) Apply direct pressure to the wound <br />\n(d) Leave the wound open to air<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5785, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why should you avoid using hydrogen peroxide on a wound? <br />\n(a) It doesn\'t clean the wound <br />\n(b) It can damage the tissue and delay healing <br />\n(c) It causes excessive bleeding<br />\n (d) It is not readily available<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5786, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following wounds is caused by a sharp object like a nail or needle? <br />\n(a) Laceration <br />\n(b) Abrasion <br />\n(c) Puncture <br />\n(d) Contusion   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5787, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main characteristic of a chronic wound? <br />\n(a) Heals within a few days <br />\n(b) Shows no sign of healing after 2-4 weeks <br />\n(c) Bleeds profusely <br />\n(d) Causes intense pain immediately <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5788, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For which type of wound is tetanus prophylaxis most important? <br />\n(a) Clean, superficial cut <br />\n(b) Laceration with minimal bleeding <br />\n(c) Deep puncture wound, especially from a dirty object <br />\n(d) Minor abrasion  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5789, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary goal of routine immunization? <br />\n(a) To diagnose diseases <br />\n(b) To treat diseases <br />\n(c) To prevent diseases <br />\n(d) To alleviate symptoms <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5790, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following diseases can be prevented by the DTaP vaccine? <br />\n(a) Diphtheria, Tetanus, Pertussis <br />\n(b) Dengue, Typhoid, Anthrax <br />\n(c) Diabetes, Thyroiditis, Asthma <br />\n(d) Diarrhea, Tuberculosis, Anemia<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5791, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what age is the first dose of the MMR vaccine typically given? <br />\n(a) At birth <br />\n(b) 6 months <br />\n(c) 12-15 months <br />\n(d) 18 months  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5792, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following vaccines is given to prevent rotavirus infection? <br />\n(a) IPV <br />\n(b) Rotavirus vaccine <br />\n(c) Hib <br />\n(d) Hepatitis B   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5793, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Hepatitis B vaccine is typically administered  <br />\n(a) Once at age 10 <br />\n(b) In three doses starting at birth <br />\n(c) Annually <br />\n(d) Only if there is an outbreak<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5794, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which vaccine is recommended for preventing cervical cancer? <br />\n(a) MMR <br />\n(b) Hepatitis A <br />\n(c) HPV <br />\n(d) Varicella  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5795, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a contraindication for live vaccines?  <br />\n(a) Mild fever <br />\n(b) Current antibiotic use <br />\n(c) Pregnancy <br />\n(d) Mild asthma  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5796, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The term \"herd immunity\" refers to: <br />\n(a) Immunity developed from surviving an infection <br />\n(b) Immunity resulting from vaccination <br />\n(c) Protection from disease when a large portion of the population is immune <br />\n(d) Immunity passed from mother to child <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:02', '2024-07-16 14:54:02'),
(5797, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How often is the influenza vaccine recommended for most people? <br />\n(a) Every 5 years <br />\n(b) Every 2 years<br />\n (c) Annually <br />\n(d) Once in a lifetime  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5798, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which vaccine is administered to protect against Haemophilus influenzae type b? <br />\n(a) Hepatitis B <br />\n(b) Hib <br />\n(c) DTaP <br />\n(d) MMR <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5799, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended age for the first dose of the Varicella (chickenpox) vaccine? <br />\n(a) At birth <br />\n(b) 6 months <br />\n(c) 12-15 months <br />\n(d) 5 years <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5800, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common side effect of vaccines? <br />\n(a) Severe allergic reaction <br />\n(b) Mild fever <br />\n(c) Chronic illness <br />\n(d) Fractures  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5801, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pneumococcal vaccine protects against infections caused by_______<br />\n (a) Staphylococcus aureus <br />\n(b) Streptococcus pneumoniae <br />\n(c) Haemophilus influenzae <br />\n(d) Mycobacterium tuberculosis  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5802, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which organization provides immunization schedules and guidelines in the United States? <br />\n(a) World Health Organization (WHO) <br />\n(b) Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)  <br />\n(c) American Medical Association (AMA) <br />\n(d) National Institutes of Health (NIH)  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5803, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What type of vaccine is the polio vaccine (IPV)? <br />\n(a) Live attenuated <br />\n(b) Inactivated <br />\n(c) Subunit <br />\n(d) Toxoid<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5804, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following vaccines is administered to adolescents to prevent meningococcal disease? <br />\n(a) Hepatitis A <br />\n(b) Meningococcal conjugate vaccine <br />\n(c) Rotavirus vaccine <br />\n(d) Tdap <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5805, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what age is the first dose of the Hepatitis A vaccine recommended? <br />\n(a) At birth <br />\n(b) 6 months <br />\n(c) 12-23 months <br />\n(d) 5 years  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5806, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many doses of the HPV vaccine are recommended for adolescents starting the series before their 15th birthday? <br />\n(a) 1 dose <br />\n(b) 2 doses <br />\n(c) 3 doses <br />\n(d) 4 doses  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5807, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which vaccine is given to prevent tetanus, diphtheria, and whooping cough in adults? <br />\n(a) DTaP <br />\n(b) MMR <br />\n(c) Tdap <br />\n(d) Varicella   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5808, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended site for administering intramuscular vaccines in infants? <br />\n(a) Deltoid muscle <br />\n(b) Vastus lateralis muscle <br />\n(c) Gluteal muscle <br />\n(d) Biceps muscle   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5809, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary cause of tooth decay? <br />\n(a) Saliva <br />\n(b) Plaque <br />\n(c) Fluoride <br />\n(d) Water <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5810, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is the best time to brush your teeth? <br />\n(a) Right after every meal <br />\n(b) before breakfast and before bed <br />\n(c) Once a day, anytime <br />\n(d) Only when they feel dirty<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5811, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What mineral in water and toothpaste helps to strengthen tooth enamel? <br />\n(a) Calcium <br />\n(b) Iron <br />\n(c) Fluoride <br />\n(d) Potassium <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5812, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How often should you visit the dentist for a routine check-up?  <br />\n(a) Once a year <br />\n(b) Every six months <br />\n(c) Only when you have a toothache <br />\n(d) Every two years  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5813, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following foods is least likely to cause tooth decay? <br />\n(a) Candy <br />\n(b) Soda <br />\n(c) Cheese <br />\n(d) Cookies  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5814, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended duration for brushing your teeth? <br />\n(a) 30 seconds <br />\n(b) 1 minute <br />\n(c) 2 minutes <br />\n(d) 5 minutes  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(5815, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is gingivitis? <br />\n(a) A type of toothpaste <br />\n(b) Inflammation of the gums <br />\n(c) A type of dental filling <br />\n(d) None of the above   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5816, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the function of dental floss? <br />\n(a) To whiten teeth <br />\n(b) To remove plaque and food particles between teeth <br />\n(c) To freshen breath <br />\n(d) To polish teeth <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5817, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a symptom of gum disease?<br />\n(a) Swollen and bleeding gums <br />\n(b) White spots on teeth<br />\n (c) Sensitive teeth <br />\n(d) Bad breath  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5818, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important to limit sugary foods and drinks for oral health? <br />\n(a) They stain the teeth<br />\n (b) They can cause cavities <br />\n(c) They make the gums sensitive<br />\n (d) They have no impact on oral health  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5819, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of the oral route of drug administration? <br />\n(a) Injection <br />\n(b) Inhalation <br />\n(c) Tablet <br />\n(d) Topical cream  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5820, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration involves injecting a drug directly into a vein? <br />\n(a) Intramuscular <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Subcutaneous <br />\n(d) Intradermal  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5821, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration is commonly used for insulin delivery? <br />\n(a) Intramuscular <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Subcutaneous <br />\n(d) Inhalation  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5822, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary advantage of the transdermal route of administration? <br />\n(a) Rapid onset of action <br />\n(b) Easy to administer<br />\n (c) Bypasses the digestive system <br />\n(d) Suitable for large doses <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5823, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration is typically used for vaccines? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intramuscular <br />\n(c) Inhalation <br />\n(d) Transdermal  <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5824, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following routes of administration provides the fastest drug action? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Subcutaneous <br />\n(d) Intramuscular  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5825, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the route of administration for drugs delivered through a nebulizer? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Inhalation <br />\n(d) Topical  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5826, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration involves placing a drug under the tongue for absorption? <br />\n(a) Buccal <br />\n(b) Sublingual <br />\n(c) Oral <br />\n(d) Subcutes <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5827, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration involves applying medication directly to the skin? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Topical <br />\n(d) Inhalation  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5828, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary advantages of the rectal route of administration? <br />\n(a) Pleasant taste <br />\n(b) Rapid absorption <br />\n(c) Bypasses the first-pass metabolism <br />\n(d) Suitable for all types of medications  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5829, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common symptom of a scorpion sting? <br />\n(a) Intense pain at the sting site <br />\n(b) High fever <br />\n(c) Severe headache <br />\n(d) Nausea and vomiting  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5830, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first step you should take if bitten by a snake? <br />\n(a) Apply ice to the bite <br />\n(b) Suck out the venom <br />\n(c) Keep the affected limb immobilized and below heart level <br />\n(d) Give the victim water to drink  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5831, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of snake bite is most dangerous? <br />\n(a) Non-venomous snake bite <br />\n(b) Venomous snake bite <br />\n(c) Dry bite (no venom injected)<br />\n (d) Snake bite on a thick-skinned area  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5832, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a potential complication of a scorpion sting? <br />\n(a) Anaphylaxis <br />\n(b) Rabies <br />\n(c) Tetanus <br />\n(d) Hemorrhagic fever  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5833, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary treatment for a venomous snake bite? <br />\n(a) Antivenom <br />\n(b) Antibiotics <br />\n(c) Painkillers <br />\n(d) Antihistamines  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5834, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which symptom is NOT commonly associated with a venomous snake bite? <br />\n(a) Swelling and bruising around the bite <br />\n(b) Excessive sweating <br />\n(c) Blurred vision <br />\n(d) Hair loss  <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5835, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can you prevent scorpion stings when traveling in areas where they are common? <br />\n(a) Wear thick-soled shoes and shake out clothes before wearing <br />\n(b) Avoid drinking tap water <br />\n(c) Always carry a flashlight <br />\n(d) Use insect repellent  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5836, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should you avoid doing after a snake bite? <br />\n(a) Washing the bite area with soap and water <br />\n(b) Using a tourniquet above the bite site <br />\n(c) Keeping the victim calm and still <br />\n(d) Seeking medical help immediately  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5837, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which region is most commonly associated with dangerous scorpions? <br />\n(a) Arctic <br />\n(b) Deserts and tropical regions <br />\n(c) Coastal areas <br />\n(d) Rainforests  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5838, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a sign that you should seek medical attention for a scorpion sting? <br />\n(a) Mild itching at the sting site<br />\n (b) Severe pain that spreads from the sting site <br />\n(c) No pain or symptoms after the sting <br />\n(d) Redness that fades quickly <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5839, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a cold chain system primarily used for? <br />\n(a) Transporting non-perishable goods <br />\n(b) Storing dry foods <br />\n(c) Keeping perishable products at required temperatures <br />\n(d) Preserving canned foods   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5840, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a component of the cold chain system? <br />\n(a) Refrigerated storage <br />\n(b) Dry warehouses <br />\n(c) Refrigerated transportation <br />\n(d) Temperature monitoring devices <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5841, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What temperature range is typically maintained for frozen products in a cold chain? <br />\n(a) 0?C to 4?C <br />\n(b) -10?C to 0?C <br />\n(c) -18?C or lower <br />\n(d) 5?C to 10?C   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5842, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is temperature monitoring crucial in a cold chain system? <br />\n(a) To ensure product safety and quality <br />\n(b) To reduce transportation costs<br />\n (c) To increase shelf life of non-perishable goods <br />\n(d) To maintain ambient warehouse conditions <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5843, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which technology is often used to monitor temperature in cold chain logistics? <br />\n(a) Barcodes <br />\n(b) GPS tracking <br />\n(c) RFID sensors <br />\n(d) QR codes   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5844, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main purpose of a refrigerated truck in the cold chain system? <br />\n(a) To transport goods at room temperature <br />\n(b) To minimize transportation time <br />\n(c) To maintain a specific temperature during transport <br />\n(d) To maximize storage capacity <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5845, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which industry heavily relies on the cold chain system? <br />\n(a) Electronics <br />\n(b) Pharmaceuticals <br />\n(c) Textiles <br />\n(d) Construction  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5846, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common consequence of a break in the cold chain? <br />\n(a) Increase in product value <br />\n(b) Extended product shelf life<br />\n(c) Degradation or spoilage of products <br />\n(d) Improved product safety  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5847, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes \"last mile delivery\" in the context of the cold chain? <br />\n(a) The initial stage of product transportation <br />\n(b) The transportation from distribution center to final destination <br />\n(c) The packaging process of cold chain products <br />\n(d) The storage phase at the manufacturer\'s facility  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5848, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of insulated containers in a cold chain system? <br />\n(a) To reduce transportation costs<br />\n (b) To protect products from physical damage <br />\n(c) To maintain temperature during transit <br />\n(d) To enhance product packaging   <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5849, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is visual acuity? <br />\n(a) The ability to distinguish colors<br />\n (b) The sharpness of vision <br />\n(c) The ability to see in low light conditions <br />\n(d) The ability to see moving objects  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5850, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which chart is most commonly used for visual acuity tests? <br />\n(a) Ishihara chart <br />\n(b) Snellen chart<br />\n (c) LogMAR chart <br />\n(d) Jaeger chart   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5851, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does 20/20 vision indicate? <br />\n(a) Perfect vision <br />\n(b) The ability to see clearly at 20 feet what should normally be seen at 20 feet <br />\n(c) The ability to see clearly at 20 feet what should normally be seen at 200 feet <br />\n(d) The ability to see clearly at 200 feet what should normally be seen at 20 feet<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5852, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of a visual acuity test? <br />\n(a) To test color vision <br />\n(b) To diagnose glaucoma <br />\n(c) To measure the clarity of vision <br />\n(d) To test peripheral vision<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5853, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is visual acuity typically expressed? <br />\n(a) As a percentage <br />\n(b) As a ratio <br />\n(c) In diopters <br />\n(d) In nanometers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5854, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Who developed the Snellen chart? <br />\n(a) Dr. Hermann Snellen <br />\n(b) Dr. Samuel Jaeger <br />\n(c) Dr. Shinobu Ishihara <br />\n(d) Dr. Edmund Landolt   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5855, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a common visual acuity test? <br />\n(a) Snellen test <br />\n(b) LogMAR test <br />\n(c) Jaeger test <br />\n(d) Ishihara test  <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5856, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is a visual acuity test typically performed? <br />\n(a) The patient reads letters on a chart from a distance <br />\n(b) The patient distinguishes between different colors <br />\n(c) The patient identifies shapes in their peripheral vision <br />\n(d) The patient follows a moving light with their eyes  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5857, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a urine test? <br />\n(a) To measure blood pressure <br />\n(b) To check for abnormalities in the urine <br />\n(c) To assess heart function <br />\n(d) To test lung capacity  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5858, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following substances is NOT typically measured in a routine urine test? <br />\n(a) Glucose <br />\n(b) Protein <br />\n(c) White blood cells <br />\n(d) Cholesterol   <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5859, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What might the presence of protein in the urine indicate? <br />\n(a) Dehydration <br />\n(b) Kidney disease <br />\n(c) Lung infection <br />\n(d) Heart disease  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5860, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following urine tests can help diagnose a urinary tract infection (UTI)? <br />\n(a) Urine glucose test <br />\n(b) Urine protein test <br />\n(c) Urine culture <br />\n(d) Urine pH test<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5861, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does a high level of glucose in the urine typically indicate? <br />\n(a) Liver disease <br />\n(b) Diabetes <br />\n(c) Heart failure <br />\n(d) Anemia  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5862, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal color of urine in a healthy person? <br />\n(a) Red <br />\n(b) Dark brown <br />\n(c) Clear to pale yellow <br />\n(D) Blue   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5863, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which test is commonly used to measure the concentration of particles in the urine? <br />\n(a) Urine culture <br />\n(b) Urine specific gravity test <br />\n(c) Urine ketone test <br />\n(d) Urine bilirubin test      <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5864, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the presence of ketones in the urine typically indicate? <br />\n(a) Dehydration <br />\n(b) Infection <br />\n(c) The body is breaking down fat for energy <br />\n(d) Kidney stones  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5865, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What can cause urine to appear red or pink? <br />\n(a) Dehydration <br />\n(b) Eating certain foods like beets<br />\n (c) High protein intake <br />\n(d) Diabetes <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5866, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following might be indicated by a high pH level in the urine? <br />\n(a) Diabetes <br />\n(b) Urinary tract infection <br />\n(c) High protein diet <br />\n(d) Liver disease  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5867, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main purpose of performing a breast self-examination (BSE)? <br />\n(a) To detect any changes or abnormalities in the breasts <br />\n(B) To diagnose breast cancer <br />\n(C) To measure breast size <br />\n(d) To enhance breast shape<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5868, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When is the best time to perform a breast self-examination? <br />\n(a) During menstruation <br />\n(b) A few days before menstruation<br />\n(c) A few days after menstruation ends <br />\n(d) Any time of the month  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5869, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a recommended position for performing a breast self-examination? <br />\n(a) Standing in front of a mirror <br />\n(b) Lying down <br />\n(c) Sitting down <br />\n(d) In the shower <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5870, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should you look for when performing a breast self-examination? <br />\n(a) Changes in skin texture, such as dimpling <br />\n(b) Unexplained pain in the breast or nipple <br />\n(c) Lumps or thickened areas <br />\n(d) All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5871, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If you find a lump during a breast self-examination, what should you do? <br />\n(a) Ignore it, as it is probably nothing <br />\n(b) Wait a few months to see if it changes <br />\n(c) Schedule an appointment with a healthcare provider <br />\n(d) Try to diagnose it yourself using online resources <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:54:03', '2024-07-16 14:54:03'),
(5872, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is the primary function of hemoglobin?<br />\n (a) Transporting nutrients<br />\n(b)Transporting oxygen<br />\n(c) Producing white blood cells<br />\n(d) Clotting blood   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5873, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which method is most commonly used for hemoglobin estimation in clinical laboratories? <br />\n(a) Sahli?s method <br />\n(b) Hematocrit method <br />\n(c) Cyanmethemoglobin method <br />\n(d) Western blotting <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5874, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range of hemoglobin for adult males? <br />\n(a) 10.5 to 12.5 g/dL <br />\n(b) 13.8 to 17.2 g/dL <br />\n(c) 18.5 to 20.5 g/dL<br />\n(d) 21.0 to 23.0 g/dL <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5875, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range of hemoglobin for adult females? <br />\n(a) 9.0 to 11.0 g/dL <br />\n(b) 11.5 to 13.5 g/dL <br />\n(c) 12.1 to 15.1 g/dL <br />\n(d) 15.5 to 17.5 g/dL <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5876, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is anemia? <br />\n(a) A condition of high blood sugar levels <br />\n(b) A condition characterized by a deficiency in the number or quality of red blood cells or hemoglobin (c) A condition where blood clotting is impaired <br />\n(d) A condition of high white blood cell count<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5877, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which instrument is commonly used to measure hemoglobin concentration in blood?<br />\n(a) Microscope <br />\n(b) Hemoglobinometer <br />\n(c) Centrifuge <br />\n(d) Autoclave   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5878, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important to estimate hemoglobin levels in patients? <br />\n(a) To diagnose and monitor liver function <br />\n(b) To diagnose and monitor conditions like anemia and polycythemia <br />\n(c) To determine blood clotting ability <br />\n(d) To measure kidney function<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5879, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first step in managing a minor wound? <br />\n(a) Apply antibiotic ointment <br />\n(b) Clean the wound with water <br />\n(c) Cover the wound with a bandage <br />\n(d) Take pain medication<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5880, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of wound is characterized by the skin being torn or jagged? <br />\n(a) Abrasion <br />\n(b) Laceration <br />\n(c) Puncture <br />\n(d) Contusion   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5881, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of a wound dressing? <br />\n(a) To decorate the wound <br />\n(b) To keep the wound dry <br />\n(c) To protect the wound from infection <br />\n(d) To help the wound bleed more<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5882, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of wound is most likely to require stitches?<br />\n(a) Superficial abrasion<br />\n(b) Minor laceration <br />\n(c) Deep cut with jagged edges <br />\n(d) Small puncture wound  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5883, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a sign of infection in a wound? <br />\n(a) Decreased swelling <br />\n(b) Clear, odorless drainage <br />\n(c) Redness and warmth around the wound <br />\n(d) Itching    <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5884, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the best way to control bleeding from a wound? <br />\n(a) Apply ice directly to the wound <br />\n(b) Elevate the wound above heart level <br />\n(c) Apply direct pressure to the wound <br />\n(d) Leave the wound open to air<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5885, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why should you avoid using hydrogen peroxide on a wound? <br />\n(a) It doesn\'t clean the wound <br />\n(b) It can damage the tissue and delay healing <br />\n(c) It causes excessive bleeding<br />\n (d) It is not readily available<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5886, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following wounds is caused by a sharp object like a nail or needle? <br />\n(a) Laceration <br />\n(b) Abrasion <br />\n(c) Puncture <br />\n(d) Contusion   <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5887, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main characteristic of a chronic wound? <br />\n(a) Heals within a few days <br />\n(b) Shows no sign of healing after 2-4 weeks <br />\n(c) Bleeds profusely <br />\n(d) Causes intense pain immediately <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5888, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For which type of wound is tetanus prophylaxis most important? <br />\n(a) Clean, superficial cut <br />\n(b) Laceration with minimal bleeding <br />\n(c) Deep puncture wound, especially from a dirty object <br />\n(d) Minor abrasion  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5889, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary goal of routine immunization? <br />\n(a) To diagnose diseases <br />\n(b) To treat diseases <br />\n(c) To prevent diseases <br />\n(d) To alleviate symptoms <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5890, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following diseases can be prevented by the DTaP vaccine? <br />\n(a) Diphtheria, Tetanus, Pertussis <br />\n(b) Dengue, Typhoid, Anthrax <br />\n(c) Diabetes, Thyroiditis, Asthma <br />\n(d) Diarrhea, Tuberculosis, Anemia<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5891, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what age is the first dose of the MMR vaccine typically given? <br />\n(a) At birth <br />\n(b) 6 months <br />\n(c) 12-15 months <br />\n(d) 18 months  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5892, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following vaccines is given to prevent rotavirus infection? <br />\n(a) IPV <br />\n(b) Rotavirus vaccine <br />\n(c) Hib <br />\n(d) Hepatitis B   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5893, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Hepatitis B vaccine is typically administered  <br />\n(a) Once at age 10 <br />\n(b) In three doses starting at birth <br />\n(c) Annually <br />\n(d) Only if there is an outbreak<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5894, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which vaccine is recommended for preventing cervical cancer? <br />\n(a) MMR <br />\n(b) Hepatitis A <br />\n(c) HPV <br />\n(d) Varicella  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5895, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a contraindication for live vaccines?  <br />\n(a) Mild fever <br />\n(b) Current antibiotic use <br />\n(c) Pregnancy <br />\n(d) Mild asthma  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5896, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The term \"herd immunity\" refers to: <br />\n(a) Immunity developed from surviving an infection <br />\n(b) Immunity resulting from vaccination <br />\n(c) Protection from disease when a large portion of the population is immune <br />\n(d) Immunity passed from mother to child <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5897, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How often is the influenza vaccine recommended for most people? <br />\n(a) Every 5 years <br />\n(b) Every 2 years<br />\n (c) Annually <br />\n(d) Once in a lifetime  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5898, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which vaccine is administered to protect against Haemophilus influenzae type b? <br />\n(a) Hepatitis B <br />\n(b) Hib <br />\n(c) DTaP <br />\n(d) MMR <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5899, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended age for the first dose of the Varicella (chickenpox) vaccine? <br />\n(a) At birth <br />\n(b) 6 months <br />\n(c) 12-15 months <br />\n(d) 5 years <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5900, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common side effect of vaccines? <br />\n(a) Severe allergic reaction <br />\n(b) Mild fever <br />\n(c) Chronic illness <br />\n(d) Fractures  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5901, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pneumococcal vaccine protects against infections caused by_______<br />\n (a) Staphylococcus aureus <br />\n(b) Streptococcus pneumoniae <br />\n(c) Haemophilus influenzae <br />\n(d) Mycobacterium tuberculosis  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5902, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which organization provides immunization schedules and guidelines in the United States? <br />\n(a) World Health Organization (WHO) <br />\n(b) Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)  <br />\n(c) American Medical Association (AMA) <br />\n(d) National Institutes of Health (NIH)  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5903, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What type of vaccine is the polio vaccine (IPV)? <br />\n(a) Live attenuated <br />\n(b) Inactivated <br />\n(c) Subunit <br />\n(d) Toxoid<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5904, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following vaccines is administered to adolescents to prevent meningococcal disease? <br />\n(a) Hepatitis A <br />\n(b) Meningococcal conjugate vaccine <br />\n(c) Rotavirus vaccine <br />\n(d) Tdap <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5905, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what age is the first dose of the Hepatitis A vaccine recommended? <br />\n(a) At birth <br />\n(b) 6 months <br />\n(c) 12-23 months <br />\n(d) 5 years  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5906, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many doses of the HPV vaccine are recommended for adolescents starting the series before their 15th birthday? <br />\n(a) 1 dose <br />\n(b) 2 doses <br />\n(c) 3 doses <br />\n(d) 4 doses  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5907, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which vaccine is given to prevent tetanus, diphtheria, and whooping cough in adults? <br />\n(a) DTaP <br />\n(b) MMR <br />\n(c) Tdap <br />\n(d) Varicella   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5908, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended site for administering intramuscular vaccines in infants? <br />\n(a) Deltoid muscle <br />\n(b) Vastus lateralis muscle <br />\n(c) Gluteal muscle <br />\n(d) Biceps muscle   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5909, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary cause of tooth decay? <br />\n(a) Saliva <br />\n(b) Plaque <br />\n(c) Fluoride <br />\n(d) Water <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5910, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is the best time to brush your teeth? <br />\n(a) Right after every meal <br />\n(b) before breakfast and before bed <br />\n(c) Once a day, anytime <br />\n(d) Only when they feel dirty<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5911, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What mineral in water and toothpaste helps to strengthen tooth enamel? <br />\n(a) Calcium <br />\n(b) Iron <br />\n(c) Fluoride <br />\n(d) Potassium <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5912, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How often should you visit the dentist for a routine check-up?  <br />\n(a) Once a year <br />\n(b) Every six months <br />\n(c) Only when you have a toothache <br />\n(d) Every two years  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5913, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following foods is least likely to cause tooth decay? <br />\n(a) Candy <br />\n(b) Soda <br />\n(c) Cheese <br />\n(d) Cookies  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5914, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended duration for brushing your teeth? <br />\n(a) 30 seconds <br />\n(b) 1 minute <br />\n(c) 2 minutes <br />\n(d) 5 minutes  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5915, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is gingivitis? <br />\n(a) A type of toothpaste <br />\n(b) Inflammation of the gums <br />\n(c) A type of dental filling <br />\n(d) None of the above   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5916, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the function of dental floss? <br />\n(a) To whiten teeth <br />\n(b) To remove plaque and food particles between teeth <br />\n(c) To freshen breath <br />\n(d) To polish teeth <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(5917, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a symptom of gum disease?<br />\n(a) Swollen and bleeding gums <br />\n(b) White spots on teeth<br />\n (c) Sensitive teeth <br />\n(d) Bad breath  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5918, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is it important to limit sugary foods and drinks for oral health? <br />\n(a) They stain the teeth<br />\n (b) They can cause cavities <br />\n(c) They make the gums sensitive<br />\n (d) They have no impact on oral health  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5919, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of the oral route of drug administration? <br />\n(a) Injection <br />\n(b) Inhalation <br />\n(c) Tablet <br />\n(d) Topical cream  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5920, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration involves injecting a drug directly into a vein? <br />\n(a) Intramuscular <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Subcutaneous <br />\n(d) Intradermal  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5921, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration is commonly used for insulin delivery? <br />\n(a) Intramuscular <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Subcutaneous <br />\n(d) Inhalation  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5922, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary advantage of the transdermal route of administration? <br />\n(a) Rapid onset of action <br />\n(b) Easy to administer<br />\n (c) Bypasses the digestive system <br />\n(d) Suitable for large doses <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5923, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration is typically used for vaccines? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intramuscular <br />\n(c) Inhalation <br />\n(d) Transdermal  <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5924, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following routes of administration provides the fastest drug action? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Subcutaneous <br />\n(d) Intramuscular  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5925, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the route of administration for drugs delivered through a nebulizer? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Inhalation <br />\n(d) Topical  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5926, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration involves placing a drug under the tongue for absorption? <br />\n(a) Buccal <br />\n(b) Sublingual <br />\n(c) Oral <br />\n(d) Subcutes <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5927, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which route of administration involves applying medication directly to the skin? <br />\n(a) Oral <br />\n(b) Intravenous <br />\n(c) Topical <br />\n(d) Inhalation  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5928, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary advantages of the rectal route of administration? <br />\n(a) Pleasant taste <br />\n(b) Rapid absorption <br />\n(c) Bypasses the first-pass metabolism <br />\n(d) Suitable for all types of medications  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5929, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common symptom of a scorpion sting? <br />\n(a) Intense pain at the sting site <br />\n(b) High fever <br />\n(c) Severe headache <br />\n(d) Nausea and vomiting  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5930, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the first step you should take if bitten by a snake? <br />\n(a) Apply ice to the bite <br />\n(b) Suck out the venom <br />\n(c) Keep the affected limb immobilized and below heart level <br />\n(d) Give the victim water to drink  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5931, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of snake bite is most dangerous? <br />\n(a) Non-venomous snake bite <br />\n(b) Venomous snake bite <br />\n(c) Dry bite (no venom injected)<br />\n (d) Snake bite on a thick-skinned area  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5932, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a potential complication of a scorpion sting? <br />\n(a) Anaphylaxis <br />\n(b) Rabies <br />\n(c) Tetanus <br />\n(d) Hemorrhagic fever  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5933, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary treatment for a venomous snake bite? <br />\n(a) Antivenom <br />\n(b) Antibiotics <br />\n(c) Painkillers <br />\n(d) Antihistamines  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5934, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which symptom is NOT commonly associated with a venomous snake bite? <br />\n(a) Swelling and bruising around the bite <br />\n(b) Excessive sweating <br />\n(c) Blurred vision <br />\n(d) Hair loss  <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5935, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can you prevent scorpion stings when traveling in areas where they are common? <br />\n(a) Wear thick-soled shoes and shake out clothes before wearing <br />\n(b) Avoid drinking tap water <br />\n(c) Always carry a flashlight <br />\n(d) Use insect repellent  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5936, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should you avoid doing after a snake bite? <br />\n(a) Washing the bite area with soap and water <br />\n(b) Using a tourniquet above the bite site <br />\n(c) Keeping the victim calm and still <br />\n(d) Seeking medical help immediately  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5937, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which region is most commonly associated with dangerous scorpions? <br />\n(a) Arctic <br />\n(b) Deserts and tropical regions <br />\n(c) Coastal areas <br />\n(d) Rainforests  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5938, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a sign that you should seek medical attention for a scorpion sting? <br />\n(a) Mild itching at the sting site<br />\n (b) Severe pain that spreads from the sting site <br />\n(c) No pain or symptoms after the sting <br />\n(d) Redness that fades quickly <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5939, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a cold chain system primarily used for? <br />\n(a) Transporting non-perishable goods <br />\n(b) Storing dry foods <br />\n(c) Keeping perishable products at required temperatures <br />\n(d) Preserving canned foods   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5940, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a component of the cold chain system? <br />\n(a) Refrigerated storage <br />\n(b) Dry warehouses <br />\n(c) Refrigerated transportation <br />\n(d) Temperature monitoring devices <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5941, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What temperature range is typically maintained for frozen products in a cold chain? <br />\n(a) 0?C to 4?C <br />\n(b) -10?C to 0?C <br />\n(c) -18?C or lower <br />\n(d) 5?C to 10?C   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5942, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Why is temperature monitoring crucial in a cold chain system? <br />\n(a) To ensure product safety and quality <br />\n(b) To reduce transportation costs<br />\n (c) To increase shelf life of non-perishable goods <br />\n(d) To maintain ambient warehouse conditions <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5943, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which technology is often used to monitor temperature in cold chain logistics? <br />\n(a) Barcodes <br />\n(b) GPS tracking <br />\n(c) RFID sensors <br />\n(d) QR codes   <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5944, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the main purpose of a refrigerated truck in the cold chain system? <br />\n(a) To transport goods at room temperature <br />\n(b) To minimize transportation time <br />\n(c) To maintain a specific temperature during transport <br />\n(d) To maximize storage capacity <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5945, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which industry heavily relies on the cold chain system? <br />\n(a) Electronics <br />\n(b) Pharmaceuticals <br />\n(c) Textiles <br />\n(d) Construction  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5946, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a common consequence of a break in the cold chain? <br />\n(a) Increase in product value <br />\n(b) Extended product shelf life<br />\n(c) Degradation or spoilage of products <br />\n(d) Improved product safety  <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5947, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best describes \"last mile delivery\" in the context of the cold chain? <br />\n(a) The initial stage of product transportation <br />\n(b) The transportation from distribution center to final destination <br />\n(c) The packaging process of cold chain products <br />\n(d) The storage phase at the manufacturer\'s facility  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5948, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the role of insulated containers in a cold chain system? <br />\n(a) To reduce transportation costs<br />\n (b) To protect products from physical damage <br />\n(c) To maintain temperature during transit <br />\n(d) To enhance product packaging   <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5949, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is visual acuity? <br />\n(a) The ability to distinguish colors<br />\n (b) The sharpness of vision <br />\n(c) The ability to see in low light conditions <br />\n(d) The ability to see moving objects  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5950, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which chart is most commonly used for visual acuity tests? <br />\n(a) Ishihara chart <br />\n(b) Snellen chart<br />\n (c) LogMAR chart <br />\n(d) Jaeger chart   <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5951, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does 20/20 vision indicate? <br />\n(a) Perfect vision <br />\n(b) The ability to see clearly at 20 feet what should normally be seen at 20 feet <br />\n(c) The ability to see clearly at 20 feet what should normally be seen at 200 feet <br />\n(d) The ability to see clearly at 200 feet what should normally be seen at 20 feet<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5952, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of a visual acuity test? <br />\n(a) To test color vision <br />\n(b) To diagnose glaucoma <br />\n(c) To measure the clarity of vision <br />\n(d) To test peripheral vision<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
(5953, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'CLINICAL SKILLS', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is visual acuity typically expressed? <br />\n(a) As a percentage <br />\n(b) As a ratio <br />\n(c) In diopters <br />\n(d) In nanometers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-16 14:55:13', '2024-07-16 14:55:13'),
