(6393, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is commonly used to treat bacterial infections?<br />\na) Amoxicillin<br />\nb) Diphenhydramine<br />\nc) Lorazepam<br />\nd) Citalopram<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6394, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following medications is commonly used as a pain reliever and anti-inflammatory?<br />\na) Naproxen<br />\nb) Duloxetine<br />\nc) Propranolol<br />\nd) Lorazepam<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6395, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term for the minimum effective dose of a drug?<br />\na) ED50<br />\nb) LD50<br />\nc) EC50<br />\nd) Therapeutic index<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6396, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a type of drug interaction?<br />\na) Antagonism <br />\nb) Synergism<br />\nc) Agonism<br />\nd) Additive effect<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6397, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term for the process by which drugs are removed from the body?<br />\na) Excretion<br />\nb) Metabolism<br />\nc) Absorption<br />\nd) Distribution<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6398, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following drugs is an example of a competitive antagonist?<br />\na) Atropine<br />\nb) Propranolol<br />\nc) Morphine<br />\nd) Aspirin<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6399, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term for the maximum effect that a drug can produce?<br />\na) Efficacy<br />\nb) Potency<br />\nc) Affinity<br />\nd) Ceiling effect<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6400, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a type of pharmacokinetic process where drugs are transported from the bloodstream into tissues?<br />\na) Distribution<br />\nb) Absorption<br />\nc) Metabolism<br />\nd) Excretion<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6401, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term for the study of the harmful effects of drugs?<br />\na) Toxicology<br />\nb) Pharmacogenomics<br />\nc) Pharmacokinetics<br />\nd) Pharmacotherapeutics<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6402, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following drugs is an example of a non-competitive antagonist?<br />\na) Haloperidol<br />\n b) Propranolol<br />\nc) Phentolamine<br />\nd) Ibuprofen<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6403, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term for the time it takes for the plasma concentration of a drug to decrease by half?<br />\na) Half-life<br />\nb) Elimination rate constant<br />\nc) Volume of distribution<br />\nd) Clearance<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6404, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a type of drug metabolism?<br />\na) All of the above<br />\nb) Oxidation<br />\nc) Hydrolysis<br />\nd) Glucuronidation<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6405, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the term for the study of the relationship between drug dose and response?<br />\na) Dose-response curve<br />\n b) Pharmacodynamics<br />\nc) Pharmacotherapeutics<br />\nd) Pharmacokinetics<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6406, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an example of a drug that undergoes first-pass metabolism?<br />\na) Propranol<br />\nb) Ceftriaxone<br />\nc) Morphine<br />\nd) Nitroglycerin<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6407, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CLASS = ?, DRUG NAME = Promethazine, INDICATION = To prevent or suppress vomiting<br />\n<br />\na) Anti-emetics<br />\n        b) Antimalaria<br />\n        c) NSAIDs<br />\n        d) Anti-helminthics<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6408, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CLASS = Non-Opiod Anagelsic, DRUG NAME = ?, INDICATION = Relieves pain by acting on the CNS without significantly altering concsioness<br />\n<br />\n a) Naproxen<br />\n b) Xylometazoline<br />\n c) Calsium<br />\n d) Tetracycline<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6409, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CLASS = Anti-infective, DRUG NAME = Vancomycin, INDICATION = ?<br />\n<br />\na) Target foreign organism while sparing the host cell<br />\nb) Dissolve characteristics cells<br />\nc) Mob up cells<br />\nd) Bind to produce free radicals<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(6410, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CLASS = ?, DRUG NAME = Ivermectin, INDICATION = Parasitic roundworm treatment<br />\na) Anti-helminthics<br />\nb) Opiod<br />\nc) Antimalaria<br />\nd) Anti-infective<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6411, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CLASS = Antimalaria, DRUG NAME = ?, INDICATION = Suppress protozoan caused by plasmodium<br />\na) Dihydroartemisin<br />\n b) Ivermectin<br />\nc) Oxitocin<br />\nd) Paracetamol<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6412, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion are _______ principles?<br />\n    a. Pharmacokinetic principles<br />\n    b. Pharmadynamic principles<br />\n    c. Pharmacology principles<br />\n    d. Toxicology principles <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6413, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An abnormal reactivity to a chemical that is peculiar to a given individual which could be an abnormally exaggerated response or an abnormal lack of response is called?<br />\n    a. Idiosyncrasy<br />\n    b. Drug abuse<br />\n    c. Adverse drug reaction<br />\n    d. Drug relapse<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6414, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Derived from natural sources but modified through chemical processes are --------?<br />\na) Semi-synthetic<br />\nb) Synthetic<br />\nc) Alternative<br />\nd) Synergic<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6415, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The first discovered antibiotic is -------?<br />\na) Peniciline <br />\nb) Ceftriaxone<br />\nc) Morphine<br />\nd) Oxycodone<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6416, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The route of administration of drug by injection under the skin is?<br />\na) Subcutaneous<br />\nb) Intravenous<br />\nc) Intramuscular<br />\nd) Sublingual<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6417, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">_______ and _____for the bases of drug classification into form<br />\na) Physical presentation and the rout of administration<br />\nb) Manufacturing company and location<br />\nc) Mass and Weight<br />\nd) Physical presentation and indication<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6418, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are examples of Semi-solid form of drug classification EXCEPT<br />\na) Syrups<br />\nb) Creams<br />\nc) Ointments<br />\nd) Gels<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6419, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The focus on drugs that shows their individual actions on different part of cardiac and vascular system is?<br />\na) Cardiovascular Pharmacology<br />\nb) Clinical Pharmacology<br />\nc) Mobile Pharmacology<br />\nd) Vascular Pahrmacology<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6420, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are class of diuretics EXCEPT<br />\na) Bismuth Subsalicylate<br />\nb) Furosemide<br />\nc) Hydrohlorothiazide<br />\nd) Amiloride<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6421, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">GIT means?<br />\na) Gastro intestinal track<br />\nb) Gastrin intestine track<br />\nc) Gastro intestine track<br />\nd) Gastro intetina truck<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6422, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">First pass metabolism is associated with which of the following route of administration?<br />\na) PO<br />\nb) IV<br />\nc) IM<br />\nd) Transdermal<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6423, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The medical situation when a particular drug should not be administered is referred to as?<br />\na) Contraindication<br />\nb) Side effect<br />\nc) Drug allergy<br />\nd) Adverse effect<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6424, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The propriety drug name supplied by a pharmaceutical company is also referred to as the?<br />\na) Trade name<br />\nb) Generic name<br />\nc) Chemical name<br />\nd) Over the counter name<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6425, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A drug that has the potential for abuse and is regulated by the Drug Enforcement agency is classified as a?<br />\na) Controlled substance<br />\nb) OTC<br />\nc) Non proprietary drug<br />\nd) Essential medicine<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6426, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Medication that does not require a physician service to obtain is referred to as?<br />\na) OTC<br />\nb) Brand<br />\nc) Non-proprietary<br />\nd) Generic<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6427, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The time a drug continues to produce its effect is its _______?<br />\na) onset of action<br />\nb) Ceiling effect<br />\nc) ED50<br />\nd) Duration of action<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6428, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The drug administration route demonstrating the slowest onset of action is?<br />\na) Transdermal<br />\nb) Intramuscular<br />\nc) Sublingual<br />\nd) Intravenous<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6429, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In other for drug to cross the blood-brain barrier, they must be?<br />\na) Lipid soluble<br />\nb) Water soluble<br />\nc) Ionized<br />\nd) Charged<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6430, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">First pass metabolism refers to the metabolism of drug in the?<br />\na) Liver<br />\nb) Heart<br />\nc) Blood vessel<br />\nd) Kidney<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6431, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Flagyl is an example of?<br />\na) Metronidazole<br />\nb) Ceftriaxone<br />\nc) Morphine<br />\nd) Abendazole<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:42:51', '2024-07-17 14:42:51'),
(6432, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The study of the physiological or biological effect that varying interaction of drugs have on the body over time is<br />\na. Pharmacodynamics<br />\nb. Pharmacology<br />\nc. Pharmacokinetics<br />\nd. Toxicology<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6433, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are the significance of Pharmacology to community health except <br />\na. Create independence in care delivery among community health workers<br />\nb. Scale up the treatment of health problems in the community either independently or as part of preoperative management <br />\nc. Employs various classes of drugs based on specific requirement to achieve therapeutic result <br />\nd. Equip dental professionals with oral health maintenance<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6434, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The uptake of nutrients and drugs from the GI tract is?<br />\n    a. Absorption<br />\n    b. Adsorption<br />\n    c. Dissolution<br />\n    d. Digestion<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6435, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Drug management is necessary because<br />\na. Drugs are part of the link between the patient and the health services<br />\nb. Drugs are health workers responsibility alone<br />\nc. The availability or absence will contribute have little or no impact on health<br />\nd. Poor drug management is a critical issues only in private sector and not public sector<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
