(6523, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The medical situation when a particular drug should not be administered is referred to as?<br />\na) Contraindication<br />\nb) Side effect<br />\nc) Drug allergy<br />\nd) Adverse effect<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6524, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The propriety drug name supplied by a pharmaceutical company is also referred to as the?<br />\na) Trade name<br />\nb) Generic name<br />\nc) Chemical name<br />\nd) Over the counter name<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6525, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A drug that has the potential for abuse and is regulated by the Drug Enforcement agency is classified as a?<br />\na) Controlled substance<br />\nb) OTC<br />\nc) Non proprietary drug<br />\nd) Essential medicine<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6526, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Medication that does not require a physician service to obtain is referred to as?<br />\na) OTC<br />\nb) Brand<br />\nc) Non-proprietary<br />\nd) Generic<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6527, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The time a drug continues to produce its effect is its _______?<br />\na) onset of action<br />\nb) Ceiling effect<br />\nc) ED50<br />\nd) Duration of action<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6528, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The drug administration route demonstrating the slowest onset of action is?<br />\na) Transdermal<br />\nb) Intramuscular<br />\nc) Sublingual<br />\nd) Intravenous<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6529, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In other for drug to cross the blood-brain barrier, they must be?<br />\na) Lipid soluble<br />\nb) Water soluble<br />\nc) Ionized<br />\nd) Charged<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6530, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">First pass metabolism refers to the metabolism of drug in the?<br />\na) Liver<br />\nb) Heart<br />\nc) Blood vessel<br />\nd) Kidney<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6531, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PHARMACOLOGY', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Flagyl is an example of?<br />\na) Metronidazole<br />\nb) Ceftriaxone<br />\nc) Morphine<br />\nd) Abendazole<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 14:43:40', '2024-07-17 14:43:40'),
(6532, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Following is true about the tympanic membrane EXCEPT:<br />\na. It is rounded in shape.<br />\nb. It is placed obliquely forming acute angle with meatus anteriorly and obtuseone posteriorly.<br />\nc. The normal tympanic membrane is pearly white in color.<br />\nd. The light reflex is due to the concave position of the membrane.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6533, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following is true about the Eustachian tube EXCEPT:<br />\na. It ends 1 em behind the posterior end of the inferior turbinate.<br />\nb. The upper 1/3 is bony while the lower 2/3 is fibrocartilagenous.<br />\nc.It is normally opened at rest.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6534, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Ear washing is not contraindicated in traumatic perforation of the drum.<br />\nb. Pathological perforation of the drum occurs at any site while traumatic onesoccurs in pars tensa only.<br />\nc. In ear washing, the sterile nozzle of the syringe is directed to the drumdirectly.<br />\nd.Ear washing is indicated in the presence of fistula between the middle& inner <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6535, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pain on mastication is present in:<br />\na.Acute mastoiditis.<br />\nb. Otosclerosis.<br />\nc.Furunculosis of the external ear.<br />\nd. Allergic otitis externa<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6536, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Bloody discharge from the ear occurs in:<br />\na.Fracture base of the skull<br />\nb. Glomus jugular tumor.<br />\nc. All of the above<br />\nd. Rupture drum<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6537, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most common cause of deafness in children:<br />\na. Acute otitis media.<br />\nb. Secretory otitis media<br />\nc. Chronic otitis media<br />\nd. Cholesteatoma<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6538, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In traumatic ossicular disruption, all is true EXCEPT:<br />\na. The audiogram shows 55 dB loss.<br />\nb. Separation of the icudo-stapedial joint is the commonest lesion.<br />\nc.There is bulging drum<br />\nd. C.Tsean is indicated<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6539, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Fever in lateral sinus thrombosis is:<br />\na. Intermittent<br />\nb. Remittent<br />\nc. Low grade<br />\nd. High grade<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6540, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> Watery discharge from the ear occurs in all of the following EXCET:<br />\na. Cerebro-spinal otorrhoea<br />\nb. Parotid fistula<br />\nc. Acute otitis media<br />\nd. Endolymphatic sac surgery<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6541, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In Rinne\'s test:<br />\na. In perceptive deafness: air conduction is better than bone conduction.<br />\nb. In conductive deafness: air conduction is better than bone conduction.<br />\nc. In perceptive deafness: sound is heard better in the healthy ear. <br />\nd. In perceptive deafness: bone conduction is better than air conduction.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6542, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In Weber\'s test:<br />\na. In conductive deafness: sound is heard better in the diseased ear.<br />\nb. In conductive deafness:sound is heard better in the healthy ear.<br />\nc. . In perceptive deafness: bone conduction is better than air conduction.<br />\nd.In perceptive deafness: sound is heard better in the diseased ear.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6543, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Schwabach\'s test is:<br />\na. Comparison between air& bone conduction of the same ear.<br />\nb. Comparison of bone conduction of both ears at the same time.<br />\nc. Comparison of duration of bone conduction of the patient & the examiner.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6544, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following is true about pure tone audiometry EXCEPT:<br />\na. It gives the amount of the hearing loss in dB.<br />\nb. It gives the type of deafness.<br />\nc. It measures the sound emitted from the cochlea.<br />\nd. It helps in hearing aid selection.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6545, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following is true about impedance audiometry EXCEPT:<br />\na. It measures the pressure changes in the middle ear.<br />\nb. It measures fixation and dislocation of the ossicular chain.<br />\nc. It measures the patency of the Eustachian tube.<br />\nd. It measures the sound emitted from the cochlea.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6546, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In lesion of the facial nerve at the stylomastoid foramen, there is:<br />\na. L.M.N.L of the facial muscles.<br />\nb. No impairment of taste.<br />\nc. No impairment of salivation.<br />\nd. . All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6547, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In lesion of facial nerve at vertical part\'\"below the nerve of stapedius\"there is:<br />\na. Loss of taste.<br />\nb. Impairment of salivation.<br />\nc.Impairment of lacrimation.<br />\nd.Hyperacusis.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6548, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In lesion of the facial nerve at horizontal part, there is:<br />\na.Loss of taste.<br />\nb. Impairment of salivation.<br />\nc. All of the above..<br />\nd.Hyperacusis.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6549, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cause of Bell\'s palsy may be one of the following EXCEPT:<br />\na. Vascular ischemia.<br />\nb. Virus infection.<br />\nc. Bacterial infection.<br />\nd. Auto immune.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6550, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The early symptom of Bell\'s palsy is:<br />\na. Dropping of angle of the affected side.<br />\nb. Obliteration of the angle of the mouth.<br />\nc. Pain of acute onset behind the ear.<br />\nd. Inability to close the eye.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6551, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Intra cranial complications of chronic suppurative otitis media includes:<br />\na. Mastoiditis.<br />\nb.Meningitis.<br />\nc.Labyrinthitis.<br />\nd.Breast abscess.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6552, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Cranial complications of chronic suppurative otitis media includes:<br />\na.Mastoiditis.<br />\nb. Labyrinthitis.<br />\nc. Petrositis.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6553, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Extra cranial complications of chronic suppurative otitis media includes:<br />\na.Mastitis.<br />\nb. Bezold abscess.<br />\nc. Lateral sinus thrombosis.<br />\nd. Otiitis external.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6554, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CSF examination in case of meningitis shows:<br />\na.Protein diminished.<br />\nb. Sugar diminished.<br />\nc.Chloride diminished.<br />\nd. f.b.c&d.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6555, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All are correct about Meniere\'s disease EXCEPT:<br />\na. It is an endolymphatichydrops.<br />\nb. Males are more affected than females.<br />\nc.The type of deafness is conductive.<br />\nd. Decompression of the labyrinth is indicated if the vertiginous attack is crippling.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6556, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The aim of radical mastoidectomyis:<br />\na. To give safe ear.<br />\nb. To preserve hearing.<br />\nc. Reconstruct the ossicles.<br />\nd. Reconstruct the tympanic membrane.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6557, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The aim of modified radical mastoidectomy is:<br />\na. To give safe ear & to preserve hearing.<br />\nb. Reconstruct the ossicles.<br />\nc.Reconstruct the tympanic membrane.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6558, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media in the suppurative stage is:<br />\na.Dull aching.<br />\nb.Throbbing.<br />\nc.Boring.<br />\nd.Burning.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6559, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media in the catarrhal stage is:<br />\na.Dull aching.<br />\nb.Throbbing.<br />\nc.Boring.<br />\nd.Burning.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6560, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media is more severe at:<br />\na.Night.<br />\nb.Morning.<br />\nc.Mid-day.<br />\nd.All the day.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6561, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media disappear after:<br />\na.Bulging of the drum.<br />\nb. Perforation of the drum.<br />\nc. Congestion of the drum.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6562, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In malignant otitis externa all the following is true EXCEPT:<br />\na. It is common in old diabetic.<br />\nb. There may be facial paralysis.<br />\nc. The commonest organism is pseudomonas.<br />\nd. Mainly treated surgically.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6563, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The middle ear magnifies the sound:<br />\na. 20 times.<br />\nb. 22 times.<br />\nc. 200times.<br />\nd. 21 times.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6564, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The test of hearing in infant is:<br />\na. Rinne test.<br />\nb.Weber test.<br />\nc. Pure tone audiometry.<br />\nd.ABR\"Auditory Brain stem Response\".<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6565, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">ABR \"Auditory Brain stem Response\" is usd in:<br />\na. Test of hearing in malingering.<br />\nb. Test of hearing in retrochoclear lesion.<br />\nc. Detection of acoustic neuroma.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6566, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are the manifestations of temporal lobe abscess EXCEPT:<br />\na. Hemi paresis.<br />\nb. Aphasia.<br />\nc.Convulsivefits.<br />\nd. Vertigo.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6567, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In traumatic rupture of the drum,all are true EXCEPT:<br />\na. The main treatment is conservative.<br />\nb. Local ear drops are highly indicated.<br />\nc. It heals spontancously within 3 months.<br />\nd. It may be caused by longitudinal fracture of the temporal bone.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6568, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Conductive deafness is the main presentation of:<br />\na. Furunculosis of the external auditory canal.<br />\nb. Ear wax.<br />\nc.Haematomaauris.<br />\nd. Non of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6569, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Unilateral hearing loss with pulsating tinnitus is suggestive of:<br />\na.Otosclerosis.<br />\nb. Extradural abscess complicating CSOM.<br />\nc. Glomus tumor.<br />\nd. Acoustic neuroma.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6570, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most common vertigo is:<br />\na. Acoustic neuroma.<br />\nb.Ototoxicity.<br />\nc.Meniere\'s disease.<br />\nd. Benign paroxysmal positional vertigo.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6571, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A case of ear infection followed by headache, blurring of vision & vomiting is suggestive of:<br />\na.Mastoiditis.<br />\nb. Petrositis.<br />\nc.Labyrinthitis.<br />\nd. Brain abscess.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6572, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The commonest organism in malignant otitis externa:<br />\na. Streptococci.<br />\nb.Pneumococci.<br />\nc. Pseudomonas aeroginosa.<br />\nd. Moraxella catarrhalis.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6573, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The medial wall of the middle ear shows the following EXCEPT:<br />\na. The oval window.<br />\nb. The promontory.<br />\nc.The pyramid.<br />\nd. The lateral semicircular canal.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6574, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mixed hearing loss may be caused by one of the following:<br />\na.Otosclerosis.<br />\nb.Meniere\'s disease.<br />\nc. Ear wax.<br />\nd. Acoustic neuroma.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6575, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pulsating ear discharge may be found in:<br />\na. Extradural abscess.<br />\nb. Acute exacerbation of CSOM.<br />\nc. Acute otitis media with small perforation.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6576, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are tests of hearing sensitivity EXCEPT:<br />\na. Tuning fork tests.<br />\nb.Tympanometry.<br />\nc. Auditory Brain stem Response.<br />\nd. Pure tone audiometry.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6577, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All are truc about the Eustachian tube EXCEPT:<br />\na.It opens during swallowing.<br />\nb. It ventilates the middle ear.<br />\nc. It is wider& horizontal in children.<br />\nd. It opens in the oropharynx<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6578, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Equilibrium during angular \"rotational\" movement is the function of:<br />\na).The utricle.<br />\nb. The saccule.<br />\nc. The cochlea.<br />\nd. The semicircular canal.<br />\n\'</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6579, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most common cause of otitis media with effusion is:<br />\na. Inadequate treatment of acute otitis media.<br />\nb. Nasopharyngeal neoplasm.<br />\nc. Allergy.<br />\nd. Otitic barotraumas.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6580, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following drugs are ototoxic:<br />\na.Neomycin.<br />\nb. Gramycin.<br />\nc.Saliclates.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6581, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The inferior meatus receives the opening of:<br />\na. The maxillary sinus.<br />\nb. The anterior ethmoidal sinus.<br />\nc.The posterior ethmoidal sinus.<br />\nd.Nusolacrimal duct.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6582, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Perforation of bony part of the nasal septum occurs in:<br />\na. Sarcoidosis.<br />\nb. Rhinoscleroma.<br />\nc.Tuberculosis.<br />\nd.Syphilis.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6583, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Spontaneous recovery is usual in:<br />\na. Rhinosporodosis.<br />\nb. Sarcoidosis.<br />\nc.Tuberculosis.<br />\nd. Syphilis.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6584, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Eosinophils in great numbers in nasal secretion is a finding in:<br />\na. Atrophic rhinitis.<br />\nb. Chronic rhinitis.<br />\nc.Allergic rhinitis.<br />\nd. Acute rhinitis.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6585, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Sneezing is a prominent feature in:<br />\na.Atrophic rhinitis.<br />\nb. Chronic rhinitis.<br />\nc.Allergic rhinitis.<br />\nd.Acute rhinitis.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6586, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Unilateralmucopurulent& purulent nasal discharge may be due to:<br />\na. Unilateral sinusitis.<br />\nb. FB in the nose.<br />\nc. Non of them.<br />\nd. All of them.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6587, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are some general causes of epistaxis EXCEPT:<br />\na. Anemia.<br />\nb.Arterial hypertension.<br />\nc.Nasopharyngealangiofibroma.<br />\nd. Renal failure.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6588, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following drugs can cause epistaxis EXCEPT:<br />\na.Salicylates.<br />\nb. Anticoagulants.<br />\nc.Quinine.<br />\nd.Ampicllin.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6589, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The commonest cause of epistaxis in 50 years old man is:<br />\na.Hypertension.<br />\nb. Angiofibroma.<br />\nc.Allergic nasal polypi.<br />\nd. Antrochoanal polyp.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6590, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cause of secondary hemorrhage is:<br />\na. Wound sepsis.<br />\nb. Unprepared patient.<br />\nc. Injury of the pharyngeal muscle.<br />\nd. Rising of blood pressure with slipping ligature.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6591, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Fever in diphtheria is:<br />\na. High grade fever.<br />\nb. Low grade fever.<br />\nc.Remittent fever.<br />\nd. Intermittent fever.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6592, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pulse in diphtheria is:<br />\na. Weak rapid pulse.<br />\nb. Full bounding pulse.<br />\nc.Synchronous with the temperature.<br />\nd. Non synchronous with the temperature.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6593, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The causative agent of thrush stomatitis is:<br />\na.Borelivencenti.<br />\nb.Candidaalbicans.<br />\nc. Barr-epestin virus.<br />\nd. Streptococci.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6594, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Membranous tonsillitis may be due to : <br />\na.Diphtheria.<br />\nb. Acute follicular tonsillitis.<br />\nc. Infectious mononucleosis.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6595, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pharyngeal ulcer may be due to:<br />\na. Herpes simplex.<br />\nb. Herpes zoster.<br />\nc. TB.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6596, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pharyngeal ulcer may be duc to:<br />\na.Blood diseases.<br />\nb. Skin diseases(linchenplanus).<br />\nc. Toxic (heavy metals).<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6597, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The swelling in acute retropharyngeal abcess is:<br />\na. In the middle line.<br />\nb. Lateral to the middle line.<br />\nc. Appears from outside the neck.<br />\nd. Non of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6598, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Acute laryngeal abscess is characterized by all of the following EXCEPT:<br />\na.Occur most commonly in infants.<br />\nb. Involves the prevertebral space.<br />\nc. Usually oceurs with TB of the cervical vertebra.<br />\nd. Is seen inIateral X-ray of neck.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6599, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Stomatitis associated with skin lesions:<br />\na.Pemphigus.<br />\nb.Linchenplanus.<br />\nc. Lupus erthromatosis.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6600, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following metabolic disorder associated with stomatitis:<br />\na.Uremia.<br />\nb. DM.<br />\nc.Liver disease.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6601, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The outer ear is differentiated from the inner ear by <br />\nA. Pinna B. Middle ear C. Otitis media <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6602, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common cause of nosebleeds?<br />\nA. nose-picking B. nose mask C. none of the above  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6603, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most effective way to stop a nosebleed?<br />\nA. direct pinching B. direct blow C. nose picking<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6604, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What medicated spray can be used to help stop a bleed?<br />\nA. Ibuprofen spray B. afrin and other nasal sprays C. none of the above  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6605, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is function of the larynx<br />\na)It does not produce voice <br />\nb)It gives support to other related structures such as pharynx that serves aspassage way for air and food<br />\nc)It doesn\'t assist trachea which filter harmidifis air<br />\nd)Its safes traffic control for air and water<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6606, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the difference between a posterior and an anterior nosebleed, and why is this important?<br />\nA. There are most common and arise from the septum (middle wall) of the nose. <br />\nB. bleeding is usually responsive to direct pressure. <br />\nC. all of the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6607, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 3 year old has a bug lodged in his ear. He is screaming and combative. What can you do to help?<br />\nA. kill the bug inside the ear with solution. B. Remove the bug with forceps. C. Remove the bug with broom stick<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6608, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Following a fight, a 25years old male declines transport. He has a large swelling of the outer ear from a direct blow. What can you advise him about the need for treatment?<br />\nA. Hematomas of the outer ear will cause breakdown of the cartilage if they are not treated with an incision and expression of clot, then a pressure dressing. B. he should continue his journey. C. no need for any medication<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6609, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">His other ear has a 2cm laceration that communicates with the other side. Why is this more dangerous than on other parts of the body?<br />\nA.  As before, lacerations to the cartilage of the ear can lead to severe cosmetic defects unless the cartilage laceration is required. B. Movement of fluid across both sides. C. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6610, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The other contestant in this fight has a very swollen nose. It was bleeding, but this has stopped now. He also declines medical treatment. Why should he have his nose looked at?<br />\nA. it may require surgery. B. A septal hematoma can occur with nasal injuries due to contained local bleeding. C. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6611, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 2 year old has stuffed a bead into her nose. Does this present any danger to her? What will happen if this was unwitnessed or unrecognized?<br />\nA. Yes. B. No C. None<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6612, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Called to an assault, you find a moderately intoxicated patient complaining of jaw pain. He is holding two of his teeth in his hand. What should you do with the teeth?<br />\nA. Return the teeth firmly in their socket, if patient cooperate. B. preserves the teeth with saliva, saline solution or milk. C. all of the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6613, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Normal alignment of the teeth during biting, normal jaw opening and no pain to palpation (especially of the mentum or point of the chin) are all good signs. B. Instability of more than one tooth in a row is a sign of a more superficial jaw fracture (alveolar ridge fracture) and requires stabilization of the teeth. C. all of the above</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6614, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The patient states that he was choked during the fight. What is one of the best signs of laryngeal edema in these patients?<br />\nA. Voice changes are one of the best indicators of laryngeal edema, either from trauma or from medical causes. B. laryngeal laceration. C. Nose bleeding  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6615, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During your exam you find that the patient has a 2cm lac to the margin of his tongue. How should this be managed? <br />\nA. Direct pressure with gauze pads will usually control bleeding from tongue lacs.<br />\nB. cut the tongue off. C. Rinse the mouth with alcohol   <br />\n\'</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6616, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 9 year old has impaled his cheek with a pencil. The pencil is still sticking through his cheek on your arrival. What should you do? <br />\nA. Remove the pencil. B. Do not remove the pencil. C. shout and cry<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6617, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A patient with a toothache for several days now is having difficulty swallowing. His right face is swollen and tender. What do you need to worry about?  A. Occlusion and death. B. eating of food. C. smell</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6618, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Another patient is 24, has had a sore throat and fever for several days with fevers. She now also complains of difficulty swallowing. She looks distressed, and is spitting her secretions. What may be happening? <br />\nA. severe pharyngitis / tonsillitis. <br />\nB. mouth sore. <br />\nC. salty taste<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6619, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A four year old is having difficulty swallowing and perhaps breathing. The auntie states that the child has had a sore throat and fever for a few days. What is this child at risk for given his age and the history? A. epiglottitis B. Nebulizations. C. haematoma</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6620, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Called on an overdose, you attend a 54year man who drank lye in a suicide attempt. You examine his oropharynx and see no burns. How well does this rule out esophageal burns? A. Household bleach is not concentrated enough to produce burns. B. take a milky drink. C.no idea </p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6621, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The smallest bone is called?<br />\n  A. Stapes B malleus C Incus<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6622, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Olfactory nerve supply<br />\nA. Mouth B Nose C Eye<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(6623, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cochlea is located in <br />\nA. Middle ear B. Outer ear. C Inner ear<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6624, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Gingivitis is a disease that affect<br />\nA Tongue. B pharynx. C Gums and it structures<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6625, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Norma is<br />\nA Degeneration of oral cavity including bones. B Cancer of new born. C Normal face expression<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6626, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Organ for smell perception<br />\nA Nose. B Mouth. C Ear D. Sight<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6627, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Otitis media is a disease of the?<br />\nA outer ear. B Middle ear. C Pinna D. Inner ear<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6628, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The vagus nerve enervate all except<br />\nA Tongue. B Nasal cavity. C The ear. D Non of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6629, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pharyngitis<br />\nA Inflammation of the cochlea. B Inflammation of the throat. C Inflammation of the Mouth D. inflammation of the Ear<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6630, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">ENT means<br />\na) Ear, Noce and Throat<br />\nb)Ear,Nice and Table<br />\nc)Ear,Nose and Throat<br />\nd) Ear, Nase and Throat<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6631, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Diseases of the nose are the following except one<br />\na)Epitaxies<br />\nb)Tumor<br />\nc)Impaired olfactory apparatus infection<br />\nd)Epiglottis<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:44:34', '2024-07-17 17:44:34'),
(6632, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Following is true about the tympanic membrane EXCEPT:<br />\na. It is rounded in shape.<br />\nb. It is placed obliquely forming acute angle with meatus anteriorly and obtuseone posteriorly.<br />\nc. The normal tympanic membrane is pearly white in color.<br />\nd. The light reflex is due to the concave position of the membrane.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6633, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following is true about the Eustachian tube EXCEPT:<br />\na. It ends 1 em behind the posterior end of the inferior turbinate.<br />\nb. The upper 1/3 is bony while the lower 2/3 is fibrocartilagenous.<br />\nc.It is normally opened at rest.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6634, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Ear washing is not contraindicated in traumatic perforation of the drum.<br />\nb. Pathological perforation of the drum occurs at any site while traumatic onesoccurs in pars tensa only.<br />\nc. In ear washing, the sterile nozzle of the syringe is directed to the drumdirectly.<br />\nd.Ear washing is indicated in the presence of fistula between the middle& inner <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6635, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pain on mastication is present in:<br />\na.Acute mastoiditis.<br />\nb. Otosclerosis.<br />\nc.Furunculosis of the external ear.<br />\nd. Allergic otitis externa<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6636, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Bloody discharge from the ear occurs in:<br />\na.Fracture base of the skull<br />\nb. Glomus jugular tumor.<br />\nc. All of the above<br />\nd. Rupture drum<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6637, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most common cause of deafness in children:<br />\na. Acute otitis media.<br />\nb. Secretory otitis media<br />\nc. Chronic otitis media<br />\nd. Cholesteatoma<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6638, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In traumatic ossicular disruption, all is true EXCEPT:<br />\na. The audiogram shows 55 dB loss.<br />\nb. Separation of the icudo-stapedial joint is the commonest lesion.<br />\nc.There is bulging drum<br />\nd. C.Tsean is indicated<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6639, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Fever in lateral sinus thrombosis is:<br />\na. Intermittent<br />\nb. Remittent<br />\nc. Low grade<br />\nd. High grade<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6640, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> Watery discharge from the ear occurs in all of the following EXCET:<br />\na. Cerebro-spinal otorrhoea<br />\nb. Parotid fistula<br />\nc. Acute otitis media<br />\nd. Endolymphatic sac surgery<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6641, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In Rinne\'s test:<br />\na. In perceptive deafness: air conduction is better than bone conduction.<br />\nb. In conductive deafness: air conduction is better than bone conduction.<br />\nc. In perceptive deafness: sound is heard better in the healthy ear. <br />\nd. In perceptive deafness: bone conduction is better than air conduction.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6642, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In Weber\'s test:<br />\na. In conductive deafness: sound is heard better in the diseased ear.<br />\nb. In conductive deafness:sound is heard better in the healthy ear.<br />\nc. . In perceptive deafness: bone conduction is better than air conduction.<br />\nd.In perceptive deafness: sound is heard better in the diseased ear.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6643, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Schwabach\'s test is:<br />\na. Comparison between air& bone conduction of the same ear.<br />\nb. Comparison of bone conduction of both ears at the same time.<br />\nc. Comparison of duration of bone conduction of the patient & the examiner.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6644, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following is true about pure tone audiometry EXCEPT:<br />\na. It gives the amount of the hearing loss in dB.<br />\nb. It gives the type of deafness.<br />\nc. It measures the sound emitted from the cochlea.<br />\nd. It helps in hearing aid selection.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6645, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following is true about impedance audiometry EXCEPT:<br />\na. It measures the pressure changes in the middle ear.<br />\nb. It measures fixation and dislocation of the ossicular chain.<br />\nc. It measures the patency of the Eustachian tube.<br />\nd. It measures the sound emitted from the cochlea.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6646, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In lesion of the facial nerve at the stylomastoid foramen, there is:<br />\na. L.M.N.L of the facial muscles.<br />\nb. No impairment of taste.<br />\nc. No impairment of salivation.<br />\nd. . All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6647, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In lesion of facial nerve at vertical part\'\"below the nerve of stapedius\"there is:<br />\na. Loss of taste.<br />\nb. Impairment of salivation.<br />\nc.Impairment of lacrimation.<br />\nd.Hyperacusis.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6648, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In lesion of the facial nerve at horizontal part, there is:<br />\na.Loss of taste.<br />\nb. Impairment of salivation.<br />\nc. All of the above..<br />\nd.Hyperacusis.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6649, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cause of Bell\'s palsy may be one of the following EXCEPT:<br />\na. Vascular ischemia.<br />\nb. Virus infection.<br />\nc. Bacterial infection.<br />\nd. Auto immune.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6650, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The early symptom of Bell\'s palsy is:<br />\na. Dropping of angle of the affected side.<br />\nb. Obliteration of the angle of the mouth.<br />\nc. Pain of acute onset behind the ear.<br />\nd. Inability to close the eye.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6651, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Intra cranial complications of chronic suppurative otitis media includes:<br />\na. Mastoiditis.<br />\nb.Meningitis.<br />\nc.Labyrinthitis.<br />\nd.Breast abscess.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6652, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Cranial complications of chronic suppurative otitis media includes:<br />\na.Mastoiditis.<br />\nb. Labyrinthitis.<br />\nc. Petrositis.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6653, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Extra cranial complications of chronic suppurative otitis media includes:<br />\na.Mastitis.<br />\nb. Bezold abscess.<br />\nc. Lateral sinus thrombosis.<br />\nd. Otiitis external.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6654, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">CSF examination in case of meningitis shows:<br />\na.Protein diminished.<br />\nb. Sugar diminished.<br />\nc.Chloride diminished.<br />\nd. f.b.c&d.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6655, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All are correct about Meniere\'s disease EXCEPT:<br />\na. It is an endolymphatichydrops.<br />\nb. Males are more affected than females.<br />\nc.The type of deafness is conductive.<br />\nd. Decompression of the labyrinth is indicated if the vertiginous attack is crippling.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6656, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The aim of radical mastoidectomyis:<br />\na. To give safe ear.<br />\nb. To preserve hearing.<br />\nc. Reconstruct the ossicles.<br />\nd. Reconstruct the tympanic membrane.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6657, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The aim of modified radical mastoidectomy is:<br />\na. To give safe ear & to preserve hearing.<br />\nb. Reconstruct the ossicles.<br />\nc.Reconstruct the tympanic membrane.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6658, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media in the suppurative stage is:<br />\na.Dull aching.<br />\nb.Throbbing.<br />\nc.Boring.<br />\nd.Burning.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6659, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media in the catarrhal stage is:<br />\na.Dull aching.<br />\nb.Throbbing.<br />\nc.Boring.<br />\nd.Burning.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6660, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media is more severe at:<br />\na.Night.<br />\nb.Morning.<br />\nc.Mid-day.<br />\nd.All the day.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6661, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pain in acute suppurative otitis media disappear after:<br />\na.Bulging of the drum.<br />\nb. Perforation of the drum.<br />\nc. Congestion of the drum.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6662, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In malignant otitis externa all the following is true EXCEPT:<br />\na. It is common in old diabetic.<br />\nb. There may be facial paralysis.<br />\nc. The commonest organism is pseudomonas.<br />\nd. Mainly treated surgically.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6663, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The middle ear magnifies the sound:<br />\na. 20 times.<br />\nb. 22 times.<br />\nc. 200times.<br />\nd. 21 times.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6664, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The test of hearing in infant is:<br />\na. Rinne test.<br />\nb.Weber test.<br />\nc. Pure tone audiometry.<br />\nd.ABR\"Auditory Brain stem Response\".<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6665, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">ABR \"Auditory Brain stem Response\" is usd in:<br />\na. Test of hearing in malingering.<br />\nb. Test of hearing in retrochoclear lesion.<br />\nc. Detection of acoustic neuroma.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6666, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are the manifestations of temporal lobe abscess EXCEPT:<br />\na. Hemi paresis.<br />\nb. Aphasia.<br />\nc.Convulsivefits.<br />\nd. Vertigo.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6667, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In traumatic rupture of the drum,all are true EXCEPT:<br />\na. The main treatment is conservative.<br />\nb. Local ear drops are highly indicated.<br />\nc. It heals spontancously within 3 months.<br />\nd. It may be caused by longitudinal fracture of the temporal bone.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6668, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Conductive deafness is the main presentation of:<br />\na. Furunculosis of the external auditory canal.<br />\nb. Ear wax.<br />\nc.Haematomaauris.<br />\nd. Non of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6669, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Unilateral hearing loss with pulsating tinnitus is suggestive of:<br />\na.Otosclerosis.<br />\nb. Extradural abscess complicating CSOM.<br />\nc. Glomus tumor.<br />\nd. Acoustic neuroma.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6670, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most common vertigo is:<br />\na. Acoustic neuroma.<br />\nb.Ototoxicity.<br />\nc.Meniere\'s disease.<br />\nd. Benign paroxysmal positional vertigo.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6671, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A case of ear infection followed by headache, blurring of vision & vomiting is suggestive of:<br />\na.Mastoiditis.<br />\nb. Petrositis.<br />\nc.Labyrinthitis.<br />\nd. Brain abscess.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6672, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The commonest organism in malignant otitis externa:<br />\na. Streptococci.<br />\nb.Pneumococci.<br />\nc. Pseudomonas aeroginosa.<br />\nd. Moraxella catarrhalis.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6673, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The medial wall of the middle ear shows the following EXCEPT:<br />\na. The oval window.<br />\nb. The promontory.<br />\nc.The pyramid.<br />\nd. The lateral semicircular canal.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6674, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Mixed hearing loss may be caused by one of the following:<br />\na.Otosclerosis.<br />\nb.Meniere\'s disease.<br />\nc. Ear wax.<br />\nd. Acoustic neuroma.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6675, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pulsating ear discharge may be found in:<br />\na. Extradural abscess.<br />\nb. Acute exacerbation of CSOM.<br />\nc. Acute otitis media with small perforation.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6676, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are tests of hearing sensitivity EXCEPT:<br />\na. Tuning fork tests.<br />\nb.Tympanometry.<br />\nc. Auditory Brain stem Response.<br />\nd. Pure tone audiometry.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6677, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All are truc about the Eustachian tube EXCEPT:<br />\na.It opens during swallowing.<br />\nb. It ventilates the middle ear.<br />\nc. It is wider& horizontal in children.<br />\nd. It opens in the oropharynx<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6678, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Equilibrium during angular \"rotational\" movement is the function of:<br />\na).The utricle.<br />\nb. The saccule.<br />\nc. The cochlea.<br />\nd. The semicircular canal.<br />\n\'</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6679, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The most common cause of otitis media with effusion is:<br />\na. Inadequate treatment of acute otitis media.<br />\nb. Nasopharyngeal neoplasm.<br />\nc. Allergy.<br />\nd. Otitic barotraumas.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6680, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following drugs are ototoxic:<br />\na.Neomycin.<br />\nb. Gramycin.<br />\nc.Saliclates.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6681, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The inferior meatus receives the opening of:<br />\na. The maxillary sinus.<br />\nb. The anterior ethmoidal sinus.<br />\nc.The posterior ethmoidal sinus.<br />\nd.Nusolacrimal duct.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6682, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Perforation of bony part of the nasal septum occurs in:<br />\na. Sarcoidosis.<br />\nb. Rhinoscleroma.<br />\nc.Tuberculosis.<br />\nd.Syphilis.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6683, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Spontaneous recovery is usual in:<br />\na. Rhinosporodosis.<br />\nb. Sarcoidosis.<br />\nc.Tuberculosis.<br />\nd. Syphilis.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6684, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Eosinophils in great numbers in nasal secretion is a finding in:<br />\na. Atrophic rhinitis.<br />\nb. Chronic rhinitis.<br />\nc.Allergic rhinitis.<br />\nd. Acute rhinitis.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6685, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Sneezing is a prominent feature in:<br />\na.Atrophic rhinitis.<br />\nb. Chronic rhinitis.<br />\nc.Allergic rhinitis.<br />\nd.Acute rhinitis.<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6686, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Unilateralmucopurulent& purulent nasal discharge may be due to:<br />\na. Unilateral sinusitis.<br />\nb. FB in the nose.<br />\nc. Non of them.<br />\nd. All of them.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6687, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are some general causes of epistaxis EXCEPT:<br />\na. Anemia.<br />\nb.Arterial hypertension.<br />\nc.Nasopharyngealangiofibroma.<br />\nd. Renal failure.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6688, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following drugs can cause epistaxis EXCEPT:<br />\na.Salicylates.<br />\nb. Anticoagulants.<br />\nc.Quinine.<br />\nd.Ampicllin.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6689, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The commonest cause of epistaxis in 50 years old man is:<br />\na.Hypertension.<br />\nb. Angiofibroma.<br />\nc.Allergic nasal polypi.<br />\nd. Antrochoanal polyp.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6690, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cause of secondary hemorrhage is:<br />\na. Wound sepsis.<br />\nb. Unprepared patient.<br />\nc. Injury of the pharyngeal muscle.<br />\nd. Rising of blood pressure with slipping ligature.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6691, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Fever in diphtheria is:<br />\na. High grade fever.<br />\nb. Low grade fever.<br />\nc.Remittent fever.<br />\nd. Intermittent fever.<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6692, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pulse in diphtheria is:<br />\na. Weak rapid pulse.<br />\nb. Full bounding pulse.<br />\nc.Synchronous with the temperature.<br />\nd. Non synchronous with the temperature.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6693, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The causative agent of thrush stomatitis is:<br />\na.Borelivencenti.<br />\nb.Candidaalbicans.<br />\nc. Barr-epestin virus.<br />\nd. Streptococci.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6694, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Membranous tonsillitis may be due to : <br />\na.Diphtheria.<br />\nb. Acute follicular tonsillitis.<br />\nc. Infectious mononucleosis.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6695, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pharyngeal ulcer may be due to:<br />\na. Herpes simplex.<br />\nb. Herpes zoster.<br />\nc. TB.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6696, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pharyngeal ulcer may be duc to:<br />\na.Blood diseases.<br />\nb. Skin diseases(linchenplanus).<br />\nc. Toxic (heavy metals).<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6697, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The swelling in acute retropharyngeal abcess is:<br />\na. In the middle line.<br />\nb. Lateral to the middle line.<br />\nc. Appears from outside the neck.<br />\nd. Non of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6698, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Acute laryngeal abscess is characterized by all of the following EXCEPT:<br />\na.Occur most commonly in infants.<br />\nb. Involves the prevertebral space.<br />\nc. Usually oceurs with TB of the cervical vertebra.<br />\nd. Is seen inIateral X-ray of neck.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6699, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Stomatitis associated with skin lesions:<br />\na.Pemphigus.<br />\nb.Linchenplanus.<br />\nc. Lupus erthromatosis.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6700, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following metabolic disorder associated with stomatitis:<br />\na.Uremia.<br />\nb. DM.<br />\nc.Liver disease.<br />\nd. All of the above.<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6701, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The outer ear is differentiated from the inner ear by <br />\nA. Pinna B. Middle ear C. Otitis media <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6702, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common cause of nosebleeds?<br />\nA. nose-picking B. nose mask C. none of the above  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6703, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most effective way to stop a nosebleed?<br />\nA. direct pinching B. direct blow C. nose picking<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6704, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What medicated spray can be used to help stop a bleed?<br />\nA. Ibuprofen spray B. afrin and other nasal sprays C. none of the above  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6705, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is function of the larynx<br />\na)It does not produce voice <br />\nb)It gives support to other related structures such as pharynx that serves aspassage way for air and food<br />\nc)It doesn\'t assist trachea which filter harmidifis air<br />\nd)Its safes traffic control for air and water<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6706, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the difference between a posterior and an anterior nosebleed, and why is this important?<br />\nA. There are most common and arise from the septum (middle wall) of the nose. <br />\nB. bleeding is usually responsive to direct pressure. <br />\nC. all of the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6707, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 3 year old has a bug lodged in his ear. He is screaming and combative. What can you do to help?<br />\nA. kill the bug inside the ear with solution. B. Remove the bug with forceps. C. Remove the bug with broom stick<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6708, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Following a fight, a 25years old male declines transport. He has a large swelling of the outer ear from a direct blow. What can you advise him about the need for treatment?<br />\nA. Hematomas of the outer ear will cause breakdown of the cartilage if they are not treated with an incision and expression of clot, then a pressure dressing. B. he should continue his journey. C. no need for any medication<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6709, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">His other ear has a 2cm laceration that communicates with the other side. Why is this more dangerous than on other parts of the body?<br />\nA.  As before, lacerations to the cartilage of the ear can lead to severe cosmetic defects unless the cartilage laceration is required. B. Movement of fluid across both sides. C. none of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6710, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The other contestant in this fight has a very swollen nose. It was bleeding, but this has stopped now. He also declines medical treatment. Why should he have his nose looked at?<br />\nA. it may require surgery. B. A septal hematoma can occur with nasal injuries due to contained local bleeding. C. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6711, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 2 year old has stuffed a bead into her nose. Does this present any danger to her? What will happen if this was unwitnessed or unrecognized?<br />\nA. Yes. B. No C. None<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6712, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Called to an assault, you find a moderately intoxicated patient complaining of jaw pain. He is holding two of his teeth in his hand. What should you do with the teeth?<br />\nA. Return the teeth firmly in their socket, if patient cooperate. B. preserves the teeth with saliva, saline solution or milk. C. all of the above <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6713, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Normal alignment of the teeth during biting, normal jaw opening and no pain to palpation (especially of the mentum or point of the chin) are all good signs. B. Instability of more than one tooth in a row is a sign of a more superficial jaw fracture (alveolar ridge fracture) and requires stabilization of the teeth. C. all of the above</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6714, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The patient states that he was choked during the fight. What is one of the best signs of laryngeal edema in these patients?<br />\nA. Voice changes are one of the best indicators of laryngeal edema, either from trauma or from medical causes. B. laryngeal laceration. C. Nose bleeding  <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6715, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During your exam you find that the patient has a 2cm lac to the margin of his tongue. How should this be managed? <br />\nA. Direct pressure with gauze pads will usually control bleeding from tongue lacs.<br />\nB. cut the tongue off. C. Rinse the mouth with alcohol   <br />\n\'</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6716, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A 9 year old has impaled his cheek with a pencil. The pencil is still sticking through his cheek on your arrival. What should you do? <br />\nA. Remove the pencil. B. Do not remove the pencil. C. shout and cry<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6717, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A patient with a toothache for several days now is having difficulty swallowing. His right face is swollen and tender. What do you need to worry about?  A. Occlusion and death. B. eating of food. C. smell</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6718, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Another patient is 24, has had a sore throat and fever for several days with fevers. She now also complains of difficulty swallowing. She looks distressed, and is spitting her secretions. What may be happening? <br />\nA. severe pharyngitis / tonsillitis. <br />\nB. mouth sore. <br />\nC. salty taste<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6719, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A four year old is having difficulty swallowing and perhaps breathing. The auntie states that the child has had a sore throat and fever for a few days. What is this child at risk for given his age and the history? A. epiglottitis B. Nebulizations. C. haematoma</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6720, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Called on an overdose, you attend a 54year man who drank lye in a suicide attempt. You examine his oropharynx and see no burns. How well does this rule out esophageal burns? A. Household bleach is not concentrated enough to produce burns. B. take a milky drink. C.no idea </p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6721, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The smallest bone is called?<br />\n  A. Stapes B malleus C Incus<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6722, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Olfactory nerve supply<br />\nA. Mouth B Nose C Eye<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6723, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cochlea is located in <br />\nA. Middle ear B. Outer ear. C Inner ear<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6724, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Gingivitis is a disease that affect<br />\nA Tongue. B pharynx. C Gums and it structures<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6725, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Norma is<br />\nA Degeneration of oral cavity including bones. B Cancer of new born. C Normal face expression<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6726, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Organ for smell perception<br />\nA Nose. B Mouth. C Ear D. Sight<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6727, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Otitis media is a disease of the?<br />\nA outer ear. B Middle ear. C Pinna D. Inner ear<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6728, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The vagus nerve enervate all except<br />\nA Tongue. B Nasal cavity. C The ear. D Non of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6729, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pharyngitis<br />\nA Inflammation of the cochlea. B Inflammation of the throat. C Inflammation of the Mouth D. inflammation of the Ear<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6730, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">ENT means<br />\na) Ear, Noce and Throat<br />\nb)Ear,Nice and Table<br />\nc)Ear,Nose and Throat<br />\nd) Ear, Nase and Throat<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(6731, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'ENT', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Diseases of the nose are the following except one<br />\na)Epitaxies<br />\nb)Tumor<br />\nc)Impaired olfactory apparatus infection<br />\nd)Epiglottis<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-17 17:45:24', '2024-07-17 17:45:24'),
(6732, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Labour is termed premature when it occurs before<br />\na. 34th weeks of pregrancy<br />\nb. 37th week of pregnancy<br />\nc. 30 weeks of pregnancy<br />\nd. 40 week of pregnancy<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6733, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">First stage of Labourpregnancy starts with regular contraction of the uterus and ends when<br />\na. Natural labour occurs<br />\nb. The cervix is fully dilated<br />\nc. Hours in multigravida<br />\nd. Hours in nullipara<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6734, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The second stage of labour starts when --------- and ends when ----- 4------<br />\na. When the baby is born and control of bleeding<br />\nb. Cervix is fully dilated and end when the baby is born <br />\nc. When the placenta is delievered<br />\nd. Just before the beginning of labour and when the cervix is fully dilated<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6735, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The third stage of starts and ends when<br />\na. It starts with the birth of the baby and ends when the placenta is expelled<br />\nb. Starts with the delivery of the baby?s head and ends with rupture of membranes<br />\nc.  Starts with the delivery of the aiterior shoulder and ends with the ligation of the cord<br />\nd. Starts with delivery of the placenta and membranes<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6736, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Signs   in the 1st stage of labours are <br />\na. Show, regular uterine contraction, dilatation of the cervix and descent of the presenting part.<br />\nb. Passing of meconium and rupture of membranes.<br />\nc. Descent of the placenta and membranes<br />\nd. Cervical dilation and spontaneous expulsion of placenta<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6737, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Signs of distress in the fetus during  labour are;<br />\na. Painful contractions<br />\nb. Passage of  meconium, reduced foetal heart beat and excessive fetal movement<br />\nc. Show<br />\nd. Excessive fetal movement, frequent uterine contractions<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6738, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Harmful practice during labour include<br />\na. Cleaning the vulva<br />\nb. Giving of Episiotomy<br />\nc. Pushing or bearing down during the 1st stage of labour<br />\nd. Providing support to the perinum<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6739, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Lochia in the 1st 3days after delivery is called ----- <br />\na. Alba<br />\nb. Rubra<br />\nc. Serosa<br />\nd. Menus<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6740, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An average blood loss during labour is estimated as<br />\n[a] 1,500mls   <br />\n[b] 5,000mls <br />\n[c] 500ls <br />\n[d] 200mls<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6741, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">PMTCT means<br />\na. Prevention of HIV<br />\nb. Prevention of mother to child transmission of HIV<br />\nc. Mother to child transmission of HIV<br />\nd. Maternal to child transmission of HIV<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6742, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Fetal movements are felt from<br />\na. 10-12wks of pregrancy<br />\nb.  24-30wks of pregnancy<br />\nc. 16wks ? 20wks of pregnancy<br />\nd. 20 ? 24wks of pregnancy<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6743, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">ACT should be administered to the pregnant woman when <br />\na. 6wks of pregnancy<br />\nb. 2nd  Trimester<br />\nc. As soon as pregnancy is confirmed<br />\nd. At delivery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6744, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For  early initiation of breast feeding,  the baby should be put to breast<br />\na. 3hours after birth<br />\nb. 12hours after delivery<br />\nc. 30mins -- 1hour after delivery<br />\nd. 24hours after delivery<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6745, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Cord dressing means<br />\na. cleaning and application of wound dressing on the cord<br />\nb. cleaning and application of 4% chlorhedixine gel<br />\nc. cleaning and application of penicillin ointment<br />\nd. cleaning and application of bandage<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6746, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the importance of ante- natal care is <br />\na. to educate mothers on happenings around their environment<br />\nb. to aid the growth of any health hazard<br />\nc. to prevent lactation<br />\nd. to prevent disease, detect early and treat any condition that can jeopardize the health of both mother and child<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6747, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Post ? natal care is done to ----<br />\na. farmiliarise the health worker<br />\nb. assist the newly delivered mother and baby to have a healthy living<br />\nc. to give the mother a social life<br />\nd. to give both mother and baby empowerment<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6748, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Post partum family planning means <br />\na. Emergency family planning<br />\nb. B. family planning without the consent of husband.<br />\nc. Post production family planning<br />\nd. Having a family planning method after the delivery of a baby<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6749, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Post partum family planning should be carried out at <br />\na. 10wks after delivery<br />\nb. 6months after delivery <br />\nc. 6 wks after delivery<br />\nd. 9 months after delivery<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6750, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Kangaroo  mother care is for<br />\na. all babies at term<br />\nb.  babies that cried well at term<br />\nc. babies of low birth weight<br />\nd. babies born by caesarian section<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6751, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Exclusive breastfeeding is <br />\na. breastfeeding the baby exclusively for 9 moths<br />\nb. breastmilk for 6 months<br />\nc. breastfeeding the baby for only 6 months<br />\nd. breastfeeding the baby only when the mother is available<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6752, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cord should be ligated at <br />\na. 3cm from the umbilicus or abdomen<br />\nb. 10cm from the navel<br />\nc. 1cm  from the umbilicus<br />\nd. 2cm from the umbilicus<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6753, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A full bladder can hinder the ------------- from contracting well.<br />\na) Cervix <br />\nB) Fallopian tube <br />\nC) Uterus <br />\nd) infundibulum<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6754, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If a patient pushes through an undilated cervix.<br />\na. the cervix can gape<br />\nb. the cervix can become thickened unable to dilate or tear<br />\nc. the cervix can become thickened to increase dilatation<br />\nd. the cervix becomes clearer<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6755, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are signs of false labour.<br />\na. irregular contractions, pregressive descent of presenting part<br />\nb. there is show, regular and expulsive contractions<br />\nc. irregular contraction, no dilatation<br />\nd. there is regular, strong, regular contraction and cervix is 4cm dilated<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6756, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The cervix is fully dilated when.<br />\na. the cervix is felt firmly attached to the presenting part but 4cm dilated<br />\nb. the cervix is no longer felt round the presenting part and it can accommodate 5 fingers<br />\nc. cervix is thick and loosely attached to the presenting part.<br />\nd. the cervix can admit only 2 fingers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6757, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Premature rupture of membranes can be caused by <br />\na. sexually transmitted infection and low socio- economic conditions<br />\nb. cord prolapsed<br />\nc. fetal engagement<br />\nd. omphalitis<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6758, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the causes of delayed in 2nd stage of labour is <br />\na. regular contractions<br />\nb. perneal laceration<br />\nc. cord round the neck<br />\nd. premature rupture of membranes<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6759, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The placenta on examination has<br />\na. 10 lobes<br />\nb. 7 lobes<br />\nc. 5 lobes<br />\nd. 3 lobes<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6760, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the complication of PROM include<br />\na. fetal engagement<br />\nb. sepsis or infection<br />\nc. maternal deformity<br />\nd. cervicitis<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6761, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Leakage or sudden gush of fluid from the vigina before the 37th week of gestation and before the onset of labour is called<br />\nA, premature rupture of membrane<br />\nb. preterm premature rupture of membranes<br />\nc. premature onset of membrane<br />\nd. premature rupture of fluid<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6762, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the cause of post partum haemorrhage is <br />\na. Cervical exposure<br />\nb. Cervical laceration<br />\nc. Cervical examination<br />\nd. Cervical contraction<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6763, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the reasons for giving episiotomy during labour is <br />\n        a. to create space for passage of the fetus<br />\n        b. to improve condition<br />\n        c. to expose the cervix<br />\n        d. to prevent pains<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6764, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the duty of community health extension worker in pre- conception care is<br />\n         a. to greet and love patients<br />\n         b. to eliminate ignorance in the life of intending couples<br />\n         c. to individualize care<br />\n        d. to consider pregnancy<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6765, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pre- conception care is<br />\n         a. an individualized care of people considering pregnancy<br />\n          b. people enjoying marital life<br />\n          c. care of people in pregnancy<br />\n          d. psychological interventions in marriage<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6766, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Pregnancy is said to occur when<br />\n          a. an ovum  is fertilized<br />\n          b. when there is uterus<br />\n         c.  when the fertilized ovum is implanted in the uterus<br />\n         d. immediately there is ovulation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6767, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Fertilization takes place in the <br />\na. Ampulla of the cervix<br />\nb. Ampulla of the fallopian tube<br />\nc. Cornua of the uterus<br />\nd. Cornua of the cervix<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6768, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Danger signs of pregnancy include<br />\na. vagina bleeding, high blood pressure<br />\nb. frequency of micturition<br />\nc. verico vein<br />\nd. adequate pelvis<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6769, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Atony of the uterus means <br />\na. Inadequate myometrial cell<br />\nb.  Uterine release <br />\nc. Inadequate contraction of the uterus<br />\nd. Inadequate pelvic<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6770, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Medications commonly used in PPH<br />\na. Non- steroidal,  heatemycin<br />\nb. Oxytocin [pitoncin], misoprostol<br />\nc. Analgesic, prstin  E2<br />\nd. Paracetamol, IPT<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6771, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The natural way to stop bleeding is<br />\na. rest and sleep<br />\nb. caregiver should massage the uterus,  allow breastfeeding<br />\nc. tell the patient to open mouth and breathe<br />\nd   shave the patient well<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6772, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Height measurement is to determine<br />\na. Uterus adequate<br />\nb. Time of delivery<br />\nc. No of miscarriages<br />\nd. Pelvic adequacy<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6773, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The first fetal movement is called <br />\na. Jumping<br />\nb. Quickening<br />\nc. Exercising<br />\nd. Moulding<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6774, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Preventive measures during antenatal period include<br />\na. Antibody testing abdominal palpation and measurement of B\\P<br />\nb. Abdominal pressure, state counting<br />\nc. Abdominal palpation, PHC services<br />\nd. Abdominal counting, abdominal palpation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6775, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">IPT and ITN is used to <br />\na. Prevent maternal interest<br />\nb. Prevent malarial attack<br />\nc. Promote food intake<br />\nd. Promote malarial uptake<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6776, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">These patients do not require routine urine testing<br />\na. Primipara with Bi- pedal oedema<br />\nb. Multipara  with stable vital signs and No complaints<br />\nc. Muiltipara with raised B\\P<br />\nd. Primipara with complaints of headache and raised B\\P<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6777, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The process of PMTCT of HIV is to prevent<br />\na. The spread of HIV from man to woman<br />\nb. Mother to child transmission of HIV<br />\nc. Circumcision of male babies<br />\nd. Malaria in pregnancy mothers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6778, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The drug that is commonly used to deworm  pregnant mothers is called<br />\na. Dazolin<br />\nb. Meperazine<br />\nc. Mebendazole<br />\nd. Combatin<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6779, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of these is a sign of complication during labour<br />\na. Puerperal sepsis<br />\nb. Foetal distress<br />\nc. Progressive dilatation of cervix<br />\nd. Expulsion contractions<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6780, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Reduce fetal movement is a sign of<br />\na. Maternal sign<br />\nb. Maternal pressure<br />\nc. Foetal distress<br />\nd. Maternal discomfort<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
(6781, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'MATERNAL HEALTH', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">increased fetal heart rate during labour is a sign of <br />\na. maternal pain<br />\nb. fetal presentation<br />\nc. flat applause<br />\nd. foetal distress<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:11:12', '2024-07-18 15:11:12'),
