(7070, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the cause of ophthalmianeonatorum?<br />\na. Vitamin A deficiency<br />\nb. Refractive errors<br />\nc. Bacterial infection<br />\nd. Glaucoma<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7071, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can ophthalmianeonatorum be transmitted?<br />\na. Contact with fomites agents<br />\nb. Direct contact with eye, nose, and throat secretion of the infected person <br />\nc. Cross infection<br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7072, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the recommended treatment for conjunctivitis?<br />\na. Local antibiotic<br />\nb. Antihistamines for 1-3 days<br />\nc. Clean eyes with boiled water or 0.9% sodium chloride <br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7073, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary cause of onchocerciasis?<br />\na. Bacterial infection<br />\nb. Fungal infection<br />\nc. Parasitic infection<br />\nd. Viral infection<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7074, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is xerophthalmia?<br />\na. A precursor to blindness caused by vitamin A deficiency<br />\nb. Refractive errors caused by aging<br />\nc. A bacterial infection of the cornea <br />\nd. An allergic reaction to foreign substances<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7075, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is cataract?<br />\na. A condition when the cornea loses its transparency <br />\nb. A condition when the lens of the eye becomes opaque <br />\nc. A condition when the optic nerve is damaged <br />\nd. A condition when the retina detaches <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7076, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What causes cataract?<br />\na. Diabetes mellitus<br />\nb. Trauma and eye injuries <br />\nc. Congenital <br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7077, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does cataract lead to blindness?<br />\na. By making the central hole in the eye look whitish or grey<br />\nb. By causing gradual loss of vision<br />\nc. By losing the transparency of the normal crystalline lens <br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
