(7080, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Can blindness caused by cataract be reversed?<br />\na. Yes<br />\nb. No<br />\nc. Only partially<br />\nd. Depends on the severity of the case<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7081, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of diabetes is a known cause of cataract?<br />\na. Type 1<br />\nb. Type 2<br />\nc. Both type 1 and type 2<br />\nd. Neither type 1 nor type 2<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7082, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which treatment involves removing the entire lens including the capsule?<br />\na. Intra-capsular cataract extraction (I C C E) <br />\nb. Extra-capsular cataract extraction (E C C E)<br />\nc. Photorefractive keratectomy (PRK) <br />\nd. Laser in-situ keratomileusis (LASIK)<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7083, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">52. What is the difference between intra-capsular cataract extraction (I C C E) and extra-capsular cataract extraction (E C C E)?<br />\na. None, they are the same procedure<br />\nb. I C C E involves removal of the entire lens including the capsule while E C C E removes only the nucleus <br />\nc. E C C E involves removal of the entire lens while I C C E removes only the nucleus with surrounding capsule <br />\nd. Both procedures only remove the cataract from one eye <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7084, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is NOT a cause of cataract?<br />\na. Extended periods of reading or using electronic screens<br />\nb. Aged <br />\nc. Congenital <br />\nd. Undernutrition<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7085, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a corneal ulcer?<br />\na. Inflammation of the cornea <br />\nb. A type of infection on the retina <br />\nc. A fungal infection in the eye <br />\nd. An ulcer on the surface of the cornea <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7086, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common cause of corneal ulcer?<br />\na. Bacterial infection <br />\nb. Fungal infection<br />\nc. Acanthamoeba keratitis <br />\nd. Herpes simplex virus <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7087, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the symptoms of corneal ulcer?<br />\na. Blurred vision <br />\nb. Redness and swelling in the eye <br />\nc. Sensitivity to light <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7088, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is corneal ulcer diagnosed?<br />\na. CT scan<br />\nb. MRI<br />\nc. Ophthalmic examination <br />\nd. Blood test <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7089, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the treatment for corneal ulcer?<br />\na. Antibiotic eye drops or ointment <br />\nb. Antifungal eye drops or ointment<br />\nc. Corticosteroid eye drops <br />\nd. Surgery<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7090, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is a refractive error?<br />\na. A type of visual impairment caused by clouding of the eye lens <br />\nb. A type of visual impairment caused by damage to the optic nerve <br />\nc. A type of visual impairment caused by abnormal curvature of the cornea or lens <br />\nd. A type of visual impairment caused by damage to the retina<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7091, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the three main types of refractive errors?<br />\na. Myopia, hyperopia, and astigmatism <br />\nb. Cataract, macular degeneration, and glaucoma <br />\nc. Conjunctivitis, uveitis, and keratitis <br />\nd. None of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7092, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is myopia?<br />\na. A condition where the eye is too short <br />\nb. A condition where the cornea is too steep <br />\nc. A condition where the lens is too strong <br />\nd. A condition where the eye is irregularly shaped <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7093, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is hyperopia?<br />\na. A condition where the eye is too long<br />\nb. A condition where the cornea is too steep <br />\nc. A condition where the lens is too weak <br />\nd. A condition where the eye is irregularly shaped <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7094, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is astigmatism?<br />\na. A condition where the eye is too short <br />\nb. A condition where the cornea is too steep <br />\nc. A condition where the lens is too weak <br />\nd. A condition where the cornea or lens is irregularly shaped <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7095, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common symptom of refractive errors?<br />\na. Blurred vision <br />\nb. Double vision <br />\nc. Eye pain <br />\nd. None of the above<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7096, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a common treatment for refractive errors?<br />\na. Eyeglasses or contact lenses <br />\nb. LASIK surgery <br />\nc. PRK surgery <br />\nd. Corneal transplant <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7097, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Can refractive errors be prevented?<br />\na. Yes<br />\nb. No<br />\nc. Only in people with a family history of refractive errors <br />\nd. Only in people who regularly visit an ophthalmologist <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7098, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following lifestyle factors can contribute to the development of refractive errors?<br />\na. Excessive screen time <br />\nb. Lack of outdoor activities <br />\nc. Poor nutrition <br />\nd. All of the above<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7099, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common cause of blindness related to a tropical disease?<br />\na. Malaria <br />\nb. Dengue fever <br />\nc. Onchocerciasis<br />\nd. Chikungunya<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7100, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is onchocerciasis?<br />\na. A parasitic infection transmitted by blackflies <br />\nb. A viral infection transmitted by mosquitoes <br />\nc. A bacterial infection transmitted by ticks <br />\nd. A fungal infection transmitted by soil <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7101, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the eye complications of onchocerciasis?<br />\na. Scratched cornea <br />\nb. Cataracts <br />\nc. Optic neuritis <br />\nd. River blindness <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7102, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most effective treatment for onchocerciasis?<br />\na. Antibiotics <br />\nb. Antimalarial medication <br />\nc. Ivermectin<br />\nd. Surgery <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7103, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is trachoma?<br />\na. A bacterial infection transmitted by flies <br />\nb. A viral infection transmitted by mosquitoes <br />\nc. A fungal infection transmitted by soil <br />\nd. A parasitic infection transmitted by blackflies <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7104, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What are the eye complications of trachoma?<br />\na. Conjunctivitis <br />\nb. Redness and swelling in the eye <br />\nc. Corneal scarring <br />\nd. All of the above <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
(7105, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'PRIMARY EYE CARE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most effective treatment for trachoma?<br />\na. Antibiotics <br />\nb. Antimalarial medication <br />\nc. Ivermectin<br />\nd. Surgery <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-18 15:18:57', '2024-07-18 15:18:57'),
