(7329, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'Research', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 50, 50, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> A study in which a category of people who share a similar life experience in a specified time period is studied is called_____________                                                                            A. time series study     B. panel study     C . cohort study     D. pilot study </p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 14:48:21', '2024-07-19 14:48:21'),
(7330, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'Research', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 50, 50, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> A study in which a category of people who share a similar life experience in a specified time period is studied is called_____________                                                                            A. time series study     B. panel study     C . cohort study     D. pilot study </p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 14:48:21', '2024-07-19 14:48:21'),
(7331, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of supervised clinical experience in community health education?<br />\n   - A) To earn academic credits<br />\n- B) To provide hands-on training in real-world settings<br />\n   - C) To socialize with healthcare professionals<br />\n   - D) To conduct independent research<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7332, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During supervised clinical experience, what is the role of the preceptor?<br />\n   - A) To provide academic lectures<br />\n   - B) To evaluate student performance<br />\n   - C) To assist with administrative tasks<br />\n   - D) To organize community events<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7333, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a typical activity during supervised clinical experience?<br />\n   - A) Attending seminars on healthcare policy<br />\n   - B) Shadowing healthcare professionals<br />\n   - C) Conducting laboratory experiments<br />\n   - D) Writing academic papers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7334, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does supervised clinical experience contribute to community health education?<br />\n   - A) By providing opportunities for networking<br />\n  - B) By offering exposure to diverse healthcare settings<br />\n   - C) By organizing community health fairs<br />\n   - D) By teaching theoretical concepts<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7335, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What skills can students develop during supervised clinical experience?<br />\n   - A) Software programming<br />\n   - B) Public speaking<br />\n- C) Patient communication and empathy<br />\n   - D) Graphic design<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7336, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an important aspect of reflective practice during supervised clinical experience?<br />\n   - A) Memorizing medical terminology<br />\n   - B) Critically analyzing experiences and learning from them<br />\n   - C) Completing administrative forms<br />\n   - D) Networking with healthcare professionals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7337, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does supervised clinical experience prepare students for their future careers in community health?<br />\n   - A) By offering paid internship opportunities<br />\n   - B) By exposing them to real-life challenges and problem-solving<br />\n   - C) By providing free healthcare services to the community<br />\n   - D) By assigning them to research projects<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7338, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common method used to measure body temperature accurately?<br />\n   - A) Oral temperature<br />\n   - B) Armpit temperature<br />\n   - C) Forehead temperature<br />\n   - D) Ear temperature<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7339, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should you avoid taking an oral temperature measurement?<br />\n   - A) After the person has had a cold drink<br />\n   - B) Before a meal<br />\n   - C) During exercise<br />\n- D) When the person is breathing through their mouth<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7340, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of thermometer is typically used for axillary (armpit) temperature measurements?<br />\n   - A) Digital thermometer<br />\n   - B) Mercury thermometer<br />\n   - C) Infrared thermometer<br />\n   - D) Disposable thermometer strips<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7341, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an advantage of using an infrared thermometer to measure temperature?<br />\n   - A) It provides a more accurate reading from the armpit<br />\n   - B) It is the most cost-effective option<br />\n- C) It can provide quick readings without touching the person<br />\n   - D) It is safe to use for infants younger than 6 month<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7342, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what location on the body should you measure tympanic (ear) temperature?<br />\n- A) The outer ear canal<br />\n   - B) Behind the earlobe<br />\n   - C) The forehead<br />\n   - D) The back of the neck<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7343, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an important consideration when using a tympanic thermometer?<br />\n   - A) It provides the most accurate core body temperature<br />\n   - B) It should be inserted deeply into the ear canal<br />\n   - C) It should be used only on children older than 5 years<br />\n- D) The ear should be positioned correctly to get an accurate reading<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7344, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should you measure rectal temperature?<br />\n   - A) When the person is lying down<br />\n   - B) After the person has eaten a meal<br />\n- C) When other methods are not feasible or accurate<br />\n   - D) Only for newborns and infants<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7345, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an advantage of using disposable thermometer strips?<br />\n   - A) They are reusable and environmentally friendly<br />\n   - B) They provide instant temperature readings<br />\n   - C) They are suitable for all age groups<br />\n   - D) They require calibration before each use<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7346, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an important step before and after using a digital thermometer for temperature measurement?<br />\n   - A) Wipe the thermometer with alcohol<br />\n   - B) Store the thermometer in a cool, dry place<br />\n   - C) Record the temperature in the person?s medical record<br />\n   - D) Check the thermometer?s battery level<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7347, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which temperature measurement method is recommended for infants under 3 months old?<br />\n    - A) Oral temperature<br />\n    - B) Axillary (armpit) temperature<br />\n    - C) Tympanic (ear) temperature<br />\n    - D) Rectal temperature<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7348, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which unit is blood pressure typically measured in?<br />\n   - A) Millimeters of mercury (mmHg)<br />\n   - B) Liters per minute (L/min)<br />\n   - C) Beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - D) Kilopascals (kPa)<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7349, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the top number (systolic) represent in a blood pressure reading?<br />\n   - A) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is contracting<br />\n   - B) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is relaxed<br />\n   - C) The average pressure in the arteries over time<br />\n   - D) The pressure in the veins when blood returns to the heart<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7350, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the bottom number (diastolic) represent in a blood pressure reading?<br />\n   - A) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is contracting<br />\n   - B) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is relaxed<br />\n   - C) The average pressure in the arteries over time<br />\n   - D) The pressure in the veins when blood returns to the heart<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7351, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which artery is commonly used to measure blood pressure?<br />\n   - A) Radial artery<br />\n   - B) Femoral artery<br />\n   - C) Carotid artery<br />\n   - D) Brachial artery<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7352, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what level should the blood pressure cuff be positioned on the arm?<br />\n   - A) Below the elbow joint<br />\n   - B) Over the bicep muscle<br />\n   - C) At the level of the heart<br />\n   - D) Near the wrist<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7353, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should the patient avoid doing immediately before having their blood pressure taken?<br />\n   - A) Sitting quietly for at least 5 minutes<br />\n   - B) Drinking a glass of water<br />\n- C) Engaging in vigorous physical activity<br />\n   - D) Eating a small snack<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7354, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many times should blood pressure be measured during a single session for accuracy?<br />\n   - A) Once, for simplicity<br />\n   - B) Twice, with a short break in between<br />\n   - C) Three times, averaging the second and third readings<br />\n   - D) Four times, taking the highest reading<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7355, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might affect blood pressure readings if the cuff is too small?<br />\n   - A) Hypertension (high blood pressure)<br />\n   - B) Hypotension (low blood pressure)<br />\n   - C) Orthostatic hypotension<br />\n   - D) False high readings<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7356, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should the stethoscope be placed when auscultating for blood pressure?<br />\n- A) Over the brachial artery<br />\n   - B) Over the carotid artery<br />\n   - C) Over the radial artery<br />\n   - D) Over the femoral artery<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7357, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an acceptable range for normal blood pressure in adults?<br />\n    - A) Systolic less than 120 mmHg, diastolic less than 80 mmHg<br />\n    - B) Systolic less than 140 mmHg, diastolic less than 90 mmHg<br />\n    - C) Systolic less than 160 mmHg, diastolic less than 100 mmHg<br />\n    - D) Systolic less than 180 mmHg, diastolic less than 120 mmHg<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7358, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which artery is commonly used to measure the pulse?<br />\n   - A) Carotid artery<br />\n   - B) Radial artery<br />\n   - C) Femoral artery<br />\n   - D) Brachial artery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7359, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Where is the radial pulse typically located?<br />\n   - A) In the neck<br />\n   - B) In the groin<br />\n   - C) On the wrist<br />\n   - D) Behind the knee<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7360, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should you position your fingers to palpate the radial pulse?<br />\n   - A) With your thumb on the artery<br />\n   - B) With your index and middle fingers on the artery<br />\n   - C) With your pinky finger on the artery<br />\n   - D) With your palm on the artery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7361, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range of pulse rate for adults at rest?<br />\nA. 60-90 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - B) 100-120 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - C) 40-60 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - D) 20-30 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7362, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the pulse rate measure?<br />\n   - A) Blood pressure in the arteries<br />\n- B) Strength of the heartbeat<br />\n   - C) Blood oxygen saturation<br />\n   - D) Respiratory rate<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7363, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should you count the pulse for a full minute?<br />\n   - A) Always, to ensure accuracy<br />\n   - B) Only if the pulse rate seems irregular<br />\n   - C) Only for children and infants<br />\n   - D) Only during exercise<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7364, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an irregular pulse rhythm called?<br />\n   - A) Tachycardia<br />\n   - B) Bradycardia<br />\n   - C) Dysrhythmia<br />\n   - D) Arrhythmia<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7365, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which pulse site is commonly used in emergency situations to assess circulation?<br />\n  - A) Carotid artery<br />\n   - B) Brachial artery<br />\n   - C) Popliteal artery<br />\n   - D) Dorsalis pedis artery<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7366, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should you describe the strength of a pulse that feels strong and bounding?<br />\n   - A) 0<br />\n   - B) 1+<br />\n   - C) 2+<br />\n   - D) 3+<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7367, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should you note about the pulse rhythm if it is irregular?<br />\n    - A) The exact beats per minute<br />\n- B) Whether it is regular or irregular<br />\n    - C) The intensity of the pulse<br />\n    - D) The duration of each pulse<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7368, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does visual acuity measure?<br />\n   - A) Color perception<br />\n   - B) Eye pressure<br />\n   - C) Ability to see objects at a distance<br />\n   - D) Sharpness of vision<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7369, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is commonly used to measure visual acuity?<br />\n   - A) Ophthalmoscope<br />\n   - B) Tonometry<br />\n   - C) Snellen chart<br />\n   - D) Otoscope<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7370, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In a Snellen chart, what does 20/20 vision mean?<br />\n   - A) The person can see clearly at 20 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n   - B) The person can see clearly at 20 meters what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n   - C) The person can see clearly at 20 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 10 feet<br />\n   - D) The person can see clearly at 10 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7371, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the Snellen chart used to assess?<br />\n   - A) Color blindness<br />\n   - B) Peripheral vision<br />\n   - C) Near vision<br />\n- D) Distance vision<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7372, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is visual acuity recorded if a person has 20/40 vision?<br />\n   - A) They can see at 20 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 40 feet<br />\n   - B) They can see at 40 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n   - C) They can see at 20 meters what a person with normal vision can see at 40 meters<br />\n   - D) They can see at 40 meters what a person with normal vision can see at 20 meters<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7373, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?20/200 vision? mean on a Snellen chart?<br />\n   - A) Legal blindness<br />\n   - B) Normal vision<br />\n   - C) Impaired near vision<br />\n   - D) Impaired distance vision<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7374, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the visual acuity measurement if a person can only read the top letter (usually ?E?) on a Snellen chart?<br />\n   - A) 20/20<br />\n   - B) 20/40<br />\n   - C) 20/100<br />\n- D) 20/200<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7375, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of acuity chart is commonly used for near vision testing?<br />\n- A) Rosenbaum chart<br />\n   - B) Snellen chart<br />\n   - C) Tumbling E chart<br />\n   - D) Landolt C chart<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7376, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?counting fingers? visual acuity mean?<br />\n   - A) The person can count fingers held up at a distance<br />\n   - B) The person can see clearly up close<br />\n   - C) The person can see shapes but not details<br />\n   - D) The person has no perception of light<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7377, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is visual acuity measured in children who cannot read letters?<br />\n    - A) By asking them to identify shapes<br />\n    - B) By observing their eye movements<br />\n   - C) By using picture charts or symbols<br />\n    - D) By measuring their pupil size<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7378, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does respiratory rate measure?<br />\n   - A) Heartbeats per minute<br />\n   - B) Oxygen saturation in the blood<br />\n   - C) Number of breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) Lung capacity<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7379, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range for adult respiratory rate at rest?<br />\n   - A) 12-20 breaths per minute<br />\n   - B) 30-40 breaths per minute<br />\n   - C) 60-80 breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) 100-120 breaths per minute<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7380, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which term describes abnormally slow breathing?<br />\n   - A) Bradypnea<br />\n   - B) Tachypnea<br />\n   - C) Apnea<br />\n   - D) Dyspnea<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7381, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What condition is associated with tachypnea?<br />\n   - A) Hypothermia<br />\n   - B) Hypertension<br />\n   - C) Hyperthyroidism<br />\n- D) Respiratory distress<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7382, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should respiratory rate be measured?<br />\n  - A) Counting the number of chest rises for 30 seconds and multiplying by 2<br />\n   - B) Counting the number of chest rises for 15 seconds and multiplying by 4<br />\n   - C) Counting the number of chest rises for 1 minute<br />\n   - D) Counting the number of chest rises for 2 minutes<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7383, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?apnea? refer to?<br />\n   - A) Increased breathing rate<br />\n  - B) Absence of breathing<br />\n   - C) Difficulty breathing<br />\n   - D) Irregular breathing pattern<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7384, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might cause bradypnea?<br />\n   - A) Anxiety<br />\n   - B) Heart failure<br />\n   - C) Fever<br />\n- D) Sedative medication use<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7385, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which situation would you expect to see an increased respiratory rate?<br />\n   - A) During sleep<br />\n   - B) After a large meal<br />\n   - C) During physical exercise<br />\n   - D) While resting quietly<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7386, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is Cheyne-Stokes respiration characterized by?<br />\n- A) Irregular breathing with periods of apnea<br />\n    - B) Fast and shallow breathing<br />\n    - C) Slow and irregular breathing<br />\n    - D) Fast and deep breathing<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7387, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does respiratory rate change in infants and young children compared to adults?<br />\n    - A) It is slower<br />\n  - B) It is faster<br />\n    - C) It remains the same<br />\n    - D) It varies depending on the time of day<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7388, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of performing a urinalysis?<br />\n   - A) To measure blood pressure levels<br />\n   - B) To assess kidney function<br />\n   - C) To diagnose diabetes mellitus<br />\n   - D) To determine oxygen saturation levels<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7389, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which component of urinalysis evaluates the physical characteristics of urine such as color, clarity, and specific gravity?<br />\n   - A) Chemical analysis<br />\n   - B) Microscopic analysis<br />\n   - C) Physical examination<br />\n   - D) Gross examination<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7390, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the presence of proteinuria indicate in urinalysis?<br />\n - A) Kidney inflammation or damage<br />\n   - B) Urinary tract infection<br />\n   - C) Dehydration<br />\n   - D) Diabetes mellitus<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7391, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which chemical test is commonly used to detect glucose in urine?<br />\n   - A) Protein test (albumin)<br />\n   - B) Ketone test (acetone)<br />\n   - C) Bilirubin test<br />\n   - D) Glucose test (Benedict?s or Clinitest)<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7392, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does hematuria indicate in urinalysis?<br />\n   - A) Elevated blood sugar levels<br />\n   - B) Presence of bacteria in urine<br />\n- C) Presence of red blood cells in urine<br />\n   - D) Excessive protein levels in urine<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7393, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which microscopic finding in urinalysis suggests a urinary tract infection (UTI)?<br />\n   - A) Casts<br />\n   - B) Crystals<br />\n- C) Bacteria<br />\n   - D) Epithelial cells<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7394, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the term ?specific gravity? measure in urinalysis?<br />\n   - A) Acidity of urine<br />\n- B) Concentration of solutes in urine<br />\n   - C) Presence of glucose in urine<br />\n   - D) Number of red blood cells in urine<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7395, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal pH range of urine?<br />\n   - A) 5.0 ? 5.5<br />\n   - B) 6.0 ? 6.5<br />\n   - C) 7.0 ? 7.5<br />\n   - D) 8.0 ? 8.5<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7396, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might cause the presence of ketones in urine?<br />\n    - A) Dehydration<br />\n    - B) Excessive protein intake<br />\n- C) Diabetes mellitus<br />\n    - D) Urinary tract infection<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7397, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the presence of bilirubin in urine indicate?<br />\n- A) Liver disease or dysfunction<br />\n    - B) Kidney stones<br />\n    - C) Urinary tract obstruction<br />\n    - D) Bacterial infection<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7398, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does respiratory rate measure?<br />\n   - A) Heartbeats per minute<br />\n   - B) Oxygen saturation in the blood<br />\n   - C) Number of breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) Lung capacity<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7399, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range for adult respiratory rate at rest?<br />\n - A) 12-20 breaths per minute<br />\n   - B) 30-40 breaths per minute<br />\n   - C) 60-80 breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) 100-120 breaths per minute<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7400, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which term describes abnormally slow breathing?<br />\n   - A) Bradypnea<br />\n   - B) Tachypnea<br />\n   - C) Apnea<br />\n   - D) Dyspnea<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7401, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What condition is associated with tachypnea?<br />\n   - A) Hypothermia<br />\n   - B) Hypertension<br />\n   - C) Hyperthyroidism<br />\n- D) Respiratory distress<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7402, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should respiratory rate be measured?<br />\n- A) Counting the number of chest rises for 30 seconds and multiplying by 2<br />\n   - B) Counting the number of chest rises for 15 seconds and multiplying by 4<br />\n   - C) Counting the number of chest rises for 1 minute<br />\n   - D) Counting the number of chest rises for 2 minutes<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7403, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?apnea? refer to?<br />\n   - A) Increased breathing rate<br />\n- B) Absence of breathing<br />\n   - C) Difficulty breathing<br />\n   - D) Irregular breathing pattern<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7404, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might cause bradypnea?<br />\n   - A) Anxiety<br />\n   - B) Heart failure<br />\n   - C) Fever<br />\n- D) Sedative medication use<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7405, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which situation would you expect to see an increased respiratory rate?<br />\n   - A) During sleep<br />\n   - B) After a large meal<br />\n   - C) During physical exercise<br />\n   - D) While resting quiet<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(7406, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What technique is used to assess tactile fremitus during a physical examination of the lungs?<br />\n   - A) Percussion<br />\n- B) Palpation<br />\n   - C) Auscultation<br />\n   - D) Inspection<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7407, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During an abdominal examination, rebound tenderness is indicative of:<br />\n- A) Appendicitis<br />\n   - B) Gastric ulcer<br />\n   - C) Cholecystitis<br />\n   - D) Diverticulitis<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7408, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which cranial nerve is primarily assessed by testing the gag reflex?<br />\n   - A) Cranial nerve V (Trigeminal)<br />\n   - B) Cranial nerve VII (Facial)<br />\n   - C) Cranial nerve IX (Glossopharyngeal)<br />\n   - D) Cranial nerve X (Vagus)<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7409, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a correct sequence for performing a comprehensive physical examination of the abdomen?<br />\n   - A) Inspection, palpation, percussion, auscultation<br />\n   - B) Palpation, auscultation, inspection, percussion<br />\n   - C) Percussion, inspection, auscultation, palpation<br />\n   - D) Auscultation, percussion, palpation, inspection<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7410, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an important step before performing a physical examination on a community member?<br />\n   - A) Obtaining informed consent<br />\n   - B) Reviewing medical literature<br />\n   - C) Performing laboratory tests<br />\n   - D) Calling a specialist<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7411, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During a community health screening, which vital sign is typically measured first?<br />\n   - A) Blood pressure<br />\n   - B) Respiratory rate<br />\n   - C) Temperature<br />\n   - D) Heart rate<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7412, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of performing auscultation during a physical examination?<br />\n   - A) To assess skin integrity<br />\n   - B) To evaluate joint mobility<br />\n- C) To listen to internal body sounds<br />\n   - D) To measure blood pressure<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7413, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which technique is used to assess capillary refill time?<br />\n   - A) Percussion<br />\n   - B) Palpation<br />\n   - C) Inspection<br />\n- D) Pressing on the nail bed<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7414, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of the BMI (Body Mass Index) measurement during a community health assessment?<br />\n - A) To assess nutritional status<br />\n   - B) To measure muscular strength<br />\n   - C) To evaluate lung function<br />\n   - D) To assess bone density<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7415, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which tool is commonly used to assess visual acuity during community health screenings?<br />\n   - A) Otoscope<br />\n   - B) Ophthalmoscope<br />\n   - C) Snellen chart<br />\n   - D) Tuning fork<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7416, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which position is typically used for assessing the rectal area during a physical examination?<br />\n   - A) Supine<br />\n   - B) Prone<br />\n   - C) Lithotomy<br />\n   - D) Sims<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7417, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During a cardiovascular assessment, where is the point of maximal impulse (PMI) typically palpated?<br />\n   - A) Over the left upper quadrant<br />\n   - B) Over the right lower quadrant<br />\n   - C) Over the right upper quadrant<br />\n   - D) Over the left lower quadrant<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7418, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an appropriate way to ensure patient safety during a physical examination in a community setting?<br />\n    - A) Using unsterile equipment<br />\n    - B) Ignoring patient preferences<br />\n    - C) Providing privacy and modesty<br />\n    - D) Rushing through the examination<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7419, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which technique is used to assess the symmetry of chest expansion during respiratory examination?<br />\n   - A) Percussion<br />\n   - B) Palpation<br />\n   - C) Auscultation<br />\n- D) Inspection<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7420, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the purpose of assessing cranial nerve function during a community health physical examination?<br />\n   - A) To measure muscle strength<br />\n   - B) To evaluate sensory perception<br />\n- C) To assess neurological function<br />\n   - D) To examine joint mobility<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7421, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During a musculoskeletal assessment, what does the ?range of motion? refer to?<br />\n   - A) Strength of muscle contraction<br />\n- B) Ability to flex and extend joints<br />\n   - C) Sensory perception in joints<br />\n   - D) Stability of ligaments<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7422, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which assessment technique involves tapping the body surface with fingers to assess underlying structures?<br />\n- A) Percussion<br />\n   - B) Palpation<br />\n   - C) Auscultation<br />\n   - D) Inspection<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7423, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During an abdominal examination, which sound indicates the presence of fluid or gas in the intestines?<br />\n   - A) Dullness<br />\n   - B) Hyperresonance<br />\n- C) Tympany<br />\n   - D) Flatness<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7424, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an important initial step to establish rapport with a patient?<br />\n   - A) Maintain a professional distance<br />\n   - B) Avoid making eye contact<br />\n  - C) Introduce yourself and greet the patient warmly<br />\n   - D) Keep conversations strictly related to medical history<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7425, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Effective communication with patients involves:<br />\n   - A) Using medical jargon to convey expertise<br />\n   - B) Speaking quickly to save time<br />\n- C) Listening actively and empathetically<br />\n   - D) Interrupting the patient to steer the conversation<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7426, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which non-verbal communication technique helps in building rapport with patients?<br />\n   - A) Crossing arms while talking<br />\n- B) Maintaining eye contact<br />\n   - C) Looking at the computer screen<br />\n   - D) Checking the watch frequently<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7427, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When discussing treatment options with a patient, it?s important to:<br />\n   - A) Only provide one option to avoid confusion<br />\n   - B) Rush through the explanation to save time<br />\n   - C) Use plain language and check for understanding<br />\n   - D) Assume the patient already knows everything<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7428, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Showing empathy towards a patient involves:<br />\n   - A) Minimizing the patient?s concerns<br />\n- B) Acknowledging and validating their feelings<br />\n   - C) Providing unsolicited advice<br />\n   - D) Focusing solely on medical facts<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7429, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following behaviors helps in establishing trust with patients?<br />\n   - A) Being defensive when patients ask questions<br />\n   - B) Sharing personal opinions about treatment options<br />\n   - C) Respecting patient autonomy and choices<br />\n   - D) Rushing through appointments to save time<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7430, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How can body language contribute to building rapport with patients?<br />\n   - A) Crossing arms and legs to appear confident<br />\n   - B) Avoiding eye contact to show<br />\nC. Using open and welcome gestures<br />\nD. Standing at a distance to maintain personal space <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:54:33', '2024-07-19 16:54:33'),
(7431, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of supervised clinical experience in community health education?<br />\n   - A) To earn academic credits<br />\n- B) To provide hands-on training in real-world settings<br />\n   - C) To socialize with healthcare professionals<br />\n   - D) To conduct independent research<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7432, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During supervised clinical experience, what is the role of the preceptor?<br />\n   - A) To provide academic lectures<br />\n   - B) To evaluate student performance<br />\n   - C) To assist with administrative tasks<br />\n   - D) To organize community events<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7433, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a typical activity during supervised clinical experience?<br />\n   - A) Attending seminars on healthcare policy<br />\n   - B) Shadowing healthcare professionals<br />\n   - C) Conducting laboratory experiments<br />\n   - D) Writing academic papers<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7434, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does supervised clinical experience contribute to community health education?<br />\n   - A) By providing opportunities for networking<br />\n  - B) By offering exposure to diverse healthcare settings<br />\n   - C) By organizing community health fairs<br />\n   - D) By teaching theoretical concepts<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7435, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What skills can students develop during supervised clinical experience?<br />\n   - A) Software programming<br />\n   - B) Public speaking<br />\n- C) Patient communication and empathy<br />\n   - D) Graphic design<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7436, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an important aspect of reflective practice during supervised clinical experience?<br />\n   - A) Memorizing medical terminology<br />\n   - B) Critically analyzing experiences and learning from them<br />\n   - C) Completing administrative forms<br />\n   - D) Networking with healthcare professionals<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7437, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does supervised clinical experience prepare students for their future careers in community health?<br />\n   - A) By offering paid internship opportunities<br />\n   - B) By exposing them to real-life challenges and problem-solving<br />\n   - C) By providing free healthcare services to the community<br />\n   - D) By assigning them to research projects<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7438, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the most common method used to measure body temperature accurately?<br />\n   - A) Oral temperature<br />\n   - B) Armpit temperature<br />\n   - C) Forehead temperature<br />\n   - D) Ear temperature<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7439, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should you avoid taking an oral temperature measurement?<br />\n   - A) After the person has had a cold drink<br />\n   - B) Before a meal<br />\n   - C) During exercise<br />\n- D) When the person is breathing through their mouth<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7440, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of thermometer is typically used for axillary (armpit) temperature measurements?<br />\n   - A) Digital thermometer<br />\n   - B) Mercury thermometer<br />\n   - C) Infrared thermometer<br />\n   - D) Disposable thermometer strips<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7441, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an advantage of using an infrared thermometer to measure temperature?<br />\n   - A) It provides a more accurate reading from the armpit<br />\n   - B) It is the most cost-effective option<br />\n- C) It can provide quick readings without touching the person<br />\n   - D) It is safe to use for infants younger than 6 month<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7442, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what location on the body should you measure tympanic (ear) temperature?<br />\n- A) The outer ear canal<br />\n   - B) Behind the earlobe<br />\n   - C) The forehead<br />\n   - D) The back of the neck<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7443, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an important consideration when using a tympanic thermometer?<br />\n   - A) It provides the most accurate core body temperature<br />\n   - B) It should be inserted deeply into the ear canal<br />\n   - C) It should be used only on children older than 5 years<br />\n- D) The ear should be positioned correctly to get an accurate reading<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7444, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should you measure rectal temperature?<br />\n   - A) When the person is lying down<br />\n   - B) After the person has eaten a meal<br />\n- C) When other methods are not feasible or accurate<br />\n   - D) Only for newborns and infants<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7445, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an advantage of using disposable thermometer strips?<br />\n   - A) They are reusable and environmentally friendly<br />\n   - B) They provide instant temperature readings<br />\n   - C) They are suitable for all age groups<br />\n   - D) They require calibration before each use<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7446, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an important step before and after using a digital thermometer for temperature measurement?<br />\n   - A) Wipe the thermometer with alcohol<br />\n   - B) Store the thermometer in a cool, dry place<br />\n   - C) Record the temperature in the person?s medical record<br />\n   - D) Check the thermometer?s battery level<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7447, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 17, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which temperature measurement method is recommended for infants under 3 months old?<br />\n    - A) Oral temperature<br />\n    - B) Axillary (armpit) temperature<br />\n    - C) Tympanic (ear) temperature<br />\n    - D) Rectal temperature<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7448, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 18, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which unit is blood pressure typically measured in?<br />\n   - A) Millimeters of mercury (mmHg)<br />\n   - B) Liters per minute (L/min)<br />\n   - C) Beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - D) Kilopascals (kPa)<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7449, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 19, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the top number (systolic) represent in a blood pressure reading?<br />\n   - A) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is contracting<br />\n   - B) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is relaxed<br />\n   - C) The average pressure in the arteries over time<br />\n   - D) The pressure in the veins when blood returns to the heart<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7450, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 20, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the bottom number (diastolic) represent in a blood pressure reading?<br />\n   - A) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is contracting<br />\n   - B) The pressure in the arteries when the heart is relaxed<br />\n   - C) The average pressure in the arteries over time<br />\n   - D) The pressure in the veins when blood returns to the heart<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7451, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 21, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which artery is commonly used to measure blood pressure?<br />\n   - A) Radial artery<br />\n   - B) Femoral artery<br />\n   - C) Carotid artery<br />\n   - D) Brachial artery<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7452, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 22, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">At what level should the blood pressure cuff be positioned on the arm?<br />\n   - A) Below the elbow joint<br />\n   - B) Over the bicep muscle<br />\n   - C) At the level of the heart<br />\n   - D) Near the wrist<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7453, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 23, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should the patient avoid doing immediately before having their blood pressure taken?<br />\n   - A) Sitting quietly for at least 5 minutes<br />\n   - B) Drinking a glass of water<br />\n- C) Engaging in vigorous physical activity<br />\n   - D) Eating a small snack<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7454, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 24, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How many times should blood pressure be measured during a single session for accuracy?<br />\n   - A) Once, for simplicity<br />\n   - B) Twice, with a short break in between<br />\n   - C) Three times, averaging the second and third readings<br />\n   - D) Four times, taking the highest reading<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7455, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 25, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might affect blood pressure readings if the cuff is too small?<br />\n   - A) Hypertension (high blood pressure)<br />\n   - B) Hypotension (low blood pressure)<br />\n   - C) Orthostatic hypotension<br />\n   - D) False high readings<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7456, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 26, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should the stethoscope be placed when auscultating for blood pressure?<br />\n- A) Over the brachial artery<br />\n   - B) Over the carotid artery<br />\n   - C) Over the radial artery<br />\n   - D) Over the femoral artery<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7457, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 27, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an acceptable range for normal blood pressure in adults?<br />\n    - A) Systolic less than 120 mmHg, diastolic less than 80 mmHg<br />\n    - B) Systolic less than 140 mmHg, diastolic less than 90 mmHg<br />\n    - C) Systolic less than 160 mmHg, diastolic less than 100 mmHg<br />\n    - D) Systolic less than 180 mmHg, diastolic less than 120 mmHg<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7458, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 28, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which artery is commonly used to measure the pulse?<br />\n   - A) Carotid artery<br />\n   - B) Radial artery<br />\n   - C) Femoral artery<br />\n   - D) Brachial artery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7459, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 29, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Where is the radial pulse typically located?<br />\n   - A) In the neck<br />\n   - B) In the groin<br />\n   - C) On the wrist<br />\n   - D) Behind the knee<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7460, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 30, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should you position your fingers to palpate the radial pulse?<br />\n   - A) With your thumb on the artery<br />\n   - B) With your index and middle fingers on the artery<br />\n   - C) With your pinky finger on the artery<br />\n   - D) With your palm on the artery<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7461, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range of pulse rate for adults at rest?<br />\nA. 60-90 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - B) 100-120 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - C) 40-60 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n   - D) 20-30 beats per minute (bpm)<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7462, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the pulse rate measure?<br />\n   - A) Blood pressure in the arteries<br />\n- B) Strength of the heartbeat<br />\n   - C) Blood oxygen saturation<br />\n   - D) Respiratory rate<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7463, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">When should you count the pulse for a full minute?<br />\n   - A) Always, to ensure accuracy<br />\n   - B) Only if the pulse rate seems irregular<br />\n   - C) Only for children and infants<br />\n   - D) Only during exercise<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7464, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is an irregular pulse rhythm called?<br />\n   - A) Tachycardia<br />\n   - B) Bradycardia<br />\n   - C) Dysrhythmia<br />\n   - D) Arrhythmia<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7465, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 35, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which pulse site is commonly used in emergency situations to assess circulation?<br />\n  - A) Carotid artery<br />\n   - B) Brachial artery<br />\n   - C) Popliteal artery<br />\n   - D) Dorsalis pedis artery<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7466, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 36, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should you describe the strength of a pulse that feels strong and bounding?<br />\n   - A) 0<br />\n   - B) 1+<br />\n   - C) 2+<br />\n   - D) 3+<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7467, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 37, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What should you note about the pulse rhythm if it is irregular?<br />\n    - A) The exact beats per minute<br />\n- B) Whether it is regular or irregular<br />\n    - C) The intensity of the pulse<br />\n    - D) The duration of each pulse<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7468, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 38, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does visual acuity measure?<br />\n   - A) Color perception<br />\n   - B) Eye pressure<br />\n   - C) Ability to see objects at a distance<br />\n   - D) Sharpness of vision<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7469, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 39, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is commonly used to measure visual acuity?<br />\n   - A) Ophthalmoscope<br />\n   - B) Tonometry<br />\n   - C) Snellen chart<br />\n   - D) Otoscope<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7470, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 40, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In a Snellen chart, what does 20/20 vision mean?<br />\n   - A) The person can see clearly at 20 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n   - B) The person can see clearly at 20 meters what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n   - C) The person can see clearly at 20 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 10 feet<br />\n   - D) The person can see clearly at 10 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7471, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 41, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the Snellen chart used to assess?<br />\n   - A) Color blindness<br />\n   - B) Peripheral vision<br />\n   - C) Near vision<br />\n- D) Distance vision<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7472, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 42, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is visual acuity recorded if a person has 20/40 vision?<br />\n   - A) They can see at 20 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 40 feet<br />\n   - B) They can see at 40 feet what a person with normal vision can see at 20 feet<br />\n   - C) They can see at 20 meters what a person with normal vision can see at 40 meters<br />\n   - D) They can see at 40 meters what a person with normal vision can see at 20 meters<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7473, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 43, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?20/200 vision? mean on a Snellen chart?<br />\n   - A) Legal blindness<br />\n   - B) Normal vision<br />\n   - C) Impaired near vision<br />\n   - D) Impaired distance vision<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7474, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the visual acuity measurement if a person can only read the top letter (usually ?E?) on a Snellen chart?<br />\n   - A) 20/20<br />\n   - B) 20/40<br />\n   - C) 20/100<br />\n- D) 20/200<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7475, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which type of acuity chart is commonly used for near vision testing?<br />\n- A) Rosenbaum chart<br />\n   - B) Snellen chart<br />\n   - C) Tumbling E chart<br />\n   - D) Landolt C chart<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7476, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?counting fingers? visual acuity mean?<br />\n   - A) The person can count fingers held up at a distance<br />\n   - B) The person can see clearly up close<br />\n   - C) The person can see shapes but not details<br />\n   - D) The person has no perception of light<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7477, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How is visual acuity measured in children who cannot read letters?<br />\n    - A) By asking them to identify shapes<br />\n    - B) By observing their eye movements<br />\n   - C) By using picture charts or symbols<br />\n    - D) By measuring their pupil size<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7478, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does respiratory rate measure?<br />\n   - A) Heartbeats per minute<br />\n   - B) Oxygen saturation in the blood<br />\n   - C) Number of breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) Lung capacity<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7479, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range for adult respiratory rate at rest?<br />\n   - A) 12-20 breaths per minute<br />\n   - B) 30-40 breaths per minute<br />\n   - C) 60-80 breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) 100-120 breaths per minute<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7480, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which term describes abnormally slow breathing?<br />\n   - A) Bradypnea<br />\n   - B) Tachypnea<br />\n   - C) Apnea<br />\n   - D) Dyspnea<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7481, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What condition is associated with tachypnea?<br />\n   - A) Hypothermia<br />\n   - B) Hypertension<br />\n   - C) Hyperthyroidism<br />\n- D) Respiratory distress<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7482, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should respiratory rate be measured?<br />\n  - A) Counting the number of chest rises for 30 seconds and multiplying by 2<br />\n   - B) Counting the number of chest rises for 15 seconds and multiplying by 4<br />\n   - C) Counting the number of chest rises for 1 minute<br />\n   - D) Counting the number of chest rises for 2 minutes<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7483, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?apnea? refer to?<br />\n   - A) Increased breathing rate<br />\n  - B) Absence of breathing<br />\n   - C) Difficulty breathing<br />\n   - D) Irregular breathing pattern<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7484, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might cause bradypnea?<br />\n   - A) Anxiety<br />\n   - B) Heart failure<br />\n   - C) Fever<br />\n- D) Sedative medication use<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7485, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which situation would you expect to see an increased respiratory rate?<br />\n   - A) During sleep<br />\n   - B) After a large meal<br />\n   - C) During physical exercise<br />\n   - D) While resting quietly<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7486, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is Cheyne-Stokes respiration characterized by?<br />\n- A) Irregular breathing with periods of apnea<br />\n    - B) Fast and shallow breathing<br />\n    - C) Slow and irregular breathing<br />\n    - D) Fast and deep breathing<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7487, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How does respiratory rate change in infants and young children compared to adults?<br />\n    - A) It is slower<br />\n  - B) It is faster<br />\n    - C) It remains the same<br />\n    - D) It varies depending on the time of day<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7488, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of performing a urinalysis?<br />\n   - A) To measure blood pressure levels<br />\n   - B) To assess kidney function<br />\n   - C) To diagnose diabetes mellitus<br />\n   - D) To determine oxygen saturation levels<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7489, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which component of urinalysis evaluates the physical characteristics of urine such as color, clarity, and specific gravity?<br />\n   - A) Chemical analysis<br />\n   - B) Microscopic analysis<br />\n   - C) Physical examination<br />\n   - D) Gross examination<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7490, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the presence of proteinuria indicate in urinalysis?<br />\n - A) Kidney inflammation or damage<br />\n   - B) Urinary tract infection<br />\n   - C) Dehydration<br />\n   - D) Diabetes mellitus<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7491, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which chemical test is commonly used to detect glucose in urine?<br />\n   - A) Protein test (albumin)<br />\n   - B) Ketone test (acetone)<br />\n   - C) Bilirubin test<br />\n   - D) Glucose test (Benedict?s or Clinitest)<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7492, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does hematuria indicate in urinalysis?<br />\n   - A) Elevated blood sugar levels<br />\n   - B) Presence of bacteria in urine<br />\n- C) Presence of red blood cells in urine<br />\n   - D) Excessive protein levels in urine<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7493, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which microscopic finding in urinalysis suggests a urinary tract infection (UTI)?<br />\n   - A) Casts<br />\n   - B) Crystals<br />\n- C) Bacteria<br />\n   - D) Epithelial cells<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7494, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the term ?specific gravity? measure in urinalysis?<br />\n   - A) Acidity of urine<br />\n- B) Concentration of solutes in urine<br />\n   - C) Presence of glucose in urine<br />\n   - D) Number of red blood cells in urine<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7495, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal pH range of urine?<br />\n   - A) 5.0 ? 5.5<br />\n   - B) 6.0 ? 6.5<br />\n   - C) 7.0 ? 7.5<br />\n   - D) 8.0 ? 8.5<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7496, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might cause the presence of ketones in urine?<br />\n    - A) Dehydration<br />\n    - B) Excessive protein intake<br />\n- C) Diabetes mellitus<br />\n    - D) Urinary tract infection<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(7497, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the presence of bilirubin in urine indicate?<br />\n- A) Liver disease or dysfunction<br />\n    - B) Kidney stones<br />\n    - C) Urinary tract obstruction<br />\n    - D) Bacterial infection<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7498, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does respiratory rate measure?<br />\n   - A) Heartbeats per minute<br />\n   - B) Oxygen saturation in the blood<br />\n   - C) Number of breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) Lung capacity<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7499, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the normal range for adult respiratory rate at rest?<br />\n - A) 12-20 breaths per minute<br />\n   - B) 30-40 breaths per minute<br />\n   - C) 60-80 breaths per minute<br />\n   - D) 100-120 breaths per minute<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7500, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which term describes abnormally slow breathing?<br />\n   - A) Bradypnea<br />\n   - B) Tachypnea<br />\n   - C) Apnea<br />\n   - D) Dyspnea<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7501, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What condition is associated with tachypnea?<br />\n   - A) Hypothermia<br />\n   - B) Hypertension<br />\n   - C) Hyperthyroidism<br />\n- D) Respiratory distress<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7502, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">How should respiratory rate be measured?<br />\n- A) Counting the number of chest rises for 30 seconds and multiplying by 2<br />\n   - B) Counting the number of chest rises for 15 seconds and multiplying by 4<br />\n   - C) Counting the number of chest rises for 1 minute<br />\n   - D) Counting the number of chest rises for 2 minutes<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7503, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does ?apnea? refer to?<br />\n   - A) Increased breathing rate<br />\n- B) Absence of breathing<br />\n   - C) Difficulty breathing<br />\n   - D) Irregular breathing pattern<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7504, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which condition might cause bradypnea?<br />\n   - A) Anxiety<br />\n   - B) Heart failure<br />\n   - C) Fever<br />\n- D) Sedative medication use<br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7505, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In which situation would you expect to see an increased respiratory rate?<br />\n   - A) During sleep<br />\n   - B) After a large meal<br />\n   - C) During physical exercise<br />\n   - D) While resting quiet<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7506, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What technique is used to assess tactile fremitus during a physical examination of the lungs?<br />\n   - A) Percussion<br />\n- B) Palpation<br />\n   - C) Auscultation<br />\n   - D) Inspection<br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7507, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During an abdominal examination, rebound tenderness is indicative of:<br />\n- A) Appendicitis<br />\n   - B) Gastric ulcer<br />\n   - C) Cholecystitis<br />\n   - D) Diverticulitis<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7508, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which cranial nerve is primarily assessed by testing the gag reflex?<br />\n   - A) Cranial nerve V (Trigeminal)<br />\n   - B) Cranial nerve VII (Facial)<br />\n   - C) Cranial nerve IX (Glossopharyngeal)<br />\n   - D) Cranial nerve X (Vagus)<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7509, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a correct sequence for performing a comprehensive physical examination of the abdomen?<br />\n   - A) Inspection, palpation, percussion, auscultation<br />\n   - B) Palpation, auscultation, inspection, percussion<br />\n   - C) Percussion, inspection, auscultation, palpation<br />\n   - D) Auscultation, percussion, palpation, inspection<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7510, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is an important step before performing a physical examination on a community member?<br />\n   - A) Obtaining informed consent<br />\n   - B) Reviewing medical literature<br />\n   - C) Performing laboratory tests<br />\n   - D) Calling a specialist<br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7511, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During a community health screening, which vital sign is typically measured first?<br />\n   - A) Blood pressure<br />\n   - B) Respiratory rate<br />\n   - C) Temperature<br />\n   - D) Heart rate<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
(7512, '2024/2025', 'Diploma in Community Health(CHEW)(DE)', '200', 'Second', 'SUPERVISED CLINICAL EXPERIENCE', 'SEMESTER-EXAM', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the primary purpose of performing auscultation during a physical examination?<br />\n   - A) To assess skin integrity<br />\n   - B) To evaluate joint mobility<br />\n- C) To listen to internal body sounds<br />\n   - D) To measure blood pressure<br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '2024-07-19 16:55:48', '2024-07-19 16:55:48'),
