(7574, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 44, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a reason why a concrete floor feels colder to the bare feet than a mat on the same floor during the rainy season?<br />\r\nA. A mat if s better conductor of heat than the feet<br />\r\nB. Mat losses heat to the bare feet at a faster rate than concrete floor<br />\r\nC. Mat losses heat to the bare feet while the concrete floor extracts heat from them<br />\r\nD. Concrete floor is a better conductor of heat than the mat.</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7575, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 45, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following best explains a person who suffers more severe burns when his skin is exposed to steam than when boiling water is poured onto his skin?<br />\r\nA. steam is at a higher temperature than boiling water<br />\r\nB. steam posses greater heat energy per unit-mass than boiling water<br />\r\nC. steam spreads more easily over a wider area of the skin than boiling water<br />\r\nD. steam panetrates more easily over a wider area of the skin than boiling water</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7576, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 46, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The temperature at which the water vapour present in the air is just sufficient to saturate it is called the<br />\r\nA. ice point</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. boiling point</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. steam point<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. dew point</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7577, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 47, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following will affect the saturation vapour pressure of a liquid?<br />\r\nA. Temperature of the liquid<br />\r\nB. Humidity of air<br />\r\nC. Volume of vapour<br />\r\nD. Volume of the liquidhich statement BEST</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7578, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 48, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transparent rectangular block 5.0cm thick is placed on a black dot. The dot when viewed from above is seem 3.0cm from the top of the block calculate the refractive index of the material of the block.<br />\r\nA. 2/5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5/3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 3/2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 3/5</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7579, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 49, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">An object is placed 36cm from a converging lens of focal length 24cm.If a real image which is 4cm high is formed, Calculate the height of the object.<br />\r\nA. 2.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 6.0cm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.0cm</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7580, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ability of the eye to focus objects at different distances is called___________<br />\r\nA. power</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. accommodation</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. normal vision<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. persistence of vision</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7581, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The change of the direction of a wave-front because of a change in the velocity of the wave in another medium is called?<br />\r\nA. refraction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. reflection</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. diffraction<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. interference</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7582, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A boy standing a distance from the foot of a tall cliff claps his hands and hears an echo 0.5s later. If the speed of sound is 340ms1, how far is he from the cliff?<br />\r\nA. 17m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 34m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 85m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 170m</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7583, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sounding tuning fork is brought near the end of a pipe containing an air column and the loudness of the sound increases. This effect is due to_______<br />\r\nA. diffraction</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. an echo</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. resonance<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. interference</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7584, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A transformer with 5500 turns in its primary is used between a 240V a. c supply and a 120V kettle. Calculate the number of turns in the secondary<br />\r\nA. 11000</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2750</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 460</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 232</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(7585, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">It takes 4 minutes to boil a quantity of water electrically. How long will it take to boil same quantity of water using the same heating coil but with the current doubled? (neglecting any external heat loss).<br />\r\nA. 1 minute</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 32 minutes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8 minutes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. 2 minutes</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7586, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following particles of ray has the highest penetrating power?<br />\r\nA. Beta particles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Gamma particles</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Electrons</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Neutrons</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7587, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is/are not correct about isotopes of an element? They have_______<br />\r\nA. the same neutron number<br />\r\nB. the same proton number<br />\r\nC. same number of electrons<br />\r\nD. same chemical properties</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7588, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not an electromagnetic radiation?<br />\r\nA. X-ray</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Radio waves</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Sunlight<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Sound waves</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7589, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">During the same interval, it is observed that a train travels the same distance as does a lorry. The two vehicles therefore have the same<br />\r\nA. uniform accelation<br />\r\nB. instateneous velocity<br />\r\nC. initial velocity<br />\r\nD. average speed</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7590, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is a derived unit?<br />\r\nA. Metre</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Coulomb</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Kilogram</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Second</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7591, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ability of organisms to maintain a constant internal environment is known as<br />\r\nA. homeostasis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. endosmosis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. plasmolysis<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. dialysis</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7592, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Double fertilization is said to occur in flowering pants because?<br />\r\nA. two embryos are formed<br />\r\nB. one egg is fertilized twice<br />\r\nC. two sperms and two pollen grains are involved<br />\r\nD. one embryo and endosperm nucleus are formed</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7593, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pulmonary artery carries___________</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A. deoxygenated blood from the right ventricles to the lungs<br />\r\nB. oxygenated blood from the right ventricle to the lungs<br />\r\nC. oxygenated blood from the left ventricles to the ventricles to the right auricle<br />\r\nD. deoxygenated blood from the left ventricles to the right auricles</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7594, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following blood components has the greatest affinity for oxygen and carbondioxide?<br />\r\nA. Blood plasma</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Leucocytes<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Thrombocytes</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Erythrocyte</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7595, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The thoracic cavity is separated from the abdominal cavity by a sheet of muscle called<br />\r\nA. pleural membrane<br />\r\nB. intercostal muscles<br />\r\nC. diaphragm<br />\r\nD. pericardium</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7596, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements on urine production is not correct?<br />\r\nA. in the presence of antidiuretic hormone dilute urine is produced<br />\r\nB. The total volume of urine produced depends on the need for water excretion<br />\r\nC. if there is excess intake of water, dilute urine is expected<br />\r\nD. if there is a shortage of water in the body the volume of the urine produced is decreased</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7597, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pigment in the malphigian layer responsible for skin colouration is known as<br />\r\nA. haemoglobin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. haemocyanin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. melanin<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. haemoerythrin</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7598, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following statements is correct of hormones? Hormones are<br />\r\nA. secreted into the blood through ducts<br />\r\nB. secreted directly into the blood streem<br />\r\nC. inactive chemical substance in the blood stream<br />\r\nD. non-specific in their mode of action</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7599, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pituitary is called &#39;master gland&#39; because<br />\r\nA. it is locatd in the brain<br />\r\nB. its secretion are the more numerous than those of the other gland<br />\r\nC. its secretion controls the other glands<br />\r\nD. it is the only organ that produces hormone</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7600, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The brain and the spinal cord make up the<br />\r\nA. pheripheral nervous system<br />\r\nB. automatic nervous system<br />\r\nC. central nervous system<br />\r\nD. somatic nervous system</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7601, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following specialized structures are stimulated by touch, pressure, pain, heat and cold?<br />\r\nA. Receptors</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Synapse</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cell bodies<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Myelin sheath</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7602, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not correct about a fruit? lt<br />\r\nA. may contain many seeds<br />\r\nB. is a mature ovary<br />\r\nC. is covered by the pericarp<br />\r\nD. may develop from the receptacle</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7603, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which structure in the maize grain stores food?<br />\r\nA. Endosperm.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Embryo</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Cytoplasm</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. Seed coat</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7604, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Even though some flowering plants contain accessory pigments which give them colours they still contain<br />\r\nthe pigment<br />\r\nA. melanin</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. chlorophyll</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. xanthrophyll<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. carotene</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7605, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The relationship between a herbivore and the bacteria which live in its caecum is known as<br />\r\nA. parasitism</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. symbiosis</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. predation<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. saprophytism</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7606, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Autotropic nutrition may be defined in terms of food obtained<br />\r\nA. from other organisms in exchange for some products.<br />\r\nB. by the breakdown of complex substances<br />\r\nC. by an organism utilizing its own store of energy<br />\r\nD. by synthesizing simple substances using energy from an external source</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7607, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following does not contribute to the biomass in an ecosystem?<br />\r\nA. Producers</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Food chains</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Consumers<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Micro-organisms</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7608, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a characteristic feature of tropical rain-forest habitat?<br />\r\nA. Trees with longer boles than those in Savannah<br />\r\nB. Fewer canopy strata than the savannah<br />\r\nC. Many more trees and climbers than savannah<br />\r\nD. Plenty of leaf litter on the ground</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7609, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following factors is not associated with aquatic habitat?<br />\r\nA. Temperature</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Light intensity</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. Humidity<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. Turbidity</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7610, '2024/2025', 'ND in Environmental Health Technology', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The causative organism of sleeping sickness is the?<br />\r\nA. Trypanosome</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. Plasmodium<br />\r\n<br />\r\nC. Vibrio bacterium</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. tsetse fly</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
