(7827, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The girl has just come out of the fattening room and her waist is <strong><ins>adorned</ins></strong> with beads.<br />\r\nA. surrounded &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. decorated &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. besieged<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. defaced</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7828, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Ade is very winsome yet his neighbour finds it difficult to <strong><ins>put up</ins></strong> with him.<br />\r\nA. live with &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. tolerate &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. depend on &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. rely on</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7829, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">There are some drugs that could <strong><ins>exacerbate</ins></strong> a particular illness<br />\r\nA. heal &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. ameliorate &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. lengthen &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. worsen</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7830, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">From the words lettered A to E below each of the following sentences, choose the word or group of words that is nearest in meaning to the underlined expression as it is used in the sentence.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">In accordance with the practice of his religion, Raman&#39;s body was <strong><ins>interred</ins></strong> the day he died<br />\r\nA. sanctified &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. preserved &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. cremated<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. buried</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7831, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Abidjan is 4 degree west of Accra and on the same circle of latitude. If the radius of this circle of latitude is 6370km, how far is Abidjan west of Accra, correct to the nearest kilometer? [Take &pi; = 22/7]<br />\r\nA. 222km &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 445km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 890km &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5005km</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7832, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 2, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If Q = (all perfect squares less than 30) and P = (all odd numbers from 1 to 10). Find Q &cap; P.<br />\r\nA. (1, 4, 9, 16, 25) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. (1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 9, 16, 25)</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. (1, 3, 5, 7, 9) &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. (1, 9)</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7833, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 3, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If K28&minus;&minus;&radic;+63&minus;&minus;&radic;&minus;7&ndash;&radic;=0, find K.<br />\r\nA. -2 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. -1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 1 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7834, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 4, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A group of 11 people can speak either English or French or Both. Seven can speak English and six can speak French. What is the probability that a person chosen at random can speak both English and French?<br />\r\nA. 2/11 &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 4/11 &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 5/11 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. &nbsp;11/13</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7835, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 5, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The interior angle of a regular polygon is twice the exterior angle. How many sides has the polygon?<br />\r\nA. 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 6</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7836, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 6, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following figures have one line of symmetry only? I. Isosceles triangle II. Rhombus III. Kite<br />\r\nA. I and II only<br />\r\nB. II and III only<br />\r\nC. I and III only<br />\r\nD. I, II, and III</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7837, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 7, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Find the 8th term of the A.P -3, -1, 1 ____<br />\r\nA. 13</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 11</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. -8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. -11</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7838, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 8, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0 1 2 3 4 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">FREQUENCY&nbsp; 2 3 4 2 7 2<br />\r\nA group of students took a test and the following frequency table shows the scores above. Find the mode<br />\r\nA. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 3</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 4</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 5</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7839, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 9, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">SCORE&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0 1 2 3 4 5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">FREQUENCY&nbsp; 2 3 4 2 7 2<br />\r\nA group of students took a test and the following frequency table shows the scores above. The mean score is__________<br />\r\nA. 1.75</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 2.5</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.75</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7840, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 10, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A ladder 9m long leans against a vertical wall, making an angle of 64? with the horizontal ground. calculate correct to one decimal place, how far the foot of the ladder is from the wall.<br />\r\nA. 4.0m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 5.8m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7.1m</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 8.1m</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7841, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 11, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The number 186,470 was corrected to 186,000. Which of the following describe the degree of approximation made?<br />\r\nI. to the nearest hundred</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">II. to the nearest thousand</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">III. to 3 significant figures</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">IV. to 4 significant figures</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"><br />\r\nA. I &amp; III only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. I &amp; IV only</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. II &amp; III only<br />\r\n<br />\r\nD. II &amp; IV only</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7842, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 12, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Points P and Q respectively 24m north and 7m east point R. Calculate |PQ| in meters<br />\r\nA. 20</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 24</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 25</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 31</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7843, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 13, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A sales girl gave a change of N1.15 to a customer instead of N1.25. Calculate her percentage error<br />\r\nA. 10%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8.0%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 2.4%</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7844, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 14, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Instead of recording the number 1.23cm of the radius of a tube, a student recorded 1.32cm. Find the percentage of error, correct to one decimal place.<br />\r\nA. 6.8%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7.3%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 9.6%</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 14.4%</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7845, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 15, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">If twice a certain integer is subtracted from 5 times the integer, the result is 63. Find the integer.<br />\r\nA. 21</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 9</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 4</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL),
(7846, '2024/2025', 'ND Dental Therapy', 'NDI', 'First', 'ENTRANCE', 'ENTRANCE', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 16, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For a class of 30 students, the scores in a Mathematics test out of 10 marks were as follows;<br />\r\n4,5,7,2,3,6,5,5,8,9,5,4,2,3,7,9,8,7,7,7,3,4,5,5,2,3,6,7,7,2.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the median score?<br />\r\nA. 2</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">B. 7</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">C. 8</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">D. 9</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', NULL, NULL);
