(7980, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 50, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Cell membrane is a portion of the cell that encloses the _____________ <br />\n(a)mitochondria <br />\n(b)protoplasm <br />\n(c)endoplasmic reticulum <br />\n(d)nucleus <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7981, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 51, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Gametes are formed by_______________<br />\n(a)meiosis <br />\n(b)mitosis <br />\n(c)zygote <br />\n(d)genetic materials <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7982, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 52, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The external genitalia are  known as ___________<br />\n(a)vulva <br />\n(b) labia major <br />\n(c) labia monora <br />\n(d)clitoris <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7983, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 53, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The spermatogenesis cords suspend the testis in the __________ <br />\n(a)scrotum  <br />\n(b)efferent duct <br />\n(c)tunicalvaginalis <br />\n(d) epididymis <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7984, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 54, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Prostate gland lies in the ________________<br />\n(a)pelvic cavity <br />\n(b)cranial cavity <br />\n(c)thoracic cavity <br />\n(d)abdominal cavity <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7985, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 55, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The male urethra provides a common pathway for the flow of _____________ <br />\n(a)urine and fluid <br />\n(b)water and lymph <br />\n(c)urine and semen <br />\n(d)semen only <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7986, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 56, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The ear is divided into ______________ distinct parts <br />\n(a)3 <br />\n(b)2 <br />\n(c)6 <br />\n(d)14 <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7987, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 57, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">______________ are three small bones that extend across the middle ear from the tympanic membrane <br />\n(a)auditoryossicles <br />\n(b)maples <br />\n(c)incurs <br />\n(d)stapes <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7988, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 58, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The oval window is concluded by part of small bone called _______________<br />\n(a)incurs <br />\n(b)maples <br />\n(c)stapes <br />\n(d)ossicles <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7989, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 59, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Hypothalamus is classified as a part of the _______________<br />\n(a)gland <br />\n(b)brain <br />\n(c)pituitary <br />\n(d)hormone <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7990, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 60, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The pituitary gland and hypothalamus act as a ________________<br />\n(a)unit <br />\n(b)force <br />\n(c)muscle <br />\n(d)neuron <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7991, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 61, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The posterior pituitary is formed from _______________<br />\n(a)neuron <br />\n(b)nervous tissue <br />\n(c)aveolar tissue <br />\n(d)muscle tissue <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7992, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 62, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> _______________ is the most abundant hormone synthesize by the anterior pituitary <br />\n(a)TSH <br />\n(b)GH <br />\n(c)ACTH <br />\n(d) Prolactin <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7993, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 63, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The medulla  is completely  surrounded  by the ___________<br />\n(a)adrenal  cortex  <br />\n(b)medulla  <br />\n(c) langerhans <br />\n(d)glucagon <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7994, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 64, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The nervous system detect  and response to change in __________<br />\n(a) outside the body only <br />\n(b)inside the body <br />\n(c)outside and inside the body <br />\n(d)inside the autonomic  systems <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7995, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 65, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The physiological units of the nervous system are called <br />\n(a)nervous  impulse/nerve  cell/ neuron  <br />\n(b)action <br />\n(c)potential <br />\n(d)charges  <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7996, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 66, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">_________is the ability to initiate  nerves  impulse in response to stimuli<br />\n(a)irritability  <br />\n(b)conductivity <br />\n(c)impulse  <br />\n(d)basal ganglia <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7997, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 67, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">____________ is the largest part of the brain and it occupiesthe anterior and middle cranial fossae (a)cerebrum <br />\n(b)pons <br />\n(c)cerebellum <br />\n(d)the brain stem <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7998, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 68, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">For descriptive purposes each hemisphere of the cerebrum is divided into ________________<br />\n(a)lobes <br />\n(b)tubules <br />\n(c)fossae <br />\n(d)cavities <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(7999, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 69, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The surface of cerebral cortex is divided into __________ <br />\n(a)grey matter <br />\n(b)cells <br />\n(c)sulcus <br />\n(d)lobes <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8000, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 70, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Blood has the following functions except ____________<br />\n(a)Temperature  regulation  <br />\n(b)Transport oxygen  <br />\n(c)Immunological  functions  <br />\n(d)photo regulation <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8001, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 71, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Peristalsis is ______ <br />\n(a)movement  of food by series  of contraction of smooth muscle in GIT <br />\n(b)A type of movement seen  in amoeba <br />\n(c) process of movement  of material across  plasma membrane  <br />\n(d)movement  of lymph  towards  the lymph nodes <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8002, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 72, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which  of the following  bones is not part of bony pelvis? <br />\n(a)pubis <br />\n(b) femur <br />\n(c) Ischium  <br />\n(d) Ulna <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8003, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 73, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the name given to the collection  of cell bodies (in PNS) enclosed in a connective tissue? (a)Nucleus  <br />\n(b)synapse <br />\n(c) Ganglion <br />\n(d) Oligodendrocyte <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8004, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 74, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of these statements is incorrect?<br />\n(a)oxygen is transported in form of Hemoglobin <br />\n(b)Hemoglobin has the capacity to transport a little carbon (iv)oxide <br />\n(c)carbon (iv)oxide is mostly transported in dissolved form as bicarbonates(HCO3) <br />\n(d)carbon (iv)oxide is transport through breathing out <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8005, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 75, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which neuron transmit impulses to effect or organs?<br />\n(a)Association <br />\n(b)sensory <br />\n(c)motor <br />\n(d)somatic <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8006, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 76, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\"> _______ is the thick middle layer of the heart? <br />\n(a) parietal pericardium <br />\n(b) myocardium <br />\n(c) endocardium <br />\n(d) epicardium <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8007, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 77, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Semilunar valve is found within the _____ <br />\n(a) vessels and capilaries <br />\n(b) aorta and pulmonary trunk <br />\n(c) aorta and vein <br />\n(d) semi lunar and aorta <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8008, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 78, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Systemic circulation is called _____ <br />\n(a) lesser circulation <br />\n(b) circulatory circulation <br />\n(c) greater circulation <br />\n(d) cytology <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8009, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 79, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The heart is located in one of the following <br />\n(a) middle mediastinum <br />\n(b) entire thoracic cavity <br />\n(c) abdominal cavity <br />\n(d) pelvic cavity <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8010, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 80, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is not a layer of the heart? <br />\n(a) myocardium <br />\n(b) epicardium <br />\n(c) atriocardium <br />\n(d) endocardium <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8011, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 81, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All arteries carry oxygenated blood except ______ <br />\n(a) pulmonary vein <br />\n(b) pulmonary artery <br />\n(c) pulmonary trunk <br />\n(d) atrioventricular artery <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8012, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 82, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">All veins carry deoxygenated blood except _____ <br />\n(a) pulmonary artery <br />\n(b) hepatic vein <br />\n(c) pulmonary vein <br />\n(d) gastric vein <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8013, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 83, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">______ is called lesser circulation <br />\n(a) pulmonary circulation <br />\n(b) systemic circulation <br />\n(c) hepatic circulation <br />\n(d) portal circulation <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8014, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 84, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Serous pericardium allows free movement of blood within the______ <br />\n(a) myocardium <br />\n(b) pericardiumm sac <br />\n(c) heart <br />\n(d) endocardium <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8015, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 85, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The space between parietal and visceral pericardium is called _____ <br />\n(a) endocardium <br />\n(b) pericardium cavity <br />\n(c) parietal pericardium <br />\n(d) potential space <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8016, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 86, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following bones is called collar bone <br />\n(a) acetabulum <br />\n(b) pelvic <br />\n(c) scapula <br />\n(d) clavicle <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8017, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 87, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Amount of CO2 in expired air is _____ <br />\n(a) 0.04% <br />\n(b) 0.03% <br />\n(c) 3.6% <br />\n(d) 21% <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00');
INSERT INTO `questions` (`id`, `session1`, `department`, `level`, `semester`, `course`, `exam_type`, `exam_mode`, `exam_category`, `no_of_qst`, `upload_no_of_qst`, `question_type`, `question_no`, `question`, `answer`, `graphic`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(8018, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 88, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which of the following is correct? <br />\n(a) lymph = plasma + WBC + RBC <br />\n(b) plasma = blood - lymphocytes <br />\n(c) neuron = citron + dentron + axon + synapse <br />\n(d) blood = plasma + RBC <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8019, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 89, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The normal blood pressure of an adult is _____ <br />\n(a) 100/80mmHg <br />\n(b) 100/60mmHg <br />\n(c) 120/80mmHg <br />\n(d) 80/120mmHg <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8020, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 90, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which taste bud is present on the lateral sides of the tongue <br />\n(a) salty <br />\n(b) sweet <br />\n(c) bitter <br />\n(d) sour <br />\n</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8021, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 91, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Nerve tissue has the characteristics of <br />\n(a)irritability <br />\n(b)growth <br />\n(c)sensation <br />\n(d)sensory <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8022, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 92, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are the structures forming the brain except <br />\n(a)fore brain <br />\n(b)the midbrain <br />\n(c)the brain stem <br />\n(d)ventricles <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8023, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 93, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Sensory nerves are arranged in groups called <br />\n(a)tracts <br />\n(b)ventricles <br />\n(c)dura mater <br />\n(d)nerve <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8024, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A strong  band of inelastic fibrous tissue which connects bone,more especially at the joint is called <br />\n(a)ligaments <br />\n(b)gland <br />\n(c)muscle <br />\n(d)nervous <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8025, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The study of hormones and how they control body function is called <br />\n(a)histology <br />\n(b)physiology <br />\n(c)embryology <br />\n(d)endocrinology <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8026, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following are fundamental tissues in the body except <br />\n(a)Epithelial tissue <br />\n(b)muscle tissue <br />\n(c)cartilage <br />\n(d)nervous tissue <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8027, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the functions of the lymphatic system is<br />\n(a)it prevents backflow of blood <br />\n(b)production of hormone <br />\n(c)it confers immunity <br />\n(d)it aids digestion <br />\n</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8028, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The following except one are factors affecting heart rate:<br />\n(a)posture <br />\n(b)age <br />\n(c)Emotional status <br />\n(d)complexion <br />\n</p>', 'D', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8029, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The thrombocytes function primarily in:<br />\n(a)Homeostasis <br />\n(b)Erythropoiesis <br />\n(c)thrombopoiesis <br />\n(d)Homostasis <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8030, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'ANATOMY', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">One of the following is an anticoagulant <br />\n(a)fibrinogen <br />\n(b)globulin <br />\n(c)lysine <br />\n(d)heparin <br />\n</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8031, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 1, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The probability assigned to an event based on experience, information and believe is known as<br />\nA. Objective approach. B. Subjective approach<br />\nC. Relative approach D. Frequency approach</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
