(8061, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 31, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The tabular arrangement of class intervals with associated frequencies  called<br />\nA . Frequency polygon. B. Frequency distribution.<br />\nC. Frequency curve D. Frequency ogive</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8062, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 32, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The type of data used by other person other than the person who   collects the data for other statistical enquiry is called<br />\nA. Secondary data. B. Primary data C. tertiary data D. frequency data</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8063, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 33, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A small scale replica of the actual survey and is carried out before the actual survey is undertaken is called<br />\nA. Pilot survey B. Simple survey C. Pre-test survey D. Post survey</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8064, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 34, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">A statistical enquiry based on a sample and from which inference is made about the population is called<br />\nA. Population survey. B. Population census.<br />\nC. Sample survey        D. Sample statistics</p>', 'C', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
