(8124, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 94, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the Infant Mortality Rate (IMR) measure? A) Deaths of infants under 1 year per 1000 live births<br />\nB) Deaths of infants aged 1-5 per 1000 live births<br />\nC) Deaths of children under 5 years per 1000 live births<br />\nD) Deaths of newborns in the first month per 1000 live births</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8125, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 95, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The General Fertility Rate (GFR) is the number of live births per 1000 women aged 15-49 years in a year.<br />\nA.   True<br />\nB.   False</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8126, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 96, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the Crude Birth Rate (CBR) measure?<br />\nA) Number of births per 1000 women aged 15-49 years<br />\nB) Number of births per 1000 population<br />\nC) Number of births per 1000 live births<br />\nD) Number of births per 1000 households</p>', 'B', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8127, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 97, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">Which demographic measure refers to the average number of years a person is expected to live?<br />\nA) Life Expectancy<br />\nB) Median Age<br />\nC) Mortality Rate<br />\nD) Crude Death Rate</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8128, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 98, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What does the term \"Neonatal Mortality Rate\" (NMR) refer to?<br />\nA) Deaths of infants under 28 days per 1000 live births<br />\nB) Deaths of infants under 1 year per 1000 live births C) Deaths of children under 5 years per 1000 live births<br />\nD) Deaths of infants under 7 days per 1000 live births</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8129, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 99, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">The Maternal Mortality Ratio (MMR) measures the number of maternal deaths per 100,000 live births.<br />\nA.   True<br />\nB.   False</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
(8130, '2024/2025', 'ND Health Information Management', 'NDII', 'First', 'BIOSTATISTICS', 'PREPARATORY', 'OBJECTIVE', 'GENERAL', 100, 100, 'text', 100, '<p style=\"font-size: 24px; font-family: Arial;\">What is the Dependency Ratio used to measure?<br />\nA) The ratio of the dependent population (ages 0-14 and 65+) to the working-age population (ages 15-64)<br />\nB) The ratio of elderly population to children<br />\nC) Women of child bearing age<br />\nD) Fertility rate.</p>', 'A', 'blank.jpg', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', '0000-00-00 00:00:00'),
